{"parentUuid":"d2c48192-03aa-48b8-96a5-6c534aeb7a02","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VfDNJ8zEDL2nxAVPUZLnsy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Adobe Substance 3D Painter helpx generators Dirt Edge Wear Mask Editor documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"helpx.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/wear-and-finish/paint.html\"},{\"title\":\"3D Painting: A Texturing Workshop Using Substance Painter — Part 2 - L6710b\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/de/max/2020/sessions/3d-painting-a-texturing-workshop-using-substance-p-l6710b.html\"},{\"title\":\"masking and effects\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/interface/layer-stack/masking-and-effects.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mask Builder\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/mask-builder\"},{\"title\":\"experienceleague.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/generator\"},{\"title\":\"Fiber Glass Edge Wear\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/fiber-glass-edge-wear\"},{\"title\":\"experienceleague.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/dirt\"},{\"title\":\"helpx.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/wear-and-finish/dirt.html\"},{\"title\":\"Last updated on\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/mesh-based-generators/mask-generators/metal-edge-wear.html\"},{\"title\":\"Last updated on\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/mesh-based-generators/mask-generators/fiber-glass-edge-wear.html\"}]\n\nI couldn't find a dedicated Painter \"Edge Wear\" generator page or a standalone Mask Editor page in these results. The closest material is below.\n\n**Docs location:** Adobe has been moving Substance documentation to Experience League, and after March 14th, HelpX pages will automatically redirect to the equivalent Experience League page.\n\n**Generators and masks:** Painter generators create a mask or textures based on the mesh topology using baked utility maps like Position, Curvature, and World Space Normal. To attach one to a mask, right-click the mask in the Layers panel and select Add generator.\n\n**Dirt generator:** It adds buildup of dirt and grunge in crevices, edges, and flat surfaces based on curvature, ambient occlusion. It outputs a monochrome (black and white) texture. Adobe recommends using additional masks to control how the dirt is applied.\n\n**Edge wear:** The Painter-specific page I found is for the Fiber Glass Edge Wear generator, which adds fiber glass edge wear and fraying details based on baked Curvature and Ambient Occlusion maps. Its Designer counterpart, Metal Edge Wear, is similar to Smart Masks in Painter. Its description says it represents edge wear on a metal object, with scratches and chips appearing on Convex raised edges.\n\n**Mask Editor:** The Mask Builder page describes a legacy version of the Mask Editor generator. It allows you to combine Grunge, AO, Curvature, Gradient, World Space Normal, Scratches, Scatter, and Micro Details in a single mask. The results also say that due to its complexity, it can impact performance more than most generators.\n\n**Tutorial:** An Adobe MAX lab covers related workflows, including how to add edge damage and wear using mask generators and how to use the mask editor to create a custom mask generator.\n\nFor the current Mask Editor and Edge Wear pages, search Experience League directly for \"