rror":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23e660fa-5024-440d-8102-09bbf7e5cfb6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f610b8c8-02b5-4c4d-a9f7-bd3394d0e982","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wgY7FX6AK7xc2SWfFSA2h","type":"tool_result","content":"The Substance Bakers are a set of advanced algorithms that compute mesh-based information into texture files. Any artist with a 3D mesh can use them to apply advanced texturing methods. Baking is central to the Substance workflow, supporting \"powerful tools\" and \"automated texturing.\" The documentation covers baking fundamentals and common issues.\n\nThe overview doesn't describe each baker, so the purposes below are inferred from their titles. Links point to the Bakers Settings section on helpx.adobe.com.\n\n| Baker | Inferred purpose | Link |\n|---|---|---|\n| Common Parameters | Settings shared across bakers (not a map itself) | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/common-parameters) |\n| Ambient Occlusion | Captures shading from how exposed each surface area is | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/ambient-occlusion) |\n| Ambient Occlusion from Mesh | Generates ambient occlusion from mesh geometry | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/ambient-occlusion-from-mesh) |\n| Bent Normals from Mesh | Stores the average unoccluded direction for lighting | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/bent-normals-from-mesh) |\n| Color Map from Mesh | Transfers color information from a mesh into a texture | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/color-map-from-mesh) |\n| Convert UV to SVG | Converts a UV layout into SVG format (not a mesh map) | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/convert-uv-to-svg) |\n| Curvature | Highlights convex and concave edges on a surface | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/curvature) |\n| Curvature from Mesh | Derives curvature from mesh geometry | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/curvature-from-mesh) |\n| Curvature from Mesh (deprecated) | Older curvature method, no longer recommended | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/curvature-from-mesh-deprecated) |\n| Height Map from Mesh | Stores surface height detail | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/height-map-from-mesh) |\n| Normal Map from Mesh | Stores surface detail as normal directions | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/normal-map-from-mesh) |\n| Opacity Mask from Mesh | Creates a transparency mask | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/opacity-mask-from-mesh) |\n| Position | Stores position data in a texture | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/position) |\n| Position Map from Mesh | Generates a position map from mesh geometry | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/position-map-from-mesh) |\n| Thickness Map from Mesh | Estimates the thickness of a mesh | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/thickness-map-from-mesh) |\n| Transferred Texture from Mesh | Transfers existing texture detail between meshes | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/transferred-texture-from-mesh) |\n| World Space Direction | Stores direction vectors in world space | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/world-space-direction) |\n| World Space Normals | Stores normals in world space instead of tangent space | [Link](https://helpx.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/world-space-normals) |"}]},"uuid":"b11b2a3a-63c2-4c02-a8ce-ee0a7c7af028","timest