{"parentUuid":"47d8bfcf-836e-4279-9a2d-13b6d7569857","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BXcr86iuj1pcUKVsQd9NW","type":"tool_result","content":"The World Space Normals baker saves mesh normal, tangent, and binormal data into a texture.\n\nIts main parameters are:\n- **Baking Type**: Chooses what to compute: Normal (the default), Tangent, or Binormal.\n- **Normal Map**: An optional input normal texture used to add surface detail.\n- **Normal Orientation**: Sets the input texture's format, either OpenGL or DirectX (the default). It applies only when Baking Type is Normal.\n\nThe page doesn't describe tangent space normals, so it doesn't explain how this baker differs from them."}]},"uuid":"1ed84f6e-d82a-4344-a864-4d9a5bcc3668","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:21:59.898Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"12bf08ff-3a89-4ed9-b9b4-16414819e5a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"47d8bfcf-836e-4279-9a2d-13b6d7569857","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"1ed5cc6b-962e-4ffb-aa18-cca92912a6c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019wtNKk6A2oWXzhjywTBRH4","type":"tool_result","content":"The Height Map from Mesh baker produces a height map from a high-poly mesh by measuring surface differences relative to a low-poly mesh. It's available in Painter, Designer, and Automation Toolkit.\n\n**Key parameters:**\n\n- **Normalization** controls how the measured height values are scaled into the output texture. It has four options:\n  - *Relative to ray distance*: scales based on the distance traced between the surfaces.\n  - *Relative to low poly mesh (per UV tile)*: the default. Scales relative to the low-poly mesh within each UV tile.\n  - *Relative to Min/Max (per UV tile)*: scales between the minimum and maximum heights found in each UV tile.\n  - *Manual*: you set the scale yourself.\n- **Scaling divisor** multiplies or divides the height values. It only appears when Normalization is set to Manual.\n\nThe page doesn't give numeric ranges, the exact measurement method beyond the ray-distance option, or detailed usage steps."}]},"uuid":"ddfb567f-ca32-44aa-ac91-e0e9660f5366","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:00.191Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"12bf08ff-3a89-4ed9-b9b4-16414819e5a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1ed5cc6b-962e-4ffb-aa18-cca92912a6c5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"45c38823-5755-4858-83f7-14e362b9f07b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XVPzBJ7EKPcMRbChLDYgxp","type":"tool_result","content":"The Normal Map from Mesh baker generates a normal map from a high-poly mesh, and you can choose between tangent-space and world-space output. It works in Substance Painter, Substance Designer, and the Substance Automation Toolkit.\n\nIts two main parameters are:\n\n- **Map Type:** Chooses between world-space and tangent-space output. Tangent space is the default. Substance Painter always uses tangent space and doesn't expose this setting.\n- **Normal Orientation:** Applies only to tangent-space output and sets the convention, either OpenGL or DirectX. DirectX is the default. In Substance Painter, this follows the project settings.\n\nThe page doesn't cover antialiasing or other details of how tangent space is computed, so I can't speak to those from this source. Based on the general purpose of the baker, it's typically used to transfer surface detail from a detailed sculpt or high-poly model onto a lower-poly asset so it appears detailed in real time."}]},"uuid":"c1d604a6-1d6c-441a-983b-fcc97135434b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:00.522Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"12bf08ff-3a89-4ed9-b9b4-16414819e5a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"45c38823-5755-4858-83f7-14e362b9f07b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dc80585d-dd38-492c-a53c-d26489e5b0db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011D5bcBufeVzTVPTmPECJoc","type":"tool_result","content":"The Color Map from Mesh baker transfers color information from a high-poly mesh into a texture. You can use it to bake polypaint or material assignments, and the resulting ID-style maps are useful for building selection masks. It's available in Substance Designer, Substance Automation Toolkit, and Substance Painter.\n\n**Key parameters:**\n\n- **Color Source** sets which high-poly property supplies the color:\n  - *Vertex Color* captures painted vertex colors and blends them smoothly between vertices.\n  - *Material Color* uses the material assigned to each polygon face.\n  - *Mesh ID* gives each separate object its own color.\n  - *Polygroup / Submesh ID* gives each sub-object (element) its own color.\n- **Color Generator** determines how those per-object or per-element colors are chosen. It only applies when Color Source is Mesh ID or Polygroup/Submesh ID:\n  - *Random* assigns randomly generated colors.\n  - *Hue Shift* assigns each item a distinct hue.\n  - *Grayscale* assigns each item a distinct gray value.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values for these parameters, so check the baker in your application to confirm them."}]},"uuid":"509ca3ad-fc19-460e-b909-540c008b6729","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:00.522Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"12bf08ff-3a89-4ed9-b9b4-16414819e5a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc80585d-dd38-492c-a53c-d26489e5b0db","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entryp