{"parentUuid":"0324891f-9f81-496b-9c78-effcb8ca63a2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FhENH7DaYCua75byFcykdK","type":"tool_result","content":"Baking mode provides the tools and parameters for producing high-quality mesh map bakes. You can enter it with the baked-croissant button at the top right of the Viewport, the F8 shortcut, or Mode > Bake Mesh Maps.\n\nThe screen splits into the Viewport and a panel area. The Viewport works as it does in Painting mode, with the same navigation and channel dropdown. Baking mode adds a visualization settings panel in the top left and buttons at the bottom to start a bake or return to Painting mode.\n\nFour panels are unique to Baking mode:\n\n- **Mesh map bakers** let you choose which mesh maps to bake. The provided text doesn't list the individual bakers.\n- **Common settings** hold options that apply to all mesh maps. The text doesn't describe them individually.\n- **Mesh map settings** adjust options for the selected map.\n- **Baking log** shows bake results and helps diagnose problems.\n\nThe page refers to a separate Mesh map settings reference for the full option list. The settings you asked about, such as output size, dilation, antialiasing, high-definition meshes, cage, frontal/rear distance, and match by name, aren't explained in the content provided, so I can't describe them from this source. The Texture Set list, Log, Display settings, and History panels also work as they do in Painting mode."}]},"uuid":"23fec2b2-057e-43d9-a8fb-6b329690add0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:13.974Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"61bbc65e-2c9e-459c-ba4b-9b18113378e5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0324891f-9f81-496b-9c78-effcb8ca63a2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8f130e80-26f4-4505-a0c5-1735449a1e38","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoN7WjMJt3UrsEVNkKAJBY","type":"tool_result","content":"The page covers settings for seven mesh map bakers. It doesn't describe Normal, World Space Normal, or Opacity, so I can't summarize those from this content.\n\n**Common high-poly settings (shared by all bakers)**\n- **Purpose:** Control how the high-poly data is transferred to the low-poly mesh.\n- **High-poly requirement:** You can bake from the project mesh itself or import separate high-poly meshes. The cage can be distance-based, automatic (experimental), or a custom file with matching vertex counts.\n- **Key settings:** Output size, dilation width, antialiasing, the Match option (always, or by mesh name with suffixes), and ignore backface.\n\n**ID**\n- **Purpose:** Assigns a distinct color to each part of the mesh.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Not stated on this page.\n- **Key settings:** Color source (vertex color, material color, file ID, or mesh ID/polygroup) and color generator (random, hue shift, or grayscale).\n\n**Ambient Occlusion**\n- **Purpose:** Shows how much each surface is shaded by nearby geometry, using rays cast to the high-poly mesh.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Implied, since the rays are described as hitting high-poly geometry.\n- **Key settings:** Secondary rays, minimum and maximum occluder distance, spread angle, distribution, ignore backface, self occlusion, attenuation, and an optional ground plane with offset.\n\n**Curvature**\n- **Purpose:** Measures how convex or concave the surface is at each point.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Not stated.\n- **Key settings:** Method, secondary rays, sampling radius, relative-to-bounding-box option, self intersection, and tonemapping (automatic per UV tile, or manual min/max).\n\n**Position**\n- **Purpose:** Encodes each point's location in space.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Not stated.\n- **Key settings:** Mode (all axes or a single axis), axis choice, normalization type (bounding box, bounding sphere, or none), and normalization scale.\n\n**Thickness**\n- **Purpose:** Estimates how thick the mesh is at each point, using rays cast to the high-poly mesh.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Implied by the ray-based method.\n- **Key settings:** Secondary rays, occluder distances, relative-to-bounding-box option, spread angle, distribution, self occlusion, and normalization.\n\n**Height**\n- **Purpose:** Records surface height values.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Not stated.\n- **Key settings:** Normalization, plus a scaling divisor when normalization is set to manual.\n\n**Bent Normals**\n- **Purpose:** Stores an averaged direction of unoccluded light for each point, using rays cast to the high-poly mesh.\n- **High-poly requirement:** Implied by the ray-based method.\n- **Key settings:** Secondary rays, occluder distances, relative-to-bounding-box option, spread angle, distribution, ignore backface, and self occlusion."}]},"uuid":"25b078bc-f400-40fd-9ba3-1fcb40ae558f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:16.877Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"61bbc65e-2c9e-459c-ba4b-9b18113378e5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f130e80-26f4-4505-a0c5-1735449a1e38","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
