{"parentUuid":"6453dc26-8440-45bb-8135-285405498ab9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TueFhuwnSsPKJZRj6JwBoU","type":"tool_result","content":"The Dirt generator creates a black-and-white dirt and grime texture, mainly in crevices, along edges, and on flat areas. It works from surface curvature and ambient occlusion, and can add finer detail with micro height and micro normal maps. Its output is a monochrome mask, so you can use it to control where dirt or grunge appears on your model.\n\n**Required baked maps:** Position, Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, and World Space Normal.\n\n**Optional inputs:** Custom Grunge, Micro Normal, and Micro Height. Each accepts a custom texture or an anchor point.\n\n**Parameters** (the page doesn't list default values or ranges for any of them):\n\n- **Seed:** Sets the random pattern used for the dirt. You can randomize it or enter a specific value.\n- **Invert:** Flips the mask so dirt and clean areas swap.\n- **Dirt Level:** Controls how strong the dirt effect is.\n- **Dirt Contrast:** Controls the contrast of the dirt effect.\n- **Use Triplanar:** Projects the texture from the X, Y, and Z axes and blends the results, instead of following the UV layout.\n- **Triplanar Blending Contrast:** Controls how soft or sharp the transitions are between triplanar projections.\n- **Grunge Amount:** Controls how intense the grunge details are.\n- **Grunge Scale:** Controls the size of the grunge details.\n- **Use Custom Grunge:** Turns the custom grunge input on or off.\n- **Edges Masking:** Adjusts how much the dirt is masked along edges, based on the curvature map.\n\n**Micro Details:**\n\n- **Micro Height:** Turns the custom Micro Height input on or off.\n- **Micro Normal:** Turns the custom Micro Normal input on or off.\n- **Curvature Type:** Selects how curvature is calculated: Standard (sharp, can miss broad detail), Sobel (similar to Standard but slightly blurrier), or Smooth (blurs at multiple levels, giving smoother curves but possibly losing detail).\n- **Curvature Intensity:** Controls curvature strength in Standard and Sobel modes.\n- **Height Details Intensity:** Controls how much Micro Height detail is applied.\n- **AO Radius:** Controls the reach of ambient occlusion in micro details.\n- **AO Depth:** Controls the intensity of ambient occlusion in micro details."}]},"uuid":"6e3a7789-6cf9-47da-adaf-20435fd39ace","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:33.114Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a74a4869-6230-4fa3-bf1a-8c31488a3631","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6453dc26-8440-45bb-8135-285405498ab9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5f886428-d4dc-4506-8764-45de821ed068","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0158HbZRK1jKHX18ecLJ8z4b","type":"tool_result","content":"The **Metal Edge Wear** generator simulates damage and scratches on the parts of a mesh most likely to be knocked. It outputs a black-and-white mask, which you can use to add edge wear to a layer. It relies on these baked maps:\n\n- **Position**\n- **Curvature** (defines the edges)\n- **Ambient Occlusion**\n- **World Space Normal**\n\nYou can also supply optional custom inputs for grunge, micro normal, and micro height, either as textures or anchor points.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Main*\n1. **Seed:** Sets the random seed for the dirt texture. You can randomize it or enter a specific value.\n2. **Invert:** Flips the mask.\n3. **Wear Level:** Controls the total amount of wear.\n4. **Wear Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast of the final result.\n5. **Use Triplanar:** Projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout.\n6. **Triplanar Blending Contrast:** Controls how soft the transitions are between triplanar projections.\n7. **Grunge Amount:** Sets how strong the grunge details are.\n8. **Grunge Scale:** Sets the size of the grunge details.\n9. **Use Custom Grunge:** Turns a custom grunge map on or off.\n10. **Edges Smoothness:** Smooths the overall edges.\n11. **Ambient Occlusion Masking:** Uses AO to keep occluded areas from receiving wear.\n12. **Curvature Weight:** Sets how much the curvature map affects the result. Very low values can remove edge wear and leave only grunge.\n\n*Micro Details*\n13. **Micro Height:** Turns a custom Micro Height map on or off.\n14. **Micro Normal:** Turns a custom Micro Normal map on or off.\n15. **Curvature Type:** Chooses the curvature method: Standard (sharp, can miss broad detail), Sobel (similar to Standard but slightly blurrier), or Smooth (blurred levels that give smoother curves but can lose detail).\n16. **Curvature Intensity:** Sets curvature strength in Standard and Sobel modes.\n17. **Height Details Intensity:** Sets the strength of the Micro Height details.\n18. **AO Radius:** Sets the range of micro-detail ambient occlusion.\n19. **AO Depth:** Sets the intensity of micro-detail ambient occlusion.\n\nThe page does not list default values or value ranges for any parameter, so I can't provide them."}]},"uuid":"f1da95c5-e658-4eb4-8dac-98ac26b3ece9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:33.228Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a74a4869-6230-4fa3-bf1a-8c31488a3631","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f886428-d4dc-4506-8764-45de821ed068","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c132b176-8810-4576-a5eb-d414dfef100a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiFnJM1CrZsdYQrQarR6NR","type":"tool_result","content":"The Mask Editor is a generator that combines several inputs (custom textures, baked maps, and micro-detail layers) into one black-and-white mask. Because it's flexible, it can be heavier on performance than most generators. It needs baked position, thickness, curvature, ambient occlusion, and world space normal maps as image inputs.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **Texture and Texture (Secondary):** custom color textures or anchor points.\n- **World Space Normals, Position Gradient, Thickness, Curvature, Ambient Occlusion:** the matching baked maps.\n- **Micro Normal and Micro Height:** custom normal and height textures or anchor points.\n\n**Global controls** (applied after all layers combine)\n- **Global Invert:** flips the final result.\n- **Global Blur:** softens the whole mask.\n- **Global Balance:** shifts the midpoint toward black or white, like brightness.\n- **Global Contrast:** adjusts overall contrast.\n\n**Layer opacities**\n- Texture, Texture 2, Ambient Occlusion, Curvature, World Space Normal, Position Gradient, and Thickness each have an opacity control for their visibility.\n\n**Texture and Texture 2** (same settings for each)\n- **Invert:** flips the texture.\n- **Grayscale Conversion:** chooses how color becomes grayscale.\n- **Blending Mode:** sets how the layer blends with others.\n- **Scale:** sets the texture size.\n- **Contrast, Brightness:** adjust falloff and luminosity.\n- **Triplanar:** projects the texture from three axes instead of using UVs, with **Triplanar Contrast** controlling how softly the projections blend.\n- **Non-Square Tiling:** toggles non-square tiling.\n\n**Ambient Occlusion**\n- **Invert, Blending Mode, Blur, Balance, Contrast:** control inversion, blend, softness, midpoint, and falloff of the AO and micro detail.\n\n**Curvature**\n- **Invert** and **Blending Mode**.\n- **Mode:** Edges (convex areas), Cavities (concave areas), Dual (both), or Unprocessed (raw curvature).\n- **Sharp, Fine, Soft, Medium, Large, Big, Huge:** visibility of each curvature detail scale.\n- **Contrast, Brightness:** falloff and luminosity.\n\n**World Space Normal**\n- **Invert, Blending Mode, Blur, Balance, Contrast, Brightness:** same general roles as in other layers.\n- **Right to Left, Top to Bottom, Front to Back:** each direction has its own Invert and Blending Mode, controlling how the effect spreads across the mesh.\n\n**Position Gradient**\n- **Invert, Balance, Contrast, Brightness, Blending Mode.**\n- It is built from three sub-gradients (Right to Left, Top to Bottom, Front to Back), each with its own Invert and Blending Mode. These blend only with each other, not with other layers in the generator.\n\n**Thickness**\n- **Invert, Blur, Contrast, Brightness:** control inversion, softness, falloff, and luminosity.\n\n**Micro Details**\n- **Micro Height and Micro Normal:** toggle the custom maps on or off.\n- **Curvature Type:** Standard (sharp, can miss wide details), Sobel (similar but slightly blurrier), or Smooth (mipmap-style blur, smoother but can lose detail).\n- **Curvature Intensity:** strength for Standard and Sobel modes.\n- **Height Details Intensity:** strength of micro height detail.\n- **AO Radius and AO Depth:** range and intensity of micro ambient occlusion.\n\n**Not covered in this page**\nThe content you provided doesn't include Grunge, Scratches, or Scatter sections, a separate Gradient section (the closest match is Position Gradient), or any default values or numeric ranges. You'd need to check the Substance 3D Painter documentation or the application itself for those details."}]},"uuid":"96da8a2b-ae36-48da-9420-92b344614711","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:34.651Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a74a4869-6230-4fa3-bf1a-8c31488a3631","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c132b176-8810-4576-a5eb-d414dfef100a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"cb1cc0a7-34ec-42ea-9e0a-c6395a2d0704","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KhWgALFTaerBURHhxNcHsM","type":"tool_result","content":"The Mask Builder is a legacy, multi-purpose generator (the Mask Editor is its newer replacement). It combines several effects into one black-and-white mask and needs baked position, curvature, ambient occlusion, and world space normal maps as inputs. Its flexibility comes at a performance cost.\n\nThe page does not list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter, so I can't provide them.\n\n**Global controls**\n- **Seed:** Sets the random pattern for the dirt texture. You can randomize it or enter a specific value.\n- **Level:** Shifts the midpoint of the final mask, like brightness.\n- **Contrast:** Controls the sharpness of the final mask's falloff.\n- **Invert:** Flips the final mask.\n- **Use Triplanar:** Projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout.\n- **Triplanar Blending Contrast:** Controls how soft the transitions are between triplanar projections.\n- **Grunge, AO, Curvature, Top/Down Gradient, World Space Normal, Scratches, Scatter:** Each sets how strongly that effect contributes. Scratches only show when Grunge, AO, or Curvature is above 0.\n\n**Grunge**\n- **Scale:** Size of the grunge texture.\n- **Use Custom Grunge:** Toggles custom grunge map 1.\n- **Secondary Custom Grunge:** Sets the visibility of custom grunge map 2.\n- **Invert:** Inverts the grunge maps.\n\n**Ambient Occlusion**\n- **Range:** Span of the AO mask.\n- **Contrast:** Sharpness of the AO falloff.\n- **Noisiness:** Adds noise, which darkens the mask.\n- **Invert:** Inverts the AO mask.\n\n**Curvature**\n- **Convex Range / Convex Contrast / Convex Invert:** Set the minimum convex angle that gets highlighted, the convex contrast, and whether the convex mask is inverted.\n- **Concave Range / Concave Contrast / Concave Invert:** The same three controls for concave areas.\n- **Smoothness:** Softens the transition between light and dark areas.\n- **Level Boost:** Widens the masked area by multiplying the convex and concave ranges.\n- **Noisiness:** Adds noise, which darkens the mask.\n\n**Gradient (Top/Down)**\n- **Range:** Span of the gradient.\n- **Contrast:** Sharpness of the gradient.\n- **Invert:** Reverses the gradient.\n- The gradient uses the Position map, so its normalization scale (Full Scene or Per Material) affects how easy it is to adjust.\n\n**World Space Normal**\n- **Top, Bottom, Front, Back, Right, Left Intensity:** Each sets the strength of one directional gradient. By default, Front is the +X axis and Right is the +Z axis, which may not match your mesh's orientation.\n\n**Scratches**\n- **Amount:** Density of scratches.\n- **Scale:** Size of scratches.\n\n**Scatter**\n- **Scale:** Higher values create more, smaller stamps; lower values create fewer, larger ones.\n- **Density:** Number of stamps.\n- **Size:** Size of stamps.\n- **Size Variation:** Randomness in stamp size. Increasing it may require raising Size to keep the average.\n- **Opacity Variation:** Randomness in stamp opacity.\n\n**Micro Details**\n- **Micro Height:** Toggles the custom Micro Height map.\n- **Micro Normal:** Toggles the custom Micro Normal map.\n- **Curvature Type:** Standard (sharp, can miss broad detail), Sobel (similar but slightly blurrier), or Smooth (blurred levels that give smoother curves but can lose detail).\n- **Curvature Intensity:** Strength of curvature in Standard and Sobel modes.\n- **Height Details Intensity:** Strength of the Micro Height details.\n- **AO Radius:** Range of micro ambient occlusion.\n- **AO Depth:** Intensity of micro ambient occlusion."}]},"uuid":"d4902f8f-0ed0-41e6-a0b2-03264afafa17","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:36.838Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a74a4869-6230-4fa3-bf1a-8c31488a3631","context":{"git