{"parentUuid":"08b204dc-f471-4328-8239-a3c335af04fb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PBtxBQNcED1EnEzGDKKF4f","type":"tool_result","content":"The Light generator simulates a directional light hitting your mesh. It works from two baked maps, World Space Normal and Position, so you need to bake them first. It can be used in a fill layer, where it outputs color, metalness, specular roughness, normal, and height channels, or as a mask.\n\nThe page lists these parameters, but it doesn't give default values or ranges for any of them:\n\n- **Invert:** Flips the output color map.\n- **Horizontal Angle:** Sets the light's direction around the horizontal axis.\n- **Vertical Angle:** Sets the light's elevation.\n- **Highlight Glossiness:** Controls how widely the highlight spreads and fades.\n- **Highlight Level:** Controls the contrast of the highlight.\n- **Light Attenuation:** Controls how quickly the light falls off."}]},"uuid":"ae7e9f4e-ba43-4c30-b1f3-82c9819ae95d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:48.453Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"54bd6a7b-c5cd-4d60-bb3a-6471807c2dd3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08b204dc-f471-4328-8239-a3c335af04fb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"cde755d1-1c2c-4c7e-af20-4917d85d274c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EHTdtAfxYhFWMT6kLj1TR8","type":"tool_result","content":"The Position generator creates a black-and-white gradient mask based on where a surface sits in 3D space, such as top-to-bottom or side-to-side. It relies on two baked maps, a Position map and a World Space Normals map, so you'll need to bake them first. It can also take a custom texture or an anchor point as an input.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or ranges for any parameter.\n\n**Global parameters** (applied after all effects are combined)\n- **Global Invert:** Inverts the final mask.\n- **Global Blur:** Softens the final mask uniformly.\n- **Global Balance:** Shifts the final mask toward black or white, like brightness.\n- **Global Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast of the final mask.\n- **Use Texture:** Turns the custom texture on or off.\n\n**Position Gradient parameters**\n- **Invert:** Inverts only the gradient.\n- **Balance:** Shifts the gradient's midpoint toward black or white.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast and falloff of the gradient.\n- **Brightness:** Adjusts the gradient's luminosity.\n- **Right to Left:** Sets how the gradient applies across the mesh horizontally.\n- **Top To Bottom:** Sets how the gradient applies vertically.\n- **Front to Back:** Sets how the gradient applies depth-wise.\n\nEach directional gradient also has:\n- **Invert:** Reverses that gradient's direction.\n- **Blending Mode:** Chooses the blend mode used for that gradient.\n\n**Texture parameters** (for the custom texture input)\n- **Texture Opacity:** Sets the texture's visibility.\n- **Invert:** Inverts the texture.\n- **Grayscale Conversion:** Chooses the method for converting color to grayscale.\n- **Blending Mode:** Chooses the blend mode.\n- **Scale:** Sets the texture's size.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the texture's contrast and falloff.\n- **Brightness:** Adjusts the texture's luminosity.\n- **Triplanar:** When enabled, projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout.\n- **Triplanar Contrast:** Controls how softly the triplanar projections blend together."}]},"uuid":"efbae55a-7b11-4166-ad99-13291765aba7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:49.762Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"54bd6a7b-c5cd-4d60-bb3a-6471807c2dd3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cde755d1-1c2c-4c7e-af20-4917d85d274c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e9cbe11a-05bd-4357-81b4-5465470956f8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S1CUU9r4HeU3z1SLeuV7Hk","type":"tool_result","content":"The Ambient Occlusion generator builds a mask from the baked Ambient Occlusion map. You can optionally blend in a custom texture or micro details. It requires baked Position, Ambient Occlusion, and World Space Normal maps as inputs. When you use it as a layer mask, you may need to invert its output so the masked layer shows in occluded areas rather than unoccluded ones.\n\nThe page does not list default values or ranges for any parameter.\n\n**Global parameters (applied to the final mask)**\n- **Global Invert:** Flips the final result after all effects are combined.\n- **Global Blur:** Softens the final mask evenly.\n- **Global Balance:** Shifts the final mask toward black or white, like brightness.\n- **Global Contrast:** Adjusts the final mask's contrast.\n- **Use Texture:** Turns the custom texture on or off.\n- **Use Micro Details:** Turns the micro details on or off.\n\n**Ambient Occlusion**\n- **Invert:** Flips only the AO and micro detail data.\n- **Blur:** Softens only the AO and micro detail data.\n- **Balance:** Shifts the midpoint of the AO and micro detail data toward black or white.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast and falloff of the AO and micro detail data.\n\n**Texture**\n- **Texture Opacity:** Sets how visible the custom texture is.\n- **Invert:** Flips only the custom texture.\n- **Grayscale Conversion:** Chooses the method for converting the texture to grayscale.\n- **Blending Mode:** Chooses how the layer blends with the layers below.\n- **Scale:** Sets the size of the custom texture.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the texture's contrast and falloff.\n- **Brightness:** Adjusts the texture's luminosity.\n- **Triplanar:** Projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout.\n- **Triplanar Contrast:** Controls how softly the triplanar projections blend together.\n\n**Micro Details**\n- **Micro Height:** Turns the custom Micro Height map on or off.\n- **Micro Normal:** Turns the custom Micro Normal map on or off.\n- **AO Radius:** Sets the range of the micro detail occlusion.\n- **AO Depth:** Sets the intensity of the micro detail occlusion."}]},"uuid":"fd2397ab-f067-43ca-8828-3c88ddad2fb9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:50.329Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"54bd6a7b-c5cd-4d60-bb3a-6471807c2dd3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e9cbe11a-05bd-4357-81b4-5465470956f8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b2054fda-db0c-4bf3-9fcd-4ac18138b2d1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Vw5Y821uuJsTpAJUmjakZ","type":"tool_result","content":"The Curvature generator produces a black-and-white mask from the baked Curvature map. It can also blend in a custom texture or micro details. Because its output is monochrome, it's meant for use as a mask rather than applied directly to a layer. It requires a baked position map as input.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **Texture:** A custom texture or anchor point (color).\n- **Micro Normal:** A custom normal texture or anchor point (color).\n- **Micro Height:** A custom height texture or anchor point (color).\n- **Curvature:** The baked Curvature map (grayscale).\n- **World Space Normals:** The baked World Space Normals map (color).\n- **Position Gradient:** The baked Position map (color).\n\n**Global parameters** (applied after all effects combine)\n- **Global Invert:** Inverts the final result.\n- **Global Blur:** Uniformly softens the final mask.\n- **Global Balance:** Shifts the final mask toward black or white, like brightness.\n- **Global Contrast:** Adjusts the final mask's contrast.\n- **Use Texture:** Turns the custom texture on or off.\n- **Use Micro Details:** Turns the custom micro details on or off.\n\n**Curvature parameters**\n- **Invert:** Inverts the generated curvature map.\n- **Mode:** Chooses which areas are masked: Edges (convex), Cavities (concave), Dual (both), or Unprocessed (raw curvature mask).\n- **Sharp, Fine, Soft, Medium, Large, Big, Huge:** Each sets the strength of curvature detail at that scale, from sharpest to broadest.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast and falloff of the curvature.\n- **Brightness:** Adjusts the curvature's luminosity.\n\n**Texture parameters**\n- **Texture Opacity:** Sets how visible the custom texture is.\n- **Invert:** Inverts only the custom texture.\n- **Grayscale Conversion:** Chooses how a color texture is converted to black and white.\n- **Blending Mode:** Sets how the texture blends with the mask.\n- **Scale:** Sets the texture's size.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the texture's contrast and falloff.\n- **Brightness:** Adjusts the texture's luminosity.\n- **Triplanar:** Projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout.\n- **Triplanar Contrast:** Controls how softly projections blend when Triplanar is on.\n\n**Micro Details parameters**\n- **Micro Height:** Turns the custom Micro Height map on or off.\n- **Micro Normal:** Turns the custom Micro Normal map on or off.\n- **Curvature Type:** Chooses the calculation method: Standard (sharp, can miss broader detail), Sobel (similar to Standard but slightly blurrier), or Smooth (multiple blur levels, smoother curves, but finer detail can be lost).\n- **Curvature Intensity:** Sets the curvature strength in Standard and Sobel modes.\n- **Height Details Intensity:** Sets the strength of the Micro Height details.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"07027c3d-3c7d-43f3-8508-3fc117c1756f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:52.093Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"54bd6a7b-c5cd-4d60-bb3a-6471807c2dd3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b2054fda-db0c-4bf3-9fcd-4ac18138b2d1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
