{"parentUuid":"5bb2aabc-df2e-4657-8218-daf121d863a4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CC1YFLa1FjSuGJUJT4JJUc","type":"tool_result","content":"Effects are actions you apply to a layer's **content** or **mask** in Substance 3D Painter's layer stack. They range from simple color adjustments to complex mask construction. You can add them by right-clicking a layer or mask, or with the button above the layer stack. Most effects have their own blend mode and opacity, and you can reorder them to build a stack. Custom effects can also be made in Substance 3D Designer.\n\nThe overview page names the effect types but doesn't describe what each one does, so I can't tell you more about their individual functions. The linked pages should cover that.\n\n**Effect pages:**\n- Generator: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/generator\n- Paint: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/paint\n- Fill: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/fill\n- Levels: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/levels\n- Compare Mask: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/compare-mask\n- Filter: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/filter\n- Anchor Point: /en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/anchor-point\n\nThese are relative paths from the Adobe documentation site."}]},"uuid":"fc347e8c-2f6f-46b9-b390-25a12b03986c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:14.712Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"703640c8-e44e-4ce0-9bd5-06d805a577fa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5bb2aabc-df2e-4657-8218-daf121d863a4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":