{"parentUuid":"573135ef-ed18-40c5-a3bb-63b6cd0f05de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8VVr8MfgjTsQThPwhh5HT","type":"tool_result","content":"The Histogram Shift filter moves an image's entire tonal range. Values that go past one end wrap around to the other. You can apply it to a fill layer, or to a mask (which outputs black and white) to shift a single channel's full range.\n\nThe page lists one parameter:\n\n- **Position:** Sets how far the histogram is shifted. The page doesn't give a default value or range."}]},"uuid":"e824576e-e67b-4450-b589-ea2abcb25d0a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:52.845Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"573135ef-ed18-40c5-a3bb-63b6cd0f05de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f01f071b-1eac-44b1-b4fc-c7ded4db9d4d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RsakpiNpjw4FJxYZzK2zEh","type":"tool_result","content":"The Height Adjust filter changes a height channel in a non-destructive way. You can flip its values, shift them up or down, or scale them. It works on a texture layer or inside a mask, where the output is black and white.\n\nThe filter has three parameters:\n\n- **Invert:** A toggle that reverses the result.\n- **Offset:** Adds or subtracts a set amount from each height value.\n- **Multiply:** Scales the height values. Higher areas become higher and lower areas become lower.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or allowed ranges for any of these.\n\nOffset is applied before Multiply. If Offset brings a point's height to zero, Multiply has no effect there, because zero times any value is zero. To multiply first and then offset, stack a second Height Adjust filter."}]},"uuid":"e84e1be5-c0cc-4140-be97-13d16fa3ecc3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:53.125Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f01f071b-1eac-44b1-b4fc-c7ded4db9d4d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b17c1fe8-ec0d-4724-8db0-b8a5209df877","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A975EdiefNPkpWNyhjM6So","type":"tool_result","content":"The Bevel filter adds a raised, sloped edge along the borders of grayscale shapes and masks. You can apply it to a texture layer or inside a mask, where it produces a black-and-white relief effect.\n\nThe page lists five parameters:\n\n- **Bevel Wrap:** Makes the bevel tile seamlessly across the texture horizontally and vertically.\n- **Distance:** Sets how wide the bevel is.\n- **Corner Type:** Chooses whether bevel corners are rounded or sharp.\n- **Smoothing:** Softens the bevel. Without it, curved bevels can show jagged stepping along the curve.\n- **Blur Mode:** Chooses between uniform blur, which is more consistent, and non-uniform blur, which concentrates on the beveled areas and can preserve more detail.\n\nThe page doesn't give default values or numeric ranges for any parameter.\n\nIt also doesn't say whether the filter works from height data. It only describes grayscale shapes and masks, so I can't confirm height-map input from this content."}]},"uuid":"78d2943d-c21a-4441-b874-cc18237dd930","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:53.478Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b17c1fe8-ec0d-4724-8db0-b8a5209df877","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3621aa2b-8d18-4224-b29b-6271d20ce005","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Di4YgAXkmRg65NkX1PSmh1","type":"tool_result","content":"The Directional Distance filter generates a gradient of distance that extends in a direction you choose. Texture layers use it to create streaks, leaks, and similar distance-based effects. It can also serve as a mask for the height channel, which adds apparent depth to the normal channel.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Distance:** Sets how far the gradient extends. Values are normalized so that 1 equals the length of the shorter side of the input image. The page doesn't list a default or range.\n- **Angle:** Sets the gradient's direction, measured in turns. 0 points right, along the positive horizontal axis. The page doesn't list a default or range.\n- **Contrast:** Controls the contrast or falloff of the result. The page doesn't list a default or range.\n- **Distance Map Multiplier:** Controls how strongly the Distance Map input changes the maximum distance. It has no effect unless a Distance Map is connected. The page doesn't list a default or range.\n\n**Input**\n\n- **Distance Map (grayscale):** An optional input that accepts either a custom texture or an anchor point."}]},"uuid":"0fd87f61-7f3a-479b-97f6-5b2e2a4d2301","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:53.589Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3621aa2b-8d18-4224-b29b-6271d20ce005","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c5611a33-8e5b-4665-8fb3-e556172704b1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xnp44sTCykbaGTvPuhuav6","type":"tool_result","content":"The Bevel Smooth filter creates a soft, sloped gradient along the edges of a mask, extending outward, inward, or both ways. It works on a texture layer or inside a mask, typically producing black-and-white output.\n\nIt takes one input, a **Distance Map** (grayscale), which can be a custom texture or an anchor point.\n\n**Parameters** (the page doesn't list default values or ranges for any of them):\n\n1. **Direction:** Chooses which side of the mask's border gets expanded.\n2. **Distance:** Sets how far the bevel spreads from the edge.\n3. **Smoothing:** Controls how strongly the mask is softened.\n4. **Curve Offset:** Shifts the mask's border inward or outward.\n5. **Curve Shape:** Switches the slope between a pinched profile and a rounded one.\n6. **Mask Threshold:** Sets the input value used to detect the mask's edges.\n7. **Distance Map Multiplier:** Scales how much the Distance Map influences the maximum distance.\n8. **Bevel Wrap:** Turns tiling on or off, so the bevel wraps horizontally and vertically."}]},"uuid":"202ede60-4100-4c88-88ad-1cf457f25f56","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:53.854Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5611a33-8e5b-4665-8fb3-e556172704b1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e6752252-c611-45d6-839e-003d5f1f1498","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011BJ7hvBQRX4kXusSAo36H5","type":"tool_result","content":"The Highpass filter isolates fine detail by removing broad brightness variations, similar to a Photoshop action of the same name. It's commonly used on texture or mask layers to clean up images for tiling.\n\nThe page lists three parameters:\n\n- **Color Space:** Sets the color space the filter uses.\n- **Radius:** Controls the highpass radius, which determines how much of the large-scale luminance variation is removed.\n- **Apply To Alpha:** Toggles whether the filter also affects the Alpha channel.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"5193611a-7fa8-402a-9cd3-ad6c2b9e3386","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:53.854Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6752252-c611-45d6-839e-003d5f1f1498","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7b0963e1-7c5e-43f6-8fe5-0d89ba6b55e3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019WWnSMRUUaQxVb1tY3G2zk","type":"tool_result","content":"The Mask Outline filter traces the edges of a mask to create a border around a masked shape. You can use it on a texture layer or inside a mask, where it outputs black and white. The border can sit outside the shape, inside it, or on both sides.\n\n| Parameter | What it does | Default / Range |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mask Position** | Sets whether the outline sits outside the mask edge, inside it, or straddles both sides. | Not specified |\n| **Start From Black** | Flips the outline's starting tone, so it works like an invert switch. | Not specified |\n| **Threshold** | Sets how the filter detects the mask edge. | Not specified |\n| **Width** | Sets how thick the outline is. | Not specified |\n| **Blur** | Softens the outline. | Not specified |\n| **Curve Shape** | Controls how the outline fades out. | Not specified |\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"d76a95b7-79df-439f-a575-4d3d6fa93b7c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:54.212Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"92487ea5-9dcc-465f-be23-fc4b90bc8dab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7b0963e1-7c5e-43f6-8fe5-0d89ba6b55e3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
