{"parentUuid":"22ad2314-2e43-4fb6-992a-ea7e8c65340c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014veQasK8RvqZzYhY2xNGXc","type":"tool_result","content":"The Clamp filter restricts values to a chosen lower and upper bound. You can apply it to a fill layer to limit part of a material, or to a mask to keep its values within a set range. It works on each color channel separately, so it can shift a color's hue. If preserving hue matters, the page suggests Levels instead.\n\nThe filter has two parameters:\n\n- **Min:** Sets the lowest allowed value.\n- **Max:** Sets the highest allowed value.\n\nThe page does not list default values or valid ranges for either parameter."}]},"uuid":"6c9fcd92-33e9-477a-a8ff-31d1098cc038","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:06.464Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22ad2314-2e43-4fb6-992a-ea7e8c65340c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"97c92836-335c-4b96-83df-8c8f158d8a4a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mErNC9pHwgaj4yWXsSDaA","type":"tool_result","content":"The Gradient Curve filter remaps a texture's grayscale values through a curve you can shape with presets. You can apply it to a texture layer or inside a mask, where it outputs black and white. It's filed under the Effects, remap, and range categories.\n\nThe page lists four parameters, but none of them include default values or numeric ranges:\n\n- **Preset:** Chooses the shape of the curve.\n- **Invert:** Flips the result, so light areas become dark and dark areas become light.\n- **Balance:** Shifts the result toward black or white, similar to adjusting brightness.\n- **Contrast:** Controls how sharp or gradual the transition is between light and dark values."}]},"uuid":"98d8abe3-30a8-43ad-b6c1-74c321aa1d5c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:06.703Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97c92836-335c-4b96-83df-8c8f158d8a4a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5f4695a6-0cad-4f54-8e80-c9a5ea24e9e5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7Gn1yvhDxQBm8XxYtVUov","type":"tool_result","content":"The Smoothstep filter isolates a band of grayscale tones between two limits. Unlike Histogram Scan, it fades smoothly between the included and excluded tones instead of cutting off sharply. You can apply it directly to a fill layer or to a mask, where it produces a black-and-white result. It's a softer alternative to Threshold or Histogram Scan.\n\n**Parameters:**\n- **Minimum:** Sets the lower edge of the tonal range to keep. The page doesn't list a default or range.\n- **Maximum:** Sets the upper edge of the tonal range to keep. The page doesn't list a default or range."}]},"uuid":"9f5e6e08-1ad1-4e15-806e-a2b6de4f8275","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:06.960Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f4695a6-0cad-4f54-8e80-c9a5ea24e9e5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0264e0a3-cc21-4b60-b523-cb4d043bdb45","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015etvJBFUS8kZR16oKBaNA6","type":"tool_result","content":"The Quantize filter reduces a texture layer's image to a small set of colors, producing flatter, posterized, or stylized color areas. It also extracts a palette of the colors it uses.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or ranges for any parameter, so I've noted only what it describes:\n\n- **Color Amount:** Sets the upper limit on how many colors the result can use. The final count may be lower, and the Palette Color Amount output shows the actual number of extracted colors.\n- **Contour Smoothing:** Blurs the input before quantizing so the result forms simpler, more solid shapes. Higher values take noticeably longer to compute.\n- **Dithering:** Controls how much dithering recreates gradients and color blends using only the post-quantization colors. The page says to set Contour Smoothing to 0 to get the expected dithering effect.\n- **Dithering Pattern:** Chooses the pattern used for that dithering.\n- **Distance Color Space:** Chooses the color space used to compare and assign colors. Lab (Color) suits perceptual color images, and RGB (Data) suits raw data such as normal maps.\n- **Apply To Alpha:** Turns quantization of the layer's alpha channel on or off.\n- **Alpha Threshold:** Sets the cutoff value for alpha."}]},"uuid":"2635f475-35f6-468d-9c84-df0f3e42e9ce","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:07.205Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0264e0a3-cc21-4b60-b523-cb4d043bdb45","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"60e457da-e3f0-4601-a37e-68d2de9b05db","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SDwVvDuJmFG17Cr3E9EZZE","type":"tool_result","content":"The Anisotropic Kuwahara filter adds a painterly, stylized look to a texture layer or mask (black-and-white output). It blurs the image along directions it detects in the content, so strong edges and directional features stay defined. It works on full materials, noise, and masks.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- **Extract Direction:** Chooses how the filter determines the blur direction.\n- **Radius:** Sets the blur size. Larger values give a stronger effect. Maximum is 32.\n- **Smoothness:** Controls how much colors mix along the blur direction. At 0, colors shift mostly in that direction with little blending.\n- **Sharpness:** Adjusts contrast in blurred areas, making them look flatter or more defined.\n- **Tensor Smoothness:** Controls how much the computed direction map is blurred. Higher values help when the image has lots of fine high-frequency detail.\n- **Anisotropy:** Sets how strongly the direction map shapes the blur. The direction map still affects the result at 0, because it is used in the filter kernel.\n- **Anisotropy Angle:** Rotates the direction map, measured in turns. This adds to the value from the Anisotropy Angle Map input.\n\nThe page does not list default values or minimum/maximum ranges, except the Radius maximum of 32."}]},"uuid":"c0d54eba-53ac-49a9-9781-94a1e7e222d8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:07.439Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60e457da-e3f0-4601-a37e-68d2de9b05db","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d5f6c9ac-fc03-4bec-bff8-8632b54ab893","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QN5EqpL1iGDxgddnckXMGB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Threshold** is an effects/adjustments filter that converts an input into a high-contrast result. Each pixel is compared against a cutoff value using a chosen comparison rule. Pixels that satisfy the rule become white, and the output is black and white, which makes it useful for building masks from specific channels. It works like Histogram Scan but always uses maximum contrast, so it's a quicker route to similar results. You can apply it directly to a fill layer or to a mask.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- **Threshold:** The luminance value that input pixels are compared against.\n- **Mode:** The comparison rule. The options are Greater, Greater or equal, Lower, and Lower or equal.\n- **_mode:** An internal setting for the mode value. The page doesn't describe it further.\n- **_threshold:** An internal setting for the threshold value. The page doesn't describe it further.\n- **_threshold_min:** An internal setting for the minimum threshold value. The page doesn't describe it further.\n- **_threshold_max:** An internal setting for the maximum threshold value. The page doesn't describe it further.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"dc8f1824-a2ec-4450-a45a-60c401200343","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:07.500Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5f6c9ac-fc03-4bec-bff8-8632b54ab893","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8f65a701-7593-499b-8090-c28110438b4d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014hvfVknRe5YpFQkp7aLdaE","type":"tool_result","content":"The Gradient filter recolors a grayscale image by mapping its tones onto a custom gradient. You can use it to adjust a grayscale image's values or to add color to one.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or ranges for any parameter.\n\n**Main controls**\n- **Display Gradient (Debug):** Shows a debug view of the gradient.\n- **Color Quantity:** Sets how many colors the gradient uses.\n- **Blend Color in Linear:** Switches color blending to linear space.\n- **Color 1 / Color 2 / Color N:** Pick the colors in the gradient.\n- **Color 1 Position / Color 2 Position / Color N Position:** Set where each color sits along the gradient.\n\n**Input Transformation**\n- **Grayscale Mode:** Chooses how the input is converted to grayscale. Options are Desaturation, Luma, Average, Max, and Min.\n- **Blur Intensity:** Controls how much the input is blurred.\n- **Balance:** Shifts the midpoint toward black or white, similar to brightness.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts the input's contrast.\n- **Invert:** Reverses the input's colors."}]},"uuid":"57f81d05-7c08-45ec-82df-7a30be7a27d2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:07.566Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9640fcd0-c9d9-4bb1-b281-d3fb1e7ee820","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f65a701-7593-499b-8090-c28110438b4d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","vers