{"parentUuid":"5fed79ec-a57f-434c-a532-aeb0b9faf867","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpHXfui2sRAMNQMpDrRZbi","type":"tool_result","content":"**What it does:** MatFX Shut Line adds panel-line and seam detail to a material. You apply it to texture layers or material stacks to create recessed shut lines, raised seams, and extra height and color detail.\n\nThe page doesn't say what inputs it expects, whether it uses baked maps, or which output channels (such as height or normal) it writes to, so I can't confirm those details.\n\n**Parameters** (the page gives no default values or ranges):\n\n*Main settings:*\n- **Cavity Width:** Controls how wide the cavity (the recessed groove) is.\n- **Slope Intensity:** Controls how strong the slope effect along the edges of the line is.\n- **Emboss Strength:** Controls how pronounced the embossed relief is.\n- **Height Intensity:** Controls how strong the height effect is.\n\n*Material section:*\n- **Line Color:** Sets the color of the line.\n- **Source Material Opacity:** Sets how opaque the underlying source material is."}]},"uuid":"844f8e17-7bab-4b5a-931e-2464754ad17d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:33.644Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5fed79ec-a57f-434c-a532-aeb0b9faf867","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7dfcea24-244c-48fc-9ef2-65cb5ee181f0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0193RNmCeGq4qjU4b3XthqH9","type":"tool_result","content":"**What it does:** MatFX HBAO is a filter that creates horizon-based ambient occlusion from height data. You apply it to texture layers or masks to add depth and contact shadowing, based on a chosen source channel or height information. The page doesn't specify the output channels or any baked maps.\n\n**Parameters** (the page gives no default values or ranges for any of them):\n\n- **Blur Intensity:** Sets how strongly the result is blurred.\n- **Blur Wrap:** When enabled, blur sampling wraps around to the opposite edge of the texture.\n- **Channel Source:** Chooses which channel the occlusion is generated from.\n- **Use World Units:** Switches the effect to world-space units.\n- **Height Depth:** Adjusts how deep the height input appears.\n- **Radius:** Sets the sampling distance used for the occlusion.\n- **Intensity:** Controls the strength of the occlusion.\n- **Relief Balance:** Adjusts how much the relief contributes to the result."}]},"uuid":"e4735961-815b-45fa-a93f-de0c652673c3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:34.031Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7dfcea24-244c-48fc-9ef2-65cb5ee181f0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"740ddc00-4ea8-4de7-8bfd-a04905ca296c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uxq7kkd9otLdTfCGMBPwdt","type":"tool_result","content":"**What it does:** MatFX Edge Damages is a filter in the Effects/blur and grayscale category. It adds chipped, worn, and scratched detail along edges of texture layers or material stacks. Unlike MatFX Detail Edge Wear, it doesn't change the color of damaged areas, so it suits plastics and resins better than painted metal. The page says the filter can change the height channel, but only if height data already exists in layers below it. Otherwise, the height change has no visible effect. The page doesn't describe baked-map inputs or normal-channel output.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n| Parameter | What it controls | Default/range |\n|---|---|---|\n| Blur Intensity | Strength of the blur effect | Not listed |\n| Blur Wrap | On/off toggle. When on, blur samples pixels from the opposite side of the texture. | Not listed |\n| Level | Overall amount of damage | Not listed |\n| Contrast | Contrast or falloff of the result | Not listed |\n| Scratches Intensity | Strength of the scratches | Not listed |\n| Damages Roughness | Roughness of damaged areas | Not listed |\n| Damages Depth | Depth of damaged areas | Not listed |\n\nThe page doesn't give default values or numeric ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"3dc4fdfe-9681-4e7e-81c9-a41209d51ab7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:35.056Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"740ddc00-4ea8-4de7-8bfd-a04905ca296c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"07b9f23f-e5e2-4838-85b3-9bf87dc660a0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jh5ybKPzV2tZfgg9pP4Nvz","type":"tool_result","content":"The MatFX Peeling Paint filter, found under Effects/blur and grayscale, simulates flaking and chipped paint on texture layers or material stacks. To reveal the material beneath, place the filter inside a group. Layers below it in the stack then show through wherever the simulated paint lifts away. The page doesn't specify baked maps or the exact output channels, though some parameters below reference height, normal, and ambient occlusion.\n\n**Core peeling and blur controls**\n- **Blur Intensity:** Sets how strong the blur is.\n- **Blur Wrap:** When on, the blur samples pixels from the opposite edge of the texture, so it tiles seamlessly.\n- **Peeling Level:** Sets the overall amount of peeling.\n- **Peeling Distance:** Sets how far the paint appears to lift off the surface.\n- **Flake Level:** Sets how much flaking occurs.\n- **Air Bubble Density:** Sets how many air bubbles appear.\n- **Flaking Density:** Sets how densely flakes are distributed.\n- **Flaking X Amount:** Sets the flake amount along the X axis.\n- **Flaking Y Amount:** Sets the flake amount along the Y axis.\n\n**Curvature input**\n- **Use Curvature:** Toggles whether the curvature input affects the result.\n- **Curvature Distance:** Sets the distance over which curvature is sampled.\n- **Curvature Contrast:** Sets the contrast of the curvature input.\n\n**Technical parameters (top surface of the peeled material)**\n- **Luminosity:** Adjusts brightness.\n- **Contrast:** Adjusts contrast or the falloff of the result.\n- **Hue Shift:** Shifts the hue.\n- **Saturation:** Adjusts color saturation.\n- **Normal Intensity:** Adjusts the strength of the normal effect.\n- **Height Range:** Sets the height range the effect uses.\n- **Height Position:** Sets the height position the effect uses.\n- **Ambient Occlusion Intensity:** Adjusts the strength of ambient occlusion.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter."}]},"uuid":"c79e471f-d546-4330-966b-4b2da9f7ff8a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:35.189Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07b9f23f-e5e2-4838-85b3-9bf87dc660a0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b0aeaa9c-62e6-42e6-905c-4f6630fe5f97","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q93JyZypiSsvDN95MNjttn","type":"tool_result","content":"**MatFX Water Drops** is a filter for texture layers or material stacks in Substance 3D Painter. It generates water droplets, directional streaks, and wet-surface variation. It takes three baked maps as inputs: ambient occlusion (grayscale), world-space normals (color), and position (color).\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or allowable ranges for any parameter, so I've described only what each one controls.\n\n**Drops**\n- **Drops Amount:** How many droplets appear.\n- **Drops Scale X / Scale Y:** The droplet size along each axis.\n- **Drops Scale Random:** How much droplet sizes vary.\n- **Drops Direction Intensity:** How strongly droplets are streaked in a direction.\n\n**Position**\n- **Influence X / Y / Z:** How much the position map affects droplet placement along each axis.\n\n**Water Accumulation**\n- **Intensity:** How much water collects.\n- **Spread:** How far the accumulation extends.\n- **AO Based Intensity:** How much ambient occlusion influences where water collects.\n\n**World Space**\n- **Masking Intensity:** Overall strength of world-space masking.\n- **Top / Bottom Intensity:** Droplet strength on upward- and downward-facing surfaces.\n- **Front / Back Intensity:** Droplet strength on front- and back-facing surfaces.\n- **Left / Right Intensity:** Droplet strength on left- and right-facing surfaces.\n\n**Material**\n- **Drops Base Color Warp Intensity:** How much the base color shifts under the droplets.\n- **Drops Rotation Vector Map Multiplier:** Scales the drop rotation vector map.\n- **Drops Height Intensity:** Strength of the droplets' height effect.\n- **Drops Roughness:** Roughness of the droplets.\n- **Drops Roughness Blending:** How droplet roughness mixes with the underlying material.\n- **Drops Metallic:** Metallic value of the droplets.\n- **Drops Metallic Blending:** How droplet metallic values mix with the underlying material.\n- **Normal Intensity:** Strength of the normal effect.\n\nThe page doesn't specify which output channels the filter writes. The height and normal parameters suggest it affects those channels, but this isn't confirmed."}]},"uuid":"bb7871f2-2679-4837-bab3-ba12976851fe","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:35.389Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b0aeaa9c-62e6-42e6-905c-4f6630fe5f97","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4715098d-d5fe-41fa-ab3b-a04d3e0a3f1f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GEkmRfQQ5MYHrG6NpVKRp5","type":"tool_result","content":"The MatFX Rust Weathering filter adds rust buildup, corrosion, drips, and aged wear to a material. You apply it to texture layers or material stacks. The page doesn't say what inputs it expects or which output maps it writes, beyond the channels in its blending controls: normal, ambient occlusion, height, base color, roughness, and metallic.\n\n**Blur**\n- **Blur Intensity:** Sets how strong the blur is.\n- **Blur Wrap:** When on, the blur samples pixels from the opposite edge of the texture, so it stays seamless across tile boundaries.\n\n**Rust and Varnish**\n- **Rust Spreading:** Controls how far the rust spreads.\n- **Spreading Smoothness:** Controls how soft the edges of the spreading are.\n- **Varnish Damage Scale:** Controls the scale of the varnish damage.\n\n**Drips**\n- **Drips Intensity:** Controls how strong the drips are.\n- **Drips Samples Amount:** Controls the number of samples used for the drips.\n- **Drips Smoothness:** Controls how smooth the drips look.\n\n**Blending (normal, AO, height)**\n- **Normal Intensity:** Controls how strongly the normal map is blended.\n- **Ambient Occlusion Intensity:** Controls how strongly the AO map is blended.\n- **Height Intensity:** Controls how strongly the height map is blended.\n\n**Metallic Roughness (base color, roughness, metallic)**\n- **Base Color Intensity:** Controls how strongly the base color is affected.\n- **Roughness Intensity:** Controls how strongly the roughness map is blended.\n- **Metallic Intensity:** Controls how strongly the metallic map is blended.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or ranges for any parameter, so check those in the Painter interface."}]},"uuid":"2992e7e2-d224-49ea-84bf-1f7c7558cf30","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:35.647Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4715098d-d5fe-41fa-ab3b-a04d3e0a3f1f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"52c86ba7-9e5d-4989-aff8-48e9257c81fd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011dKtFn6eujaaQXbUjjDXvv","type":"tool_result","content":"**What it does:** MatFX Detail Edge Wear adds worn edges and grunge breakup to a texture layer or material stack. It finds edges from the varied normal information in the layers below it, so it has no visible effect if the normal channel is empty or uniform. The page also says it can adjust material properties, driven by masks and curvature. It doesn't describe baked-map inputs or name specific output channels such as height or roughness beyond the material settings below.\n\n**Parameters** (the page lists no default values or ranges for any of them)\n\n**General wear controls**\n- **Blur Intensity:** Sets how strong the blur is.\n- **Blur Wrap:** Toggles whether the blur samples from the opposite edge of the texture.\n- **Input Mode:** Selects the input used to drive the wear.\n- **Wear Level:** Sets the overall amount of wear.\n- **Wear Contrast:** Sets the contrast of the wear mask.\n- **Edges Smoothness:** Sets how soft or smooth the worn edges look.\n- **Grunge Amount:** Sets how much grunge is added to the wear.\n- **Grunge Scale:** Sets the size of the grunge pattern.\n\n**Material (PBR Metallic Roughness)**\n- **Base Color:** Sets how much the base color contributes.\n- **Metallic:** Sets the metallic value.\n- **Roughness:** Sets the roughness value.\n\n**Material (PBR Specular Glossiness)**\n- **Diffuse:** Sets how much the diffuse contributes.\n- **Specular Color:** Sets the specular color.\n- **Glossiness:** Sets the glossiness value.\n\n**Settings**\n- **Generator Mask Control:** Sets how strongly the generator mask influences the effect.\n- **Generator Mask Contrast:** Sets the contrast of the generator mask.\n- **Generator Mask Blur:** Sets the blur applied to the generator mask.\n- **Alpha Background Value:** Sets the background alpha value.\n- **Curvature Intensity:** Sets the strength of the curvature input.\n- **Invert Curvature:** Toggles inversion of the curvature input.\n- **Combine Curvature:** Toggles blending the inverted and non-inverted curvature data.\n- **Normal Intensity:** Sets the normal intensity.\n- **AO Spreading:** Sets how far the ambient occlusion effect spreads."}]},"uuid":"4da00313-a407-49af-b606-2bec303746fc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:35.951Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aeadfd69-bdc8-4d00-81fd-bbead0ccd2b2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52c86ba7-9e5d-4989-aff8-48e9257c81fd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
