{"parentUuid":"26a12156-6eb3-4791-acad-e20faff23302","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01357z2B1BFi4pAzA7vvgAP8","type":"tool_result","content":"An anchor point exposes a layer or mask element in the stack so other layers can reference it, each with its own adjustments. This lets you link layers or masks so one anchor affects several parts of a project. You add one from the Effects menu, on either a layer or a mask.\n\nOther layers can reference an anchor point from a Fill Layer, a Fill Effect, or the input of a substance filter (Effect, Procedural, or Generator). The referencing layer then uses the anchor's content.\n\nKey caveats from the page:\n- Only anchors **below** the referencing layer can be used. Moving an anchor above it breaks the reference, though you can undo that.\n- Anchors can only be referenced within the texture set where they were created. Links across texture sets aren't possible.\n- In the anchor's properties, you can see which layers reference it. From a Fill layer or effect that uses an anchor, you can jump to the anchor.\n\nThe page doesn't cover Custom Noise or Micro Height inputs, the behavior of anchors on height channels versus masks, how changes propagate, resolution, or channel-specific details. You'd need other Substance 3D Painter documentation for those."}]},"uuid":"1b1d696d-7f25-4d4f-8d9c-c2d9f3a88be0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:46.021Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5d5ebc15-23ac-4ce9-a8fd-a21e16dee8a6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"26a12156-6eb3-4791-acad-e20faff23302","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"