{"parentUuid":"ed9a0371-ff37-4977-bde9-818dd45943e2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuA7xp7Gj4qGc3PsaD6n5H","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance 3D Painter \"Normal Mixing\" Combine Replace height channel normal channel texture set settings height force documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Normal Map Painting\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/painting/advanced-channel-painting/normal-map-painting\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-painter-discussions/prevent-height-map-data-baked-into-normal-map/m-p/14472860\"},{\"title\":\"Texture Set settings\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/interface/texture-set/texture-set-settings\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Painter 1.x\",\"url\":\"https://steamcommunity.com/app/273390/discussions/0/143388250762926599/?l=greek\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-painter-discussions/how-to-get-normals-to-not-bleed-through-from-texture-to-another/m-p/15216233\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Painter 1.x\",\"url\":\"https://steamcommunity.com/app/273390/discussions/0/143388250762926599\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-painter-discussions/paint-over-parts-of-height-map-with-new-height-info/m-p/14706657/highlight/true\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-painter-discussions/how-to-export-only-the-normal-texture-map-instead-of-height/td-p/13749466\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2690730/\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Texture Set settings\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/interface/texture-set/texture-set-settings\"},{\"title\":\"texture set settings\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/interface/texture-set/texture-set-settings.html\"},{\"title\":\"Normal Map Painting\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/painting/advanced-channel-painting/normal-map-painting\"},{\"title\":\"texture set list\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/interface/texture-set/texture-set-list.html\"},{\"title\":\"8 Easy Steps To Import Paintable Textures In Substance Painter\",\"url\":\"https://nest.point-broadband.com/?p=11809\"},{\"title\":\"From the course: Substance Painter 2018 Essential Training\",\"url\":\"https://origin-www.lynda.com/Substance-Painter-tutorials/Understanding-texture-sets-settings/746259/793472-4.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2543838\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2544039\"},{\"title\":\"How to convert height into a Normal Map in Substance Painter\",\"url\":\"https://www.versluis.com/2023/10/how-to-convert-height-into-a-normal-map-in-substance-painter/\"}]\n\nThe official docs cover the Normal mixing setting and the height channel, but the search didn't turn up an official explanation of \"height force.\"\n\n**Normal mixing (Texture Set settings)**\n- The setting controls how the baked normal map is combined with the Normal channel. Replace ignores the baked normal map and uses only the Normal channel for that Texture Set. The other option, Combine, is the default and uses a detail-oriented function to merge the Normal channel with the baked normal map.\n- If the Normal channel is missing or empty, the baked normal map is still used under Replace (if the Normal channel is not present or if the Normal channel output is empty the baked normal map will still be used.).\n- The docs describe Replace as the way to paint over a baked normal map. A new texture set starts on Combine, so switching to Replace is required before you can override the normal map. The viewport normal map then disappears, which the docs call expected. Replace makes Painter use only the Normal and Height channels when it generates the final normal map. (Source: the Normal Map Painting page in the Advanced channel painting docs.)\n\n**Height channel and normal output**\n- Painter converts height into normal data. When you paint with the height channel, Painter automatically converts that height into the normal map.\n- The Height to normal method setting offers Sharp, which produces a more defined normal map at the risk of noise and aliasing and is suited to repeating patterns like fabrics. The default, Smooth (Sobel), produces a smoother normal map with a Sobel filter, at the risk of losing details, and suits most cases.\n- Adobe staff say most export presets merge height into the normal map by design. Most of its export presets merge the Height and the Normal channel. To keep them separate, you can create your own export preset with only the channels needed.\n\n**Height force**\n- I found no official doc entry for \"height force\" in these results. The only mention is a Polycount forum post saying to keep the height force at 1 in Substance Painter, since it is a legacy shader setting that should not be modified. That is community advice, not Adobe documentation, so verify it against your Painter version.\n- The same thread notes that in Painter the height channel is used to generate normal map data, so real displacement or parallax needs a separate displacement channel. Parallax is set in the shader settings, which the post says is only available in Painter 2.6 and later.\n\n**Common pitfall**\n- Switching Normal mixing to Replace to fix height blending can remove the rest of the height detail. One Polycount user found that changing the texture set's Normal Mixing setting to Replace just nukes all of the height detail except for the stitches. Because Replace takes height from the Normal and Height channels only, painting over a texture set can lose the existing height detail.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"90a96389-d14f-4b96-8953-bd8e6a6984b8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:23.203Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8af76bfa-c61e-40b1-94da-68feaaebdbdf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed9a0371-ff37-4977-bde9-818dd45943e2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
