{"parentUuid":"02fa01a5-f7ad-4443-a78d-ac49c5c3a750","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F1BRorKJqx26RMw2jNWqfW","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't cover everything you asked about. It doesn't discuss Sharp vs. Smooth Sobel conversion, converting height to normal, or brush height settings, so I can only address the normal and height interaction it does describe.\n\n**How Painter combines normals and height:**\n\n- **Painting normals:** You add a normal channel to the Texture Set, enable it on your painting tool, and load a normal map into the tool's Material section. Painting works much like height map painting, but the baked normal gives more precise detail.\n- **Blending modes:** Normal layers offer three modes: Detail (the default), Inverse Detail, and Combine.\n- **Color space:** Painter assumes DirectX (Y-) normal maps by default, regardless of project settings. For OpenGL (Y+) maps, change the bitmap's color space from its settings menu.\n- **Normal mixing:** A Texture Set defaults to Combine, which merges the painted normals with the baked normal. Switching to Replace makes the final normal map come only from the normal and height channels, so the baked normal disappears from the viewport.\n- **Painting over a baked normal:** Set normal mixing to Replace, add a fill layer with the baked normal in its normal slot (adjusting tiling if needed), and set that layer's normal blend mode to \"normal,\" since the bitmap has no alpha and replaces what's below. Layers above it can then paint over the baked detail."}]},"uuid":"5d189a35-ad91-4a1f-a2bf-a0b4e5eef771","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:35.247Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"68e55f48-88bb-4e96-bf04-b0c7012cbc00","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02fa01a5-f7ad-4443-a78d-ac49c5c3a750","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bf4755b1-a7eb-4ae2-90ec-6611a1f3b684","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NwHWiXND18EL9wtHRNDZAa","type":"tool_result","content":"Height painting in Painter works like this:\n\n- **Workflow:** You load a normal map baked from a high-poly mesh onto the low-poly mesh and paint extra surface detail on the height channel. Painter composites your height through all layers, converts it to a normal map in real time, and blends it with the high-poly normal. You only need to paint height.\n- **HDR format:** The height channel stores positive and negative values without the 0-255 brightness ceiling of traditional height maps.\n- **Painting with textures:** When you paint with a bitmap or Substance source, its 0-255 values are remapped to -1 to 1. Mid-grey becomes zero. Darker values subtract height and lighter values add it, under the default blend mode, Linear Dodge (Add).\n- **Painting with color:** A flat color lets you pick a height value directly between -1 and 1.\n- **Visualization:** In Solo mode, the default preview shows only positive values, with negatives appearing as strong black. The +/- color setting displays both directions in different colors. The Scale setting widens or narrows the visible range when you've added or subtracted beyond -1 to 1.\n\nThe source doesn't cover the other blend modes (Subtract, Replace, Normal), the full set of height brush settings, displacement output, or height depth and world-unit scaling, so I can't describe those from this page."}]},"uuid":"47e5ce2b-da5f-4325-a260-164ec337fa8b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:35.266Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"68e55f48-88bb-4e96-bf04-b0c7012cbc00","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf4755b1-a7eb-4ae2-90ec-6611a1f3b684","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"94a4e3bd-5bb0-47d8-a8a1-c6cd4d15829b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EHBbKApgXzodEnkSVSmvbb","type":"tool_result","content":"**Texture Set settings**\n\n- **Name:** The texture set's label, usually inherited from the material name on the 3D model.\n- **Description:** A free-text note shown in the Texture Set list and Baking windows.\n- **Size:** Sets channel resolution. You can unlock the width/height link for non-square sizes. Resolution is adjustable at any time, and the app caps internal channels at 4096 and exports at up to 8192 if the GPU supports it. Changing it may trigger a long recomputation.\n- **Shader instance:** Chooses which shader renders the texture set in the viewport.\n\n**Channels list**\n\n- **Add channel:** Opens a menu of supported, unsupported, and user channels. There's no hard limit, but many channels cost performance and memory.\n- **Remove channel:** Drops a channel from the list without deleting its painted data, so it can be restored later.\n- **Channel name:** Shows the channel's name. Only user channels can be renamed.\n- **Channel settings (storage format):** Sets precision and layout: 8-bit, 16-bit, or 16/32-bit float, in grayscale (L) or RGB variants. The format doesn't change how the app interprets the data's color space.\n- **Channel settings (color management):** Toggles color management, editable only for user channels.\n- **Color managed indicator:** Shows whether a channel is color managed.\n\n**Mixing settings**\n\n- **Normal mixing:** *Replace* ignores the baked normal map and uses only your Normal channel. *Combine* (default) blends them with a detail-oriented function. This is disabled if no Normal channel exists.\n- **Height to normal method:** Converts height data to a normal map. *Sharp* gives crisper detail but may add noise and aliasing, suiting repeating patterns like fabric. *Smooth (Sobel)* (default) is smoother but can lose fine detail.\n- **Ambient occlusion mixing:** *Replace* uses only your AO channel. *Multiply* (default) multiplies it with the baked AO. This is disabled if no AO channel exists.\n- **UV padding:** Controls the border pixels outside UV islands. *3D Space Neighbor* (default) samples across UV seams, good for continuous patterns. *2D Space Neighbor* copies from within each island, better for islands with very different content. The normal channel always uses the 2D method.\n\n**Mesh maps**\n\nThese are baked textures specific to the mesh and texture set. They feed filters, Smart Materials, and Smart Masks. The page doesn't list individual maps or a bake button; see the baking documentation for those.\n\n**Not covered on this page**\n\nThe page doesn't describe OpenGL/DirectX normal map format options, or any height depth, tessellation, displacement, scale, or offset parameters. Height appears only in the Height to normal method setting. Check other Substance 3D Painter documentation for those."}]},"uuid":"aab70061-d9fb-44e2-9106-9546c2fa0570","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:39.828Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"68e55f48-88bb-4e96-bf04-b0c7012cbc00","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"94a4e3bd-5bb0-47d8-a8a1-c6cd4d15829b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
