r add-on packs.\n\n**What the results show about edge, dirt, and light masks:**\n- One marketplace pack includes 20 edge-dirt masks built in Substance Painter version 11, which it says are meant for adding wear and dirt along model edges. This collection features 20 smart mask (Smart Mask) dirt edge masks, meticulously designed and crafted in Substance Painter version 11.\n- A separate 15-mask dirt pack says its masks intelligently place dirt and grime exactly where it naturally accumulates — crevices, corners, under edges, and low areas.\n- A 47-mask metal pack lists categories including Edge Damage / Scratches / Grunge & Dust / Paint Wear / Rust / Heavy Worn Surfaces. Its listing gives the install location as Documents/Adobe/Substance 3D Painter/assets/smart-masks, which is where custom masks go, not a list of built-in ones.\n- A 10-mask collection covers edge wear, dirt accumulation, rust, scratches, and more.\n\n**What's missing:** Nothing here covers the Mask Editor, a \"Light\" smart mask, or the default smart mask library that ships with the software. For that, check Adobe's official Substance 3D Painter documentation under Smart Masks, or open the Shelf in the app and browse the Smart Masks section. Those sources will reflect your installed version.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"07059aa0-3f4d-4bdf-afdf-27f6bcf8c009","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:49.499Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a539946d-4874-47bf-be08-56d6e54b2838","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b872a737-d0be-46e1-9fae-c9af1ae48223","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray