{"parentUuid":"efc30bf1-5b4c-484f-8655-da7506b1dd6d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LNLuK2vMp1PRAG8xXBEdHr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance 3D Painter smart masks smart materials documentation what is a smart mask baked mesh maps experienceleague\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"smart materials and masks\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/features/smart-materials-and-masks.html\"},{\"title\":\"Smart mask\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-dev/painter-python/api/substancepainter-package/layerstack-module/layers-and-effects/smartmask\"},{\"title\":\"Smart Materials and Masks\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/features/smart-materials-and-masks\"},{\"title\":\"Masking and effects\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/interface/layer-stack/masking-and-effects\"},{\"title\":\"masking and effects\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/interface/layer-stack/masking-and-effects.html\"},{\"title\":\"how to use smart masks in substance painter\",\"url\":\"https://scil-wiki.su.edu/books/texturing/page/how-to-use-smart-masks-in-substance-painter\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Painter | Research\",\"url\":\"https://sophierowsonmediaproject1.blogs.lincoln.ac.uk/?p=274\"},{\"title\":\"smart materials and masks\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/ja/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/features/smart-materials-and-masks\"},{\"title\":\"scil-wiki.su.edu\",\"url\":\"https://scil-wiki.su.edu/books/texturing/page/how-to-use-smart-masks-in-substance-painter/export/pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Materiales inteligentes y máscaras\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/es/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/features/smart-materials-and-masks\"}]\n\nSmart masks are reusable mask setups in Substance 3D Painter. The search returned the smart mask documentation but not the baking page, so I can't yet confirm how baked mesh maps relate to them.\n\n**What a smart mask is**\nThe developer documentation describes smart masks as presets of the mask effect stack, which lets you save and re-use complex mask configurations across projects. The user guide frames them the same way: a way to save a mask and its effect to easily re-use them on other layers or other projects.\n\n**Creating and applying one**\n- You create one from an existing mask by right-clicking it and choosing the create option (\"Create smart mask\").\n- Dropping a smart mask onto a layer creates a black mask if none exists. If a mask already exists, the effects are merged into it. Holding CTRL while dropping the smart mask overwrites the whole effect list instead.\n- Placement is limited: smart materials can be used anywhere in the layer stack, while smart masks can only be used in the effect stack.\n\n**Baking mesh maps**\nThe Experience League table of contents has a Baking section with a \"How to bake mesh maps\" page, plus pages on mesh map settings and baking visualization settings. However, the search results only show those page titles, not their content. For baking steps, open that page directly: experienceleague.adobe.com under Substance 3D Painter, Baking.\n\n**Documentation location**\nAdobe moved Substance 3D Painter documentation to Experience League, and after March 14th, HelpX pages will automatically redirect to the equivalent Experience League page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d5dc3cd2-c92c-404b-a457-c50e0e4fdde0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:51.039Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a539946d-4874-47bf-be08-56d6e54b2838","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility