{"parentUuid":"4fb5f866-cec2-486d-975b-e4208a401e07","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jz54V55oHWVyexbQFwLCRn","type":"tool_result","content":"The page covers masks and effects only at a high level. It doesn't explain the individual effect types (Paint, Fill, Levels, Compare Mask, Filter, Generator, Anchor point), evaluation order, blend modes, opacity, folders, or the \"Add black/white mask\" options. Those are on the linked effects page.\n\n**What this page covers:**\n\n- **Mask basics:** A mask acts as an intensity control over a layer's content, and it is always grayscale. Colors you paint onto a mask are converted to gray values.\n- **Creating masks:** You can add one from the right-click menu or the dedicated button. Holding Ctrl while dragging a fill layer in creates a mask at the same time.\n- **Replacing masks:** Adding or removing a mask again deletes it along with any effects attached to it.\n- **Mask tools:** Alt-clicking a mask thumbnail isolates it in the viewport. Shift-clicking toggles it off and on. You can copy a mask's content into another mask and invert a mask's background, which helps keep effects intact.\n- **Effects placement:** Effects can go on a mask or on a layer's content. Generators, for example, suit masks. Each has its own stack, and a thumbnail's underline shows whether effects exist (gray for none, red for one or more).\n- **Smart masks:** You can save a mask and its effects for reuse. Dropping one onto a layer creates a black mask if none exists, or merges its effects into the existing list. Holding Ctrl while dropping replaces the list instead."}]},"uuid":"40e74f05-108f-4c96-a78e-85f61751e9fa","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:01.298Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e3c6b700-cca2-4f43-8e7c-f995cd4e9eef","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4fb5f866-cec2-486d-975b-e4208a401e07","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f534e68e-b73a-4d19-b3e6-5353687c24e6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Naoz2LEsgexSbnDSf8X9Bk","type":"tool_result","content":"**Smart materials** are reusable layer presets. You can apply a similar texturing workflow across texture sets or projects, and the results adapt to each mesh's topology. **Smart masks** are presets of effects, so they work only within effect stacks.\n\n**Creating them:** A smart material is built from a folder. Right-clicking the folder and choosing the create option adds the preset to the current shelf, named after the folder. A smart mask is made by right-clicking a layer and choosing the create option.\n\n**Saving and sharing:** Presets are saved to disk in a dedicated folder. You can find the shelf location in the documentation on adding content from the hard drive. Others can import the file into their own shelf.\n\n**Applying them:**\n- Smart materials can be dragged from the shelf into the layer stack, or added through a Smart Material button that opens a mini-shelf.\n- Smart masks are dragged onto a target layer. Dragging several accumulates them. Holding CTRL while dropping replaces the whole effect stack.\n\n**Placement:** Smart materials can go anywhere in the layer stack, while smart masks are restricted to effect stacks.\n\n**Limitations:** Once added, the stack doesn't record which smart material was used, so updating one means redoing the work manually. Individual resources can be refreshed with the Resources Updater.\n\n**Mesh maps and baked maps:** The page doesn't describe which mesh maps smart materials depend on, how generators or filters read baked maps, or any baked map requirements. It only says presets adapt to mesh topology, so I can't confirm those details from this content."}]},"uuid":"2c12bebf-ad64-4762-a2c4-3188687902e8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:01.681Z",