{"parentUuid":"b932fec1-d84d-4092-b134-f9f32ff87ed3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TA8KoKTHYVb4UrjFyJ19hi","type":"tool_result","content":"The Fiber Glass Edge Wear generator creates a black-and-white mask that simulates worn and frayed edges on fiberglass. It works from baked Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal, and Position maps. You can optionally add Micro Height and Micro Normal maps, or a custom grunge texture, for finer detail.\n\nThe page doesn't list default values or numeric ranges for any parameter.\n\n**Core parameters**\n- **Seed:** Sets the random pattern used for the dirt texture. You can randomize it or enter a specific value.\n- **Invert:** Flips selected internal maps, such as Curvature or AO, before they're combined.\n- **Wear Level:** Controls the overall amount of wear and how visible the effect is.\n- **Wear Contrast:** Adjusts the contrast of the final wear result.\n- **Use Triplanar:** Projects the texture from three axes instead of following the UV layout, then blends the results.\n- **Triplanar Blending Contrast:** Controls how soft or sharp the transitions are between triplanar projections.\n- **Grunge Amount:** Sets the intensity of the grunge detail.\n- **Use Custom Grunge:** Turns a custom grunge map on or off.\n- **Edges Smoothness:** Controls how soft the edge wear appears.\n- **Ambient Occlusion Masking:** Sets how strongly the AO map influences the result.\n- **Curvature Weight:** Sets how strongly the curvature map influences the result.\n\n**Micro Details**\n- **Micro Height:** Turns the custom Micro Height map on or off.\n- **Micro Normal:** Turns the custom Micro Normal map on or off.\n- **Curvature Type:** Selects the curvature calculation method: Standard (sharp, can miss broad detail), Sobel (slightly blurrier, based on a Sobel filter on the normal map), or Smooth (multiple blur levels, smoother curves, possible loss of fine detail).\n- **Curvature Intensity:** Sets the strength of curvature in Standard and Sobel modes.\n- **Height Details Intensity:** Sets how much Micro Height detail is applied.\n- **AO Radius:** Sets the range of ambient occlusion in micro details.\n- **AO Depth:** Sets the intensity of ambient occlusion in micro details."}]},"uuid":"d83d85e8-a8d3-4586-811f-e7fd20cf7cb5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:14.764Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"25ae5f68-b9e3-44ae-97e5-cd36af29e0bd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b932fec1-d84d-4092-b134-f9f32ff87ed3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
