{"parentUuid":"c800449f-e582-409c-bb70-c45839e18480","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NbiSW86y9PNkq9uqaKDe9S","type":"tool_result","content":"**Remap node parameters**\n\n**Channel and type controls**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Sets how much of the new value mixes into the original. Higher values use more of the new value. The default of 1 uses only the new value.\n- **Toggle RGB:** Turns the Red, Green, and Blue channels on or off together.\n- **Red, Green, Blue, Alpha:** Choose which channels the node affects.\n\n**Operation menu**\n- **Remap:** Maps values from an input range to an output range.\n- **Threshold:** Maps values based on a cutoff point and a width, with the threshold at the midpoint of the output range.\n\n**Remap settings** (used when Operation is Remap)\n- **Compute Range:** Automatically sets Input Min and Input Max from the minimum and maximum values of the source.\n- **Input Min / Input Max:** Define the input range. Values at or beyond these limits are mapped to the output ends. An eyedropper can sample values from the layer.\n- **Output Min / Output Max:** Define the low and high ends of the output range.\n- **Outside Range menu:**\n  - **Clamp at End:** Holds out-of-range values at the nearest input limit.\n  - **Repeat:** Wraps out-of-range values back through the input range in a loop.\n  - **Extend:** Continues the output range beyond its ends for out-of-range values.\n\n**Threshold settings** (used when Operation is Threshold)\n- **Threshold When menu:** Chooses which values get pushed to the high end of the output: Greater, Greater or Equal, Less, or Less or Equal.\n- **Threshold:** The input value that lands at the midpoint of the output. An eyedropper can sample it.\n- **Width:** Sets how far the input range extends on each side of the threshold. A width of 0 produces a hard cutoff.\n\n**Shaping**\n- **Use Ramp:** Turns the ramp shaping on or off.\n- **Ramp:** A mono ramp that reshapes the remapped output. A connected ramp input overrides it.\n\n**Optional inputs**\n- **source:** The layer, VDB, or attribute to remap.\n- **input_min, input_max, output_min, output_max:** Per-pixel values that override the matching parameters.\n- **ramp:** Per-pixel ramp that overrides the Ramp parameter.\n- **mask:** Per-pixel amount that scales the Mask parameter."}]},"uuid":"d9042e6c-237e-478b-b9e0-dd667d9e34c9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:51.305Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07929af7-b9ea-4138-b82b-4a21a6742cb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c800449f-e582-409c-bb70-c45839e18480","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b7dda66a-c264-47dd-a38d-c8fd41175091","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Wb8BUakUujFcyfedg8AZ2","type":"tool_result","content":"**Distort COP parameters**\n\n- **Signature:** The layer type the source accepts.\n- **Border:** Sampling behavior outside the layer's edges. It automatically uses the layer's border property.\n- **Filter:** The sampling filter for the source layer. Area filters (Box and later) help when distortion shrinks large regions.\n- **Mask:** How much of the new value is mixed with the original. Default is 1, meaning only the new value is used.\n- **Direction Type:** Sets the distortion direction as either an angle or a two-component X/Y vector. Applies only when no `dir` input is connected.\n  - **Angle:** Uses an angle in degrees, where 0 points along positive X.\n  - **Coordinates:** Uses the Direction vector.\n- **Direction:** The X/Y direction in image space, used when Direction Type is Coordinates.\n- **Normalize Direction:** Normalizes the Direction vector when enabled.\n- **Angle:** The distortion angle, used when Direction Type is Angle.\n- **Scale:** Overall distortion strength. Negative values trace backward. With only a `source` UV input, it shifts UVs left and right.\n- **Scale by Timestep:** Multiplies strength by the current timestep, usually 1/FPS.\n- **Streak:** How pixels are combined along the distortion path.\n  - **Off:** No smearing.\n  - **Blur:** Averages samples, smearing along the direction.\n  - **Min:** Keeps the smallest value along the path, useful for eroding shapes.\n  - **Max:** Keeps the largest value along the path, useful for adding edge roughness.\n- **Use Streak Weight Ramp:** Weights path samples when Streak is Blur, Min, or Max.\n- **Streak Weight:** A ramp that scales pixel values along the path, with the left side as the trajectory start. Used only when the weight ramp is enabled.\n- **Pixels per Step:** When off, one step per pixel is used (fast but less accurate). When on, curved paths are traced more accurately, and the value sets tracing quality.\n- **Maximum Steps:** Caps the number of tracing steps when Pixels per Step is on. Raise it if distortion doesn't follow the directions well.\n\n**Distort COP inputs**\n\n- **source:** The original layer to distort.\n- **dir:** Per-pixel distortion direction. Overrides the Direction Type parameters when connected.\n- **scale:** Per-pixel strength multiplier applied on top of the Scale parameter.\n- **mask:** Optional per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Distort COP outputs**\n\n- **distort:** The distorted layer.\n\n**Distort by Slope recipe**\n\nThis recipe creates a Distort COP and a Slope Direction COP, wired into the Distort node's `dir` input. The source image is pushed away from higher values of the controlling Mono layer and toward lower ones, so it follows the slopes downhill."}]},"uuid":"a0c173f3-e9ef-4a47-b8a1-5d2328c607f6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:51.729Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07929af7-b9ea-4138-b82b-4a21a6742cb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b7dda66a-c264-47dd-a38d-c8fd41175091","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ae206d21-21d8-45ea-aa96-36990966f645","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VqRbRMnVXFjLigswLdARS1","type":"tool_result","content":"**Feather COP overview:** The node limits how quickly pixel values can change from one pixel to the next, which can give height fields a beveled look. It can also grow or shrink masks outward or inward, unlike a Blur COP.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the feathered value replaces the original. The default of 1 uses only the new value, and lower values keep more of the original.\n- **Feather from High to Low:** When on, bright pixels stay unchanged and darker neighbors are raised until the slope limit is met. When off, dark pixels stay unchanged and bright pixels are lowered instead.\n- **Include Border:** Lets initial pixel values come from outside the image bounds. This can create an edge mask when borders are constant. Turn it on when making tiling textures.\n- **Feather Direction:** Sets which passes enforce the slope limit:\n  - *Diamond* uses horizontal and vertical passes, producing diamond-shaped islands.\n  - *Square* uses diagonal passes, producing square-shaped islands.\n  - *Octagon* uses horizontal, vertical, and diagonal passes, producing octagon-shaped islands.\n  - *Custom* lets you choose passes with Sweep Directions.\n  - *Circle* applies the limit evenly in all directions, producing circular islands.\n- **Sweep Directions (Custom only):** Selects which of the eight directions (four axis-aligned, four diagonal) apply the feather. Choosing only some directions creates one-sided, ramp-like shapes.\n- **Feather Method:** Chooses how the maximum change is defined. The two options are inverses of each other:\n  - **Distance for Unit Change:** The distance over which a value of 1 can fall to 0.\n  - **Change per Distance:** How much the value can change per unit of distance.\n\n  Each method shows only its own corresponding field.\n\n**Inputs**\n\n- **source:** The original layer to feather.\n- **mask (optional):** A per-pixel amount that is scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Outputs**\n\n- **feather:** The resulting layer with the rate-of-change limit applied."}]},"uuid":"1d2bae71-36d9-45fd-b314-7736638e3279","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:52.448Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07929af7-b9ea-4138-b82b-4a21a6742cb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae206d21-21d8-45ea-aa96-36990966f645","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0f4148ab-fc6e-4111-92a5-8c991a8c9372","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GDg7boVV2e2aQtcLxtQ6cZ","type":"tool_result","content":"## Scatter Shapes COP\n\n**Inputs**\n\n- **size_ref:** Sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **stamps:** Supplies up to 10 stamp layers. If unwired, a default star is used.\n- **density:** Thins stamps through rejection sampling.\n- **jitter:** Offsets each stamp's position randomly.\n- **direction:** Sets stamp rotation direction, such as from Slope Direction.\n- **angle:** Rotates stamps, mapping 0 to 1 onto 0 to 360 degrees.\n- **scale:** Multiplies each stamp's uniform size.\n- **stretch:** Multiplies each stamp's non-uniform (X/Y) size.\n- **color:** Tints stamps.\n- **alpha:** Multiplies stamp opacity.\n- **sort:** Controls depth ordering when stamps overlap.\n- **select:** Chooses stamps in Layer Select mode.\n\n**Outputs**\n\n- **result:** The image with stamps applied.\n- **id:** Per pixel, the ID of the stamp contributing most, or its point number if no ID attribute exists.\n- **uv:** Per pixel, the UV coordinates of the dominant stamp in image space.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Placement and seed*\n\n- **Stamps X / Y / Stamps (Link Stamps):** Number of stamps along each axis, with an option to link X and Y.\n- **Scatter Seed:** Seeds all placement randomness: jitter, density, angle, scale, and stretch.\n- **Grid Type:** Chooses a regular grid or a hexagonal grid with offset rows.\n- **Do Tiled:** Limits grid angle to 90 degrees and snaps offset and scale so stamps don't clip at image edges.\n- **Grid Scale, Offset, Angle:** Control grid size, position, and rotation.\n- **Jitter / Jitter Scale:** Random position offset, with per-axis scaling when per-component controls are on.\n- **Jitter Layer Mask / Strength:** Blend in the jitter input and scale its effect.\n- **Post-Jitter:** Samples other inputs at each stamp's jittered position.\n- **Density:** Removes stamps randomly; 0.8 means each stamp has a 20% chance to disappear.\n\n*Scale*\n\n- **Stamp Scaling:** Keeps stamps at image-relative size or stretches them to fit the tile.\n- **Image Scale / Tile Scale:** Base size in image or tile space.\n- **Scale Mode:** Uniform (no change), Variance (random spread around the base), or Min/Max (random pick within a range).\n- **Scale Variance:** Sets the random spread; a value of 1 gives roughly half to double size.\n- **Min Value / Max Value:** Bounds for random scale multipliers.\n- **Scale Layer Mask:** Blends in the scale input.\n\n*Rotation (Angle)*\n\n- **Angle:** Base rotation in degrees.\n- **Angle Mode:** Uniform, Variance, or Min/Max, as with scale.\n- **Angle Variance:** Random rotation range on each side of the base.\n- **Min Value / Max Value:** Bounds for random rotation.\n- **Round to Multiples:** Snaps angles to fixed increments.\n- **Angle Layer Mask / Direction Layer Mask:** Blend in the angle and direction inputs.\n\n*Stretch*\n\n- **Stretch X / Stretch Y:** Non-uniform scale multipliers.\n- **Stretch Mode:** Uniform, Variance, Min/Max, or Random per Component, which randomizes X and Y separately.\n- **Stretch Variance, Min Value, Max Value:** Control random stretch, as with scale.\n- **Stretch Layer Mask:** Blends in the stretch input.\n\n*Blending*\n\n- **Blend Method:**\n  - *Depth-Sorted Over:* Sorts by depth for accurate overlap, but costs performance and handles transparency poorly.\n  - *Unsorted Depth-Weighted Over:* Approximates depth order without sorting.\n  - *Add, Subtract, Multiply:* Combine overlapping pixel values arithmetically.\n  - *Maximum, Minimum:* Keep the brighter or darker value against the background.\n- **Use Sort Layer:** Multiplies depth values by the sort input.\n- **Treat Mono as Alpha:** Expands mono stamps as GGGG, making them darker, rather than GGG1.\n\n*Color and alpha*\n\n- **Color Seed:** Seeds color and alpha randomness.\n- **Stamp Color:** Uniform, Variance (random hue, saturation, and value offsets), or Random from Ramp.\n- **Hue / Saturation / Value:** Random variance ranges.\n- **Color Layer Mask:** Blends in the color input.\n- **Stamp Alpha:** Uniform, Variance, or Random from Ramp.\n- **Alpha Variance:** Random alpha range.\n- **Alpha Layer Mask:** Blends in the alpha input.\n- **Background Color / Background Alpha:** Initial color and opacity behind the stamps.\n\n*Stamp selection*\n\n- **Mode:** Cycle through stamps, pick them Randomly, use the select input (Layer Select), or Limit Selection to cap the number used.\n- **Select Seed:** Seeds random stamp choice."}]},"uuid":"dd4224f2-9a1b-48a5-81e6-03d27c6f7adb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:59.298Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07929af7-b9ea-4138-b82b-4a21a6742cb1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f4148ab-fc6e-4111-92a5-8c991a8c9372","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
