n be treated as background."}]},"uuid":"ee52493b-a52b-4a52-8cb6-718c01dd4a11","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:11.986Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e815e2d4-36a7-4846-8df3-b0ada0c271ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1315d46d-b89e-43ef-b603-c78e5dac7ecf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"09de4a72-420b-4d34-861c-b671da6d4122","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013d1MqWScA5rsGhKkj5ht36","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer to which the streak blur is applied.\n- **direction:** An optional UV layer that sets the streak direction per pixel, instead of a fixed angle.\n- **scalelength:** An optional layer that multiplies the Length parameter.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel layer that scales the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **blur:** The source layer with the streak blur applied.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the blurred result replaces the original. At 1 (the default), only the new result is used.\n- **Border:** Sets how pixels outside the layer's edges are sampled. It uses the layer's own border setting by default.\n- **Direction Type:** Chooses whether the streak direction is set as an angle or as polar coordinates.\n- **Angle:** Sets the streak direction, where 0 is horizontal and 90 is vertical. Used when Direction Type is Angle.\n- **Direction:** Sets the streak direction as a vector, where (1, 0) points right and (0, 1) points up. Used when Direction Type is Direction.\n- **Normalise Direction:** When on, the direction vector is scaled to unit length. When off, its magnitude multiplies the Length.\n- **Units:** Chooses whether the Length is measured in Image Space or in pixels.\n- **Length:** Sets how long each streak is, in the selected units.\n- **Bias:** Positions each streak relative to the pixel that creates it. 0 centers it, -1 makes it end at that pixel, and 1 makes it start at that pixel.\n- **Mode:** Sets how the pixel values along each streak are combined:\n  - **Blur:** Averages the values, smearing the image along the streak direction.\n  - **Min:** Keeps the darkest value, which is useful for eroding shapes.\n  - **Max:** Keeps the brightest value, which is useful for adding edge roughness.\n- **Use Streak Weight:** When on, the samples along each streak are weighted by the Streak Weight ramp.\n- **Streak Weight:** A ramp that multiplies pixel values along the streak, with the left side at the start of the trajectory. With Blur mode and the default linear ramp, pixels fade toward the start of the streak.\n\nThe page does not list a samples parameter, so sample count is not covered."}]},"uuid":"389bd0b9-100f-485c-af18-5ef98cfc2e77","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:12.203Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e815e2d4-36a7-4846-8df3-b0ada0c271ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"09de4a72-420b-4d34-861c-b671da6d4122","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0a7bf648-ca28-4094-ab4a-7178cec36d60","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018gSMSNELB79PN8Jqj3mnXg","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **id**: An ID layer. Each connected island of IDs becomes a separate UV map.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **uv**: A UV layer with per-pixel coordinates, in either Texture or Image space. Pair it with an Image Sample or Texture Sample.\n- **uvscale**: The scale factor applied when the UV map is resized. UV Sample can use it to adjust filtering to the island size.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Mode**: Chooses what each pixel stores:\n  - UV Map: the pixel's position within its island's UV map.\n  - Center, Minimum, Maximum, Size: the island's bounding-box center, lower-left corner, upper-right corner, or dimensions.\n- **UV Space**: Sets the coordinate system:\n  - Texture: 0 to 1, stretched to fill each island's bounding box. This is the closest option to per-island 0-1 fitting.\n  - Image: -1 to 1, fitted to the bounding box while keeping pixels square.\n- **Auto Scale**: Determines whether the UV map is scaled to fit the island's bounding box.\n- **U Border / V Border**: Decide what happens to coordinates outside the valid range:\n  - Clamp: snaps them to the nearest valid value.\n  - Mirror: reflects them at the boundary.\n  - Wrap: repeats them from the opposite side.\n  - Extend: leaves them unchanged, which is useful for overscan.\n- **U Shift / V Shift**: Offset the coordinates horizontally or vertically before the border rule is applied.\n- **U Cycles / V Cycles**: Multiply the coordinates to scale them. With Wrap, this creates repeating tiles.\n- **Zero Negative IDs**: Sets negative IDs to zero. Otherwise, negative IDs form their own islands, which can be a problem if they mark invalid regions.\n\nThe page does not mention rotation, so I can't confirm whether this node supports it."}]},"uuid":"38928e0b-ebb3-436e-9b19-5db967613b74","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:13.977Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e815e2d4-36a7-4846-8df3-b0ada0c271ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0a7bf648-ca28-4094-ab4a-7178cec36d60","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ff1f6f11-1b9a-43c2-8e48-024cbdea23d9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RLTutgdXmFifvS8kVr1B9s","type":"tool_result","content":"## Outputs\n\n- **tiles:** The tiled layer with the generated rectangles.\n- **id:** An ID layer that stores an ID value for each tile.\n- **uv:** A UV layer that stores UV values.\n\n## Pattern Types\n\n**Brick and bond patterns**\n- **Stack Bond:** Tiles sit directly on top of each other, with all joints aligned.\n- **Header Bond:** Each course is offset so its joints fall halfway over the course below.\n- **Stretcher Bond:** Like Header Bond, but with stretcher courses offset halfway over the joints below.\n- **Flemish Bond:** Stretchers and headers alternate within a single course.\n- **American (Common) Bond:** A running bond with full-header courses at regular intervals.\n- **Monk Bond:** A Flemish variant with two stretchers between each pair of headers.\n- **English Bond:** Stretcher and header courses alternate, with stretcher courses starting from a three-quarter brick.\n- **Double English Bond:** Two stretcher courses alternate with two header courses.\n\n**Geometric and woven patterns**\n- **Windmill:** A square surrounded by four rectangles twice its size, forming a grid-like look.\n- **Cross Hatch:** Lines at angles to each other within each tile.\n- **Basketwave:** Warp and weft groups interlace in a criss-cross pattern.\n- **Hopscotch:** A modular layout of two sizes of square tiles.\n- **Herringbone N:1 and 3:2:** Rectangles arranged in a fish-bone style. N:1 uses an adjustable edge-length ratio, and 3:2 is a fixed ratio.\n- **French (Versailles):** An interlocking modular pattern resembling historic stone floors.\n- **Custom:** You define the layout yourself (see below).\n\n## Core Layout Parameters\n\n- **Pattern Size:** The area the tiles must cover, usually matching the image size.\n- **Clip to Size:** Removes tiles whose centers fall outside the pattern area when Pattern Size is smaller than the image.\n- **Mode (Custom):**\n  - *Seamless:* Uses Divisions so the pattern tiles without seams.\n  - *Tile Count:* Sets tile size from Rows and Columns.\n  - *Tile Size:* Sets tile size directly from Tile Width and Tile Height.\n- **Rows / Columns:** The number of rows and columns.\n- **Iris (Windmill):** Sets the size of the central square relative to the surrounding tiles.\n- **Row / Column Divisions (Cross Hatch):** The number of horizontal and vertical divisions.\n- **Row / Column Thickness (Basketwave):** The thickness of the horizontal and vertical strands.\n- **Draw Square Bonds (Basketwave):** Toggles drawing the squares between the waves.\n- **N (Herringbone N:1):** Controls how thin and elongated the tiles are.\n- **Flip Pattern:** Rotates the pattern 90 degrees.\n\n## Custom Pattern Controls\n\n- **Use Expression:** Switches between nested per-row/column parameters and a text expression.\n- **Pattern Expression:** A text format for defining rows (offset, height) and columns (width), with flags for:\n  - *-s:* Slide offset per row.\n  - *-h:* Column height override.\n  - *-o:* Column vertical offset.\n  - *-v:* Column visibility.\n  - *-r:* Column rotation.\n  - *-r (reflect):* Whether repeated columns start from the first or last entry.\n- **Per-row settings:** Visible, Offset, Reflect Block, Slide Offset, Height.\n- **Per-column settings:** Visible, Width, Height override, Offset, Rotate.\n\n## Position and Offsets\n\n- **Row Offset / Column Offset:** Shifts every tile horizontally or vertically.\n- **Row Slide Offset:** Shifts each row progressively, which creates brick-wall looks.\n- **Row Slide Variation:** Adds randomness to the per-row shift.\n- **Uniform Jitter:** Random positional movement in both directions.\n- **Horizontal / Vertical Jitter:** Random positional movement along one axis.\n\n## Size and Spacing\n\n- **Uniform Scale:** Scales all tiles, with optional per-tile variation.\n- **Horizontal / Vertical Scale:** Scales tiles along each axis, with optional variation.\n- **Inset:** Uniformly expands or adjusts tile edges regardless of tile dimensions. The documentation has no separate grout or spacing control, so Inset is the closest match.\n- **Orient Tiles:** Sets an orientation attribute so horizontal and vertical scaling affect the correct edges.\n\n## Rotation\n\n- **Rotate Pattern:** Rotates the entire pattern in degrees.\n- **Rotate Tile:** Rotates each tile around its center.\n- **Rotate Variation:** Sets the random range around Rotate Tile.\n- **Checkerboard Rotate:** Alternates tiles between 0 and 90 degrees.\n\n## Shape and Rounding\n\n- **Shape Class / Shape:** Chooses the shape placed in each tile (Basic, Marker, or Compound).\n- **Stretch Shape:** Stretches the shape to match the tile proportions.\n- **Round Corners (Rectangle):** Rounds the rectangle's corners. Separate Controls sets each corner individually, from 0 (sharp) to 1 (fully rounded).\n\n## Values and Drawing\n\n- **Tile Value:** The value inside each tile. Set Varying randomizes it per tile.\n- **Background Value:** The value outside the shape.\n- **Draw As:** Filled, Distance (fades from center to edge), Gradient, or Outline.\n- **Anti-Aliasing and Shape Edge Filter:** Smooth jagged edges and control edge filtering.\n- **Fade Distance, Outline Width, Ramp Type, Rotate:** Settings for the Distance, Outline, and Gradient modes.\n\n## Randomization\n\nMost variation settings include a **Variation** amount and a **Seed**. Set Varying on a parameter randomizes it per tile. **Randomize Stamp Order** changes the order in which shapes are stamped.\n\n## Prune Tiles\n\n- **By Tile Order:** Default, Reverse, Random, or Shift (offset the removal order).\n- **Threshold:** The fraction of tiles to remove, from 0 (none) to 1 (all). Negate Selection inverts the choice.\n- **Every Nth Tile / Row / Column:** Removes every Nth item.\n- **Checkerboard:** Removes tiles in an alternating pattern.\n\n## Split Tiles\n\n- **Split Tiles:** Splits tiles according to the rules below.\n- **Iterations:** The maximum number of times a tile can be split again.\n- **Area Threshold:** Tiles smaller than this area are not split.\n- **Split Threshold:** The fraction of tiles to split.\n- **Number of Splits:** How many pieces each split produces, with optional variation.\n- **Jitter Scale:** Moves the split position.\n- **Orient Ratio:** Controls horizontal versus vertical splitting, from all horizontal (0) to all vertical (1)."}]},"uuid":"044b3119-8d88-451b-868d-78ece2dc70e4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:22.268Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e815e2d4-36a7-4846-8df3-b0ada0c271ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ff1f6f11-1b9a-43c2-8e48-024cbdea23d9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
