{"parentUuid":"460f80c1-1936-4ae4-901e-10a492ff7321","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ENECin5ek9tfSk3LSpYpvW","type":"tool_result","content":"The Dilate Erode page doesn't list **operation**, **shape**, **size**, or **border** parameters. Its closest equivalents are below.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source:** The original layer to dilate or erode.\n- **radius:** An optional per-pixel radius that scales the Radius parameter.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel mask that scales the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **dilate:** The dilated or eroded source layer.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the new value mixes with the original. A value of 1 uses only the new value, which is the default.\n- **Units:** Sets how the dilation radius is measured: image space, pixels, or local space.\n- **Radius:** Sets the dilation or erosion amount. Positive values dilate and negative values erode. The Maximum Pixel Radius limit applies.\n- **Soft Edge:** Adds a gradient to the edge, producing a softer transition.\n- **Fill Holes / Remove Specks:** Expands the layer inward, which can fill holes inside a shape.\n- **Maximum Pixel Radius:** Caps the Radius value to limit the performance cost of large radii."}]},"uuid":"50a216d1-3cb1-43de-b7ec-0432009b1990","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:32.387Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"460f80c1-1936-4ae4-901e-10a492ff7321","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-d