{"parentUuid":"656ab7ef-900e-47ad-bf7e-8dbf07913b06","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVZZebEk9ZiWJmhVwUpyVB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **Source:** Takes the image to be processed.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **Edge:** The image with detected edges.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mode:** Chooses whether edges are computed from the luminance of the input or separately for each color channel (RGB and RGBA inputs).\n- **Method:** Selects the edge detection algorithm:\n  - **Sobel:** A 3×3 filter that estimates horizontal and vertical gradients.\n  - **Prewitt:** A 3×3 filter with less contrast than Sobel.\n  - **Laplacian:** A 3×3 filter that measures how quickly the gradient changes, highlighting rapid intensity shifts.\n  - **Simple:** A basic 3×3 detector.\n  - **Thresholded Sobel:** A more advanced method that smooths the image first, then keeps strong edges and removes weak edges that aren't connected to them.\n- **Normalize:** Scales the output so values fall between 0 and 1.\n- **Blur Before:** Blurs the image before detection to reduce noise-driven edges.\n- **High Threshold:** Sets the intensity above which pixels count as strong edges. It only applies to the Thresholded Sobel method.\n\nThe page doesn't list a width parameter, so I can't describe one for this node. The related Edge Detect by Contour, Normal, and Depth nodes cover other edge types."}]},"uuid":"01997ed2-d8a5-43d6-abbb-16261923c12e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:32.833Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"656ab7ef-900e-47ad-bf7e-8dbf07913b06","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0f907a15-6560-4706-ace5-f67bd5278968","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbNohKHXhQLsWyb4mjMjR1","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **Layer:** The original height layer that the node uses to compute ambient occlusion.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **Occlusion:** The resulting ambient occlusion layer.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Height*\n- **Height Scale:** Multiplies the height values before occlusion is computed. Higher values make small height differences show up more strongly.\n\n*Quality*\n- **Space:** Sets the coordinate space used to interpret the steepness of the height data.\n- **View Radius:** Sets how far the node casts rays to check whether a pixel is blocked. Larger radii are more accurate but cook more slowly.\n- **Step Scale:** Sets how far apart the samples are spaced along each ray, measured in buffer space. Larger steps cook faster but can miss thin features. Smaller steps are more precise but slower.\n- **Sample Count:** Sets how many rays are cast per pixel. More rays give more accurate results at the cost of speed.\n- **Sample from Hemisphere:** Changes the angle calculation so it is scaled to a 90-degree range instead of 180 degrees.\n- **Remap Ramp:** Uses a ramp to remap the final occlusion values."}]},"uuid":"51535b6c-f48f-4f74-bda3-560a26695807","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:33.128Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f907a15-6560-4706-ace5-f67bd5278968","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenra