{"parentUuid":"509cfe89-9c00-4fa1-bf1e-ff1b11ae5b5d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HC9mDzZ3uG5KHJqGqGeQJ2","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer or VDB to blur.\n- **size:** A mono or float input that scales the blur amount.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **blur:** The blurred layer or VDB.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Filter:** Sets the blur kernel.\n  - *Gaussian* (default) weights nearby pixels by a Gaussian distribution, so closer pixels contribute more.\n  - *Box* averages all pixels in a square area around each pixel equally.\n- **Read Pixels outside Image:** When enabled, pixels beyond the image edges contribute to the average. The border type determines what values those outside pixels take.\n- **Units:** Sets how the blur radius is measured.\n  - *Image* (default) uses Image Space.\n  - *Pixels* uses a raw pixel count.\n  - *Local* uses Local Space.\n- **Size:** The blur radius, in the units chosen above.\n- **Scale Size:** Scales the blur radius along a specific axis.\n- **Scale by Timestep:** Scales overall blur strength by the current timestep. This is normally 1/FPS, or the current step size in a sub-stepped simulation."}]},"uuid":"dcb26f1f-b640-4738-bae5-ac809831687c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:33.598Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"509cfe89-9c00-4fa1-bf1e-ff1b11ae5b5d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"be99f490-6e50-46fe-b2f8-ffbfe9de082e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFT6FSxgy1hPSuFDEemf54","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **height:** A Mono layer or Float VDB that represents a heightmap.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **slopedir:** A UV layer or Vector VDB holding the slope direction of the height input. Steeper slopes produce larger values.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Space:** Sets how the slope is computed: Image space, Pixel space, or Local (world-space pixel size). This affects magnitude, and can affect direction when pixels are scaled unevenly.\n- **Angle:** Rotates the computed direction by a set amount. A value of 90 makes the directions bypass uphill paths and travel around hills instead.\n- **Scale:** Globally adjusts the vector magnitude, since height values often aren't in real-world units.\n- **Read Pixels outside Image:** Controls whether boundary derivatives read past the image edge (useful for wrapped, seamless textures) or stay within the image range.\n- **Kernel Size:** Widens the distance, in buffer elements, used for the derivative. This smooths out stepping artifacts when height values change slowly.\n\n**Direction encoding**\nThe page doesn't explicitly say whether the direction points uphill or downhill. It describes the output as the \"direction of the slope,\" and the Angle note implies the default points up the slope, so that's likely, but it isn't stated outright. The direction is expressed in the layer's or VDB's own frame: for layers, (1,0) follows increasing pixels along the width, and for VDBs, (0,0,1) follows increasing voxels along the depth."}]},"uuid":"9a24ff2e-55cb-427e-bd38-7a8ec8737d87","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:34.966Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be99f490-6e50-46fe-b2f8-ffbfe9de082e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"01bf202c-6d43-4180-9d0e-7b530ea8ea26","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfByDFmCAsMRC81yGek8fY","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **Source:** Takes either a mono layer, treated as a height field, or an RGB layer, treated as a normal vector field derived from a height field.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **Curvature:** A layer containing the computed curvature values.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Main settings*\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Space:** Sets the space in which curvature is measured.\n- **Method:**\n  - *Finite Difference* compares each pixel with its neighbors using derivatives. It's more stable on smooth inputs.\n  - *Angle Deficit* sums the angles around each pixel as if it were a polygon vertex. It handles complex or uneven surfaces more robustly.\n- **Curvature Type:**\n  - *Gaussian* is positive in both convex and concave areas and negative at saddle points.\n  - *Mean* is positive in convex areas, negative in concave areas, and near zero in flat areas.\n  - *Principal (max)* highlights the strongest outward-curving features.\n  - *Principal (min)* highlights the strongest inward-curving, recessed features.\n- **Output Type:**\n  - *Curvature* outputs the full curvature result.\n  - *Convexity* isolates convex regions.\n  - *Concavity* isolates concave regions.\n\n*Pre-process*\n- **Normal Type:** Must match the Height to Normal COP's setting when the input is a normal field. Options are Signed (geometry-compatible) and Offset (normal-map-compatible).\n- **Scale:** Adjusts the input pixel values.\n- **Read Pixels outside Image:** Includes pixels beyond the image edge when computing boundary curvature. Results are accurate with wrapping borders. With constant borders, disable it for correct edge values.\n- **Kernel Size:** Sets the neighborhood radius used per pixel. Larger values produce smoother curvature.\n\n*Post-process*\n- **Scale:** Adjusts the output values.\n- **Normalize:** Remaps the output to the 0–1 range, which makes curvature structure easier to see. This is useful because small pixel differences can produce extreme values.\n- **Minimum / Maximum:** Clamp the output to a chosen range."}]},"uuid":"59afca31-4341-4729-8994-9514445db5c3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:35.700Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5babb6e9-7c3f-4d41-862a-c909bc4673e3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"01bf202c-6d43-4180-9d0e-7b530ea8ea26","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
