{"parentUuid":"aab3b8be-4387-4f86-b249-3e8ec3ce0375","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xm5JQ8xpfG9seBQfG98ZXq","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** A reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **pos:** An optional UV layer whose values replace the pixel image coordinates when positioning the ramp.\n- **ramp:** An optional per-pixel amount that overrides the Ramp parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **ramp:** The generated ramp.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Ramp shape (Type):*\n- **Horizontal / Vertical:** A linear ramp running across the image horizontally or vertically.\n- **Radial:** A ramp whose color bands spread outward from a center point like sunbeams.\n- **Concentric:** A ramp whose bands form rings around a center point, like ripples.\n\n*Direction and placement:*\n- **Rotation:** Rotates a linear ramp, in degrees (Horizontal/Vertical only).\n- **Start Position:** The origin of a linear ramp, or the center of a radial/concentric ramp.\n- **End Position:** The end of a linear ramp. For Radial, it sets where the crossover occurs. For Concentric, it sets the ring radius.\n- **Center:** The center point for Radial or Concentric ramps. You can pick it directly in the image.\n- **Size Method:** Either fits the ramp to the display window or uses a two-point definition.\n\n*Repetition:*\n- **Number of Cycles:** How many times the pattern repeats.\n- **Phase:** Offsets where the pattern starts. Zero starts it at the first point.\n- **Outside Range:** Controls what happens beyond the start and end points. Clamp holds the end values, Repeat restarts the pattern, and Mirror reverses it on each repeat.\n\n*Ramp editor:*\n- **Ramp:** The gradient or curve itself. RGB ramps vary color, and mono ramps vary a single value.\n- **Point No., Position, Color, Value:** Select a keyframe and adjust its location and its color or value.\n- **Interpolation (per point):** Controls how values blend from one point to the next. The page recommends using the global interpolation setting from the ramp parameter documentation instead.\n\n**Not covered:** The page does not describe a \"bias\" parameter, so I can't say what it does. \"Direction\" and \"repeat mode\" aren't labeled as such; they correspond to Rotation/Start/End Position and Outside Range."}]},"uuid":"73378170-99ff-48f7-a717-5bef417cd9c5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:04.064Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aab3b8be-4387-4f86-b249-3e8ec3ce0375","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8c77729d-b57d-4a3a-92e6-adc0f0d3fe19","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JRhPraxcGXbi2XCP87YUik","type":"tool_result","content":"## Inputs\n\n- **source:** The Mono, UV, RGB, or RGBA layer to extend outward.\n- **fillarea:** A layer that marks which areas are interior. Its values determine where the edge of the filled region sits.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel amount that controls how strongly the effect applies. The page says it's scaled by a **Mask** parameter, but that parameter isn't described in the parameter list.\n\n## Output\n\n- **extrapolation:** The source extended into the exterior area.\n\n## Parameters\n\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source input accepts.\n- **Exterior:** Controls what happens to exterior pixels that weren't filled by copying.\n  - *Unchanged* leaves them as they are.\n  - *Black* sets them to black.\n  - *Diffuse Fill* smoothly interpolates values across them.\n- **Inner Side:** Chooses which side of the fillarea threshold counts as the interior.\n  - *Below Threshold* treats darker values as inside, which fills white regions of the fillarea.\n  - *Above Threshold* treats brighter values as inside, which fills black regions.\n- **Threshold:** The value that separates interior from exterior in fillarea. You can use the eyedropper to pick it from the layer.\n- **Edge Padding:** How far outward, in image coordinates, pixel values are copied directly. This creates a bleed border around the edge.\n- **Edge Offset:** How far back to look for clean source values. This avoids copying colors that already include exterior contamination from the edge padding.\n- **Sample Only Present:** Limits sampling to pixels inside the source area (those passing the threshold). This stops black from uninitialized areas leaking in. It's useful when fillarea data is unreliable, and you can usually set Edge Offset to 0 with it on. Turn it off if fillarea holds valid data and you want a smooth edge value.\n- **Diffuse Iterations:** In Diffuse Fill mode, sets how many relaxation passes smooth the extrapolated values."}]},"uuid":"dd616247-cfd5-400c-94a0-b3958b5a099f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:04.594Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c77729d-b57d-4a3a-92e6-adc0f0d3fe19","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"42093692-7cfa-488e-9891-b5be8ac0c8d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DnmBqg8a8KJskiLdAxNFJW","type":"tool_result","content":"**Input**\n- **sdf:** The 2D signed distance field mono layer to convert.\n\n**Output**\n- **mono:** The resulting grayscale mono image layer.\n\n**Parameters**\n\nThe page has no parameter named \"mode,\" and \"falloff\" appears only under shadowing. The closest matches are listed below.\n\n- **Mode (value remapping):** The Background Value and Shape Value menus switch between a fixed constant and remapping by distance (Iso Distance).\n- **Distance:** Iso Range sets how far the background remapping extends. Iso Distance sets how far the shape remapping extends from the shape's border. Iso Offset moves the edge itself, enlarging or shrinking the shape.\n- **Ramp:** Remap Ramp, for both background and shape, controls how distance values translate into output values across the distance span. Number of Cycles repeats that pattern within the range.\n- **Falloff:** Shadow Falloff sets how far the shadow spreads. Shadow Density controls how visible it is, and Shadow Value sets its color.\n- **Inside/outside:** Invert swaps the inside and outside of the shape. Outline Alignment places the outline inside the border, outside it, or centered on it.\n- **Toggles:** Draw Shape, Draw Outline, and Draw Shadowing turn each visual element on or off.\n- **Other:** Outline Value and Outline Width style the outline. Onion Skin hollows the shape into a thin band. Smooth blurs edges, and Anti-Aliasing reduces jagged edges."}]},"uuid":"e1358109-5c72-4ffd-b4c8-d34a49f42779","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:05.200Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"42093692-7cfa-488e-9891-b5be8ac0c8d6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"471a6c9b-b095-4c02-929a-b307562b1f9e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L66nVkgPhxQr1qVgi7KGrz","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** Sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **pos:** Optional UV layer that replaces the pixel's image coordinates as the noise source.\n- **time:** Supplies a per-pixel time value.\n- **octaves:** Optional multiplier for the Max Octaves parameter.\n- **roughness:** Optional multiplier for the Roughness parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **noise:** The computed fractal noise.\n\n**Range parameters**\n- **Amplitude:** Multiplies the noise before the Center offset is applied.\n- **Center:** Shifts the output range up or down.\n- **Noise Contrast:** Increases or decreases contrast inside the noise function, before Amplitude and Center.\n\n**Pattern parameters**\n- **Noise Type:** Selects the base noise function:\n  - *Torus:* 4D simplex noise on a flat torus, periodic by construction.\n  - *Perlin:* Grid-based noise with a natural look.\n  - *Worley F1:* Cell-like pattern based on distance to the nearest point.\n  - *Worley F2-F1:* Cell-border pattern based on the gap between the two nearest points.\n  - *White (Random):* Random constant value per element.\n  - *Alligator:* Bumpy, reptile-skin-like pattern.\n  - *Sparse Convolution:* Smooth value noise, softer than Perlin.\n- **Per Component:** Generates separate noise for each channel instead of grayscale.\n- **Metric (Worley types only):** Changes how distance is measured: Euclidean (circular cells), Manhattan (diamond cells), or Chebyshev (square cells).\n- **Jitter (Worley types only):** Randomly displaces each Worley point. Values above 1 can cause artifacts.\n- **Element Size:** Sets the size of the basic noise feature in image coordinates.\n- **Element Scale:** With Per-Component Controls on, scales the element size separately on each axis.\n- **Offset:** Moves the whole noise pattern in image coordinates.\n- **Tile Size:** Sets the repeat period of the noise. Matching the image aspect ratio is recommended for non-square images. When tiling is enforced, Element Size and Lacunarity are rounded or clamped.\n\n**3D Noise parameters**\n- **3D Noise (toggle):** Adds a third dimension to the noise, with the image supplying the first two.\n- **Animate:** Automatically adds time as the third coordinate.\n- **Pulse Length:** Sets how long each pulse lasts. Shorter values make the pattern change faster.\n- **Time Offset:** Adds a time offset to the start frame.\n- **Time Scale:** Multiplies the start frame time to control change speed.\n- **Loop Length (sec):** Makes the animation repeat after a set time, for seamless loops.\n\n**Fractal parameters**\n- **Fractal Type:** Controls how extra noise layers are added:\n  - *None:* No extra layers.\n  - *Sharp:* Sharp, detailed layers.\n  - *Dampened:* Softer, reduced-detail layers.\n  - *Terrain:* Smooth layers resembling landscapes.\n  - *Hybrid Terrain:* Smooth layers with sharpened peaks, like rocky terrain.\n- **Max Octaves:** Number of noise layers added together.\n- **Lacunarity:** Frequency scale applied at each layer. Rounded to an integer for tileable noise.\n- **Octave Offset:** Shifts the noise position for each layer.\n- **Roughness:** Controls how strongly each successive layer contributes.\n\n**Turbulence:** The page doesn't describe a turbulence parameter, so I can't say what it does.\n\n**Post Processing** (applied in the order listed)\n- **Fold:** Converts negative values to their positive equivalents.\n- **Complement:** Inverts values in the 0 to 1 range.\n- **Bias:** Pushes mid-grey values toward 0 or 1.\n- **Gain:** Pushes mid-grey values together and spreads out the darks and lights.\n- **Gamma:** Brightens or darkens the overall result.\n- **Contrast:** Expands or compresses the tonal range around mid-grey.\n- **Clamp Minimum / Clamp Maximum:** Limits values below or above set thresholds."}]},"uuid":"07c5c43c-88d0-45a3-9224-f5399bdaefd2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:06.721Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"471a6c9b-b095-4c02-929a-b307562b1f9e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bc139fc5-cb72-47d4-b31a-24290c027e59","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wnjcha91w2Ea7XbUuvWaA7","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **bg (background):** The layer, VDB, or attribute that the blend is composited onto.\n- **fg (foreground):** The top or source layer, VDB, or attribute blended into the background.\n- **mask (optional):** A per-pixel mask whose values are scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **blend:** The fg and bg results combined.\n\n**Blend modes**\n- **Blend:** Replaces the background with the foreground (default).\n- **Over:** Places the foreground on top of the background.\n- **Under:** Places the foreground beneath the background's alpha.\n- **Add:** Adds the foreground to the background.\n- **Subtract:** Subtracts the foreground from the background.\n- **Multiply:** Multiplies the background by the foreground.\n- **Divide:** Divides the background by the foreground.\n- **Screen:** A saturating add, similar to layering photographs.\n- **Hypot:** Takes the length of the vector formed by matching fg and bg channels.\n- **Difference:** Takes the absolute difference between fg and bg.\n- **Exclusion:** A lower-contrast version of Difference. A value of 1 inverts the source, and 0 leaves it unchanged.\n- **Sharpen:** Increases background contrast, using the foreground as the midpoint.\n- **Maximum / Minimum:** Keeps the larger or smaller of the two values, per component unless Compare Lengths is on. (The page uses these names, not \"Max\" and \"Min.\")\n- **Overlay:** Multiplies where the background is below 0.5 and screens where it is above.\n- **SoftLight:** Applies gentle contrast to the background based on the foreground, which is clamped to 0–1.\n- **HardLight:** Multiplies or screens depending on whether the foreground is below or above 0.5.\n- **Dodge:** Lightens the background according to the foreground value.\n- **Burn:** Darkens the background according to the foreground value.\n- **Hue, Saturation, Luminosity, Color:** Replace the matching property of the background (hue, saturation, luminosity, or full color) with the foreground's.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Space:** Sets how foreground and background pixels are matched: Image (2D canvas, ignoring 3D transforms), Texture (stretches data windows to overlap), Pixel (matches pixel size with offsets), or World (projects through the background's camera).\n- **Border:** Controls sampling outside the input's boundaries. Auto uses the layer's border property.\n- **Filter:** Sets the sampling method.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the blended result is mixed in. The default of 1 uses only the new value. This is the closest equivalent to an opacity control, since the page has no separate opacity parameter.\n- **Toggle RGB and Red / Green / Blue / Alpha:** Choose which channels the node affects.\n- **Alpha Compositing:** For RGBA layers, applies alpha compositing rules. Mono layers are treated as fully opaque. When off, each channel, including alpha, is processed independently.\n- **Swap FG and BG:** Swaps the inputs, which matters for non-commutative modes like Subtract or Divide.\n- **Compare Lengths:** For Maximum and Minimum, chooses based on vector magnitude rather than per component.\n- **Clip by Data Window:** Limits the result to the foreground's data window with a hard edge, so it doesn't extend into the background.\n- **Crop to Content:** Crops the output to the combined area of the transformed foreground data window and the background data window."}]},"uuid":"52db165d-c3a1-4b67-9ae6-fc0296e71fa3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:08.280Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc139fc5-cb72-47d4-b31a-24290c027e59","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f36f3505-de20-44b7-9c6b-6191e0fbda72","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TsYPETxeqtuAx3UkDHvpTL","type":"tool_result","content":"## SDF Shape Node\n\n**Input**\n- **size_ref:** A reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata.\n\n**Output**\n- **sdf:** A Mono SDF layer. Values are negative inside the shape and positive outside it.\n\n**Shape Selection**\n- **Shape Class:** Chooses the group (Basic, Marker, or Compound), which determines the shape list shown.\n\n**Basic Shapes**\n- **Circle:** Radius sets its size. Arc makes an open pie-slice when below 1. Thickness hollows it into a ring when below 1. Round Ends rounds the ring's ends when Arc and Thickness are both on. Quadratic Circle changes it into a quadratic circle.\n- **Diamond:** Size sets its horizontal and vertical extent.\n- **Line:** Length sets its horizontal length. Use Points lets you set start and end positions. Add Thickness sets separate start and end thicknesses, or Bulge controls thickness at the center.\n- **Rectangle:** Size sets its dimensions. Round Corners sets corner roundness, from sharp at 0 to fully rounded at 1. Separate Controls sets each corner (top left, top right, bottom left, bottom right) individually.\n- **Polygon:** Radius sets its size. Number of Sides sets how many sides it has; more sides look more circular.\n- **Spiral:** Radius sets its size. Arc Bend sets how much each segment curves toward the center. Number of Arcs sets how many segments it has.\n- **Squircle:** Radius sets its size. Blend shapes it between a diamond (1), a circle (2), and a square (higher values).\n- **Star:** Radius sets its size. Number of Sides sets the point count. Angle Factor sets how deep the points are; 2 gives a regular polygon.\n- **Trapezoid:** Height sets its vertical size. Bottom Length and Top Length set its widths.\n- **Triangle:** Width and Height set its size. Use Points lets you place the three corners (Point 0, 1, and 2) directly.\n- **Wave:** Arc sets the distortion amount. Element Size sets the pattern scale.\n\n**Marker Shapes**\n- **Size:** Sets the marker's radius.\n\n**Compound Shapes**\n- **Arch:** Width sets its breadth and Height sets its height; 0 gives a half-circle.\n- **Arrow:** Length sets total length. Use Points lets you set start and end positions. Shaft Thickness and Head Thickness set the widths. Head Ratio sets the head size relative to the shaft.\n- **Cross:** Cross Size sets overall size. Cross Inset trims the square's corners. Cross Bevel rounds the inner corners.\n- **Egg:** Radius sets its size. Roundness sets how rounded the top is, from pointed to circular.\n- **Fishscale:** Thickness sets its thickness, useful for tile patterns.\n- **Horseshoe:** Size sets overall size. Separation sets the gap; 0 closes it into a circle. Length sets the ends' extent. Thickness sets its thickness.\n- **Moon:** Outer Radius sets the outer body. Inner Radius sets the cut-out. Inner Offset sets where the cut-out sits.\n- **Octagon-Dot:** Thickness sets its thickness, useful for tile patterns.\n- **Cross-style shape:** Size sets overall size, where 0 gives a circle. Thickness sets the cross's thickness.\n- **Vesica:** Radius sets its size. Roundness sets its vertical thickness.\n\n**Transform**\n- **Translate:** Moves the shape horizontally and vertically. Clicking the position sample button and then a spot in the image sets it.\n- **Rotate:** Rotates the shape.\n- **Shear:** Skews the shape.\n- **Uniform Scale:** Scales the shape evenly in all directions."}]},"uuid":"78ae8a0a-ac5c-439a-8f59-80f8d059cacc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:09.957Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a4030b4-85d0-4ec8-bfd1-83829f4958f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"}