{"parentUuid":"fc8dfa09-f7d5-40ab-b754-fa87997d3c44","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZt6kRFF3PM1My56RYkPzZ","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer whose region will be smoothly filled.\n- **fillarea:** A Mono layer that marks the area to fill.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel mask that scales how much the result is applied, combined with the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **smoothfill:** The source layer with the marked region filled in smoothly.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source input accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the filled result replaces the original. At 1, only the new values are used; lower values keep more of the original.\n- **Fill:** Chooses whether to fill values below or above the threshold in the fillarea layer.\n- **Threshold:** The fillarea value where filling begins. You can pick it directly from the layer with the dropper.\n- **Iterations:** How many relaxation passes run to smooth the filled region. More passes give a smoother result, and the solver may need many to converge.\n- **Acceleration:** Speeds convergence using successive over-relaxation. A value of 1 keeps the smoothing stable, and values up to about 1.98 converge faster."}]},"uuid":"c52fe394-a8bf-4a27-af8a-d491d48d3886","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:43.343Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fc8dfa09-f7d5-40ab-b754-fa87997d3c44","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0d0565ad-f0d2-415c-94b9-5000ed35f29e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FgDEtZ1JdehGm5T72efgGq","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **sdf**: The signed distance field layer that defines the boundary of the region to inflate.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **height**: The inflated height layer.\n- **sdf**: A signed distance field rebuilt from the inflated region.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Core inflation*\n- **Height Scale**: Multiplies the base inflation. Positive values raise and fill the shape; negative values flip the height direction.\n- **Pre Scale**: Sets the base inflation strength before the height is solved. Higher values make the inflated region stronger.\n- **Noise Scale**: Controls how much the Wrinkles and Mounds noise is added to the region.\n\n*Wrinkles (fine detail)*\n- **Wrinkles** (toggle): Adds fine phasor-noise creases.\n- **Size**: Higher values give fewer, wider wrinkles; lower values give more, tighter ones.\n- **Boundary Blend**: Makes the wrinkle pattern respond more strongly near the boundary.\n- **Seed**: Changes the random wrinkle pattern.\n\n*Mounds (broader detail)*\n- **Mounds** (toggle): Adds larger fractal-noise bumps.\n- **Size**: Larger values create bigger mounds.\n- **Max Octaves**: Number of noise layers combined.\n- **Lacunarity**: How much the frequency changes between layers.\n- **Roughness**: How much each successive layer's amplitude changes.\n\n*Blur (smoothing)*\n- **Scale**: Blurs and flattens the noise, blending it with the original shape. A value of 0 leaves the noise unsmoothed. This is applied after Wrinkles and Mounds.\n- **Mask from Boundary**: Offsets the SDF boundary used to build the blur mask.\n- **Mask Smoothing**: Softens the edge of the blur mask.\n\n*Solver*\n- **Iterations**: Number of Poisson solve passes. More iterations give a more converged height but take longer. Increase this if the result has flat areas.\n\n**Notes**\nThe page does not list a \"profile\" parameter, so I haven't included one. The page also warns that inflating right at the image edge can create artifacts, so the SDF should sit inside the image boundary.\n\n**Good for**\nPillow- or balloon-like shapes built from a 2D SDF, such as puffy text, quilted fabric, cobblestones, and texture displacement. Wrinkles and Mounds add organic surface variation, and Blur softens it into a base terrain or cushion shape."}]},"uuid":"228d44ed-f99d-4b18-928c-eb45cd7cff3f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:44.564Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d0565ad-f0d2-415c-94b9-5000ed35f29e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"dc1ebb3f-fa1e-42b4-b9b1-e59b2cf86b06","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LwLyz3EuXSxyf6kVwVTgzZ","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source**: The mono layer to be segmented.\n\n**Output**\n- **id**: An ID layer that stores the generated segment numbers. Pixels in the same value band get the same ID, even if they aren't connected.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Band definition*\n- **Method**: Chooses how the value bands are defined, either by a fixed width with an offset or by a set number of segments.\n- **Width**(Width and Offset method): The largest value difference allowed for two pixels to share a segment.\n- **Offset** (Width and Offset method): Where the first band starts, measured from zero.\n- **Segments** (Number of Segments method): How many bands fit between the Minimum and Maximum Values.\n- **Segment Location**: Controls how a value becomes an integer segment. *Starts at Value* rounds down, so each band begins at its value. *Centered at Value* rounds to the nearest integer, so each band is centered on its value.\n\n*Value range*\n- **Minimum Value**: The lowest value to segment. Values below it follow the Values Below rule. With the Number of Segments method, it marks the start of the interval. A dropper can sample it from the layer.\n- **Maximum Value**: The highest value to segment. Values above it follow the Values Above rule. With the Number of Segments method, it marks the end of the interval. A dropper can sample it from the layer.\n\n*Out-of-range handling*\n- **Values Below** and **Values Above** each offer four options:\n  - **Extend**: Converts values without clamping.\n  - **Invalid (-1)**: Outputs -1 as the segment ID.\n  - **Clamp**: Limits values to the minimum or maximum.\n  - **Wrap**: Repeats the segment values cyclically.\n\nThe page has no \"threshold counts\" parameter. The closest equivalents are **Segments** and **Width**, which control how many bands are created and how wide each one is."}]},"uuid":"d2d638bb-3607-49ce-9d73-579b107c6b0d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:45.464Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc1ebb3f-fa1e-42b4-b9b1-e59b2cf86b06","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a20578bc-4027-4001-9a47-3a9a7fb29861","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GVmpNWgEf7yHgw152eUy5H","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **id:** The original ID layer that gets converted into the mask.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel mask whose values are scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **mask:** The resulting mask layer.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*General*\n- **ID Pattern:** A group expression that selects which IDs to include. If left blank, all IDs are included. You can also click the dropper and pick IDs directly in the viewport.\n- **Invert Mask:** Flips the generated mask so selected and unselected areas swap.\n\n*Keep by Range*\n- **Keep by Range:** Turns range-based filtering on or off.\n- **Range Type:** Chooses how the range is defined:\n  - *Start and End* (default) sets the first and last IDs, both inclusive.\n  - *Start and Length* sets a first ID and a count of IDs to include.\n- **Start ID / End ID (Start and End mode):** The first and last IDs in the range. Each can be disabled to remove that bound. Defaults are 0 and 100.\n- **Range Offset:** A value added to both the Start and End IDs. Default is 0.\n- **Start ID (Start and Length mode):** The first ID in the range. Default is 0.\n- **Length:** How many consecutive IDs to include. Default is 5.\n- **Range Filter** (a sub-filter that thins out the range in a repeating pattern):\n  - **Select / of:** How many IDs to keep out of each block. For example, 1 of 2 keeps every other ID. Defaults are 1 and 2.\n  - **Offset:** Shifts where the repeating pattern starts, relative to the start of the range. Default is 0.\n\n*Keep by Chance*\n- **Keep by Chance:** Turns random filtering on or off.\n- **Probability:** The approximate fraction of IDs to keep. Default is 0.5 (about 50%).\n- **Seed:** Sets the random pattern. Changing it produces a different selection. Default is 30.\n\n*Keep within Mask*\n- **Keep within Mask:** When a mask input is connected, limits the kept IDs to areas of that mask.\n- **Threshold:** Mask pixels brighter than this value count as inside the mask. Default is 0.5."}]},"uuid":"be8d023a-db55-4336-bc30-02572c9b66bb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:45.470Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a20578bc-4027-4001-9a47-3a9a7fb29861","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d6b1ab96-2097-4b52-8503-aa54bb32dfa3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kuh3cBNwWaAwNTYis6vV1d","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n\n- **size_ref:** A reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **pos:** An optional UV layer that replaces the pixel's image coordinates as the noise source.\n\n**Outputs**\n\n- **dist1:** Mono layer of the distance to the nearest point (commonly called F1).\n- **dist2:** Mono layer of the distance to the second-nearest point (F2). Subtracting dist1 from dist2 gives a common border estimate.\n- **border:** SDF Mono layer with the exact distance to the border between the two closest points, useful for even-width cell edges.\n- **center:** UV layer holding the image coordinates of the closest grid point, which a UV Sample COP can use for mosaic effects.\n- **id:** ID layer holding a hash of the closest grid point. These values can be negative.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Type Info:** Sets the data type of the resulting layer.\n- **Element Size:** Sets the size of each noise cell in image coordinates. Enabling Per-Component Controls exposes Element Scale.\n- **Element Scale:** Scales cell size per axis for stretched, anisotropic noise (only with Per-Component Controls on).\n- **Jitter:** Randomly moves each grid point before distances are measured. Values above 1 can create artifacts because points move beyond the search radius. Per-Component Controls exposes Jitter Scale.\n- **Jitter Scale:** Applies jitter separately along each axis.\n- **Lattice Type:** Chooses a square grid (default) or a simplex-style grid that produces hexagonal cells.\n- **Metric:** Sets how distance is measured.\n  - *Euclidean* gives round cells.\n  - *Manhattan* gives diamond cells.\n  - *Chebyshev* gives square cells.\n- **Round Border:** Smooths the exact border calculation to round the edges between cells. It only appears when Metric is Euclidean.\n- **Offset:** Shifts the whole noise pattern in image coordinates.\n- **Tile Size:** Sets the repeat period of the noise in image coordinates. For non-square images, match the aspect ratio. When the tiling option is on, parameters such as Element Size are rounded or clamped so the noise stays seamless.\n\n**Post Processing** (applied in the order listed)\n\n- **Complement:** Inverts values in the 0–1 range (x becomes 1 − x).\n- **Bias:** Pushes mid-gray values toward 0 or 1.\n- **Gain:** Pushes mid-gray values together while spreading values near 0 and 1 apart.\n- **Gamma:** Adjusts overall brightness. Higher values darken the noise; lower values brighten it.\n- **Contrast:** Expands or compresses the tonal range around mid-gray. This is separate from any Noise Contrast setting in other nodes.\n- **Clamp Minimum:** Raises values below a threshold.\n- **Clamp Maximum:** Lowers values above a threshold."}]},"uuid":"1d0d95e7-934f-4421-9108-8ad4eb38b9f3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:47.515Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6b1ab96-2097-4b52-8503-aa54bb32dfa3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"590910f1-0036-4c3c-a1e3-d66c35e011ee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsRcz9udBZmhLq8UK9Uon4","type":"tool_result","content":"## Scatter on Curves: Inputs, Outputs, and Parameters\n\n**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** Sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **curve (required):** The path that stamps are scattered along.\n- **density:** Rejects some stamps during placement, which thins out the scatter.\n- **direction:** Sets stamp angle from a direction field, such as one from Slope Direction.\n- **angle:** Rotates stamps based on a grayscale value.\n- **scale:** Multiplies the uniform size of stamps.\n- **stretch:** Multiplies the non-uniform (X/Y) size of stamps.\n- **color:** Tints stamps.\n- **alpha:** Controls stamp opacity.\n- **sort:** Controls which stamps draw in front when depth sorting.\n- **select:** Picks which stamp to use when Selection Mode is Layer Select.\n- **stamps:** Up to 8 stamp images. If unconnected, a star pattern is used.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **result:** The final image with stamps applied.\n- **id:** Identifies the stamp that contributed most to each pixel (or its point number).\n- **uv:** The UV coordinates, in image space, of the dominant stamp at each pixel.\n\n**Scattering (spacing and placement)**\n- **Distribution:** Chooses how stamps are spaced. *Distance* spaces them evenly, *Scatter* places them randomly (by density or count), and *By Count* places a fixed number.\n- **Segment Length / Maximum Segments:** For Distance mode, sets the maximum gap between stamps and the total number of segments.\n- **Treat Input Curve As:** Controls curve smoothing: straight lines, subdivision smoothing (doesn't hit original points), or interpolating smoothing (hits points but can overshoot).\n- **Density Layer Mask / Density Scale:** Controls how much the density input affects placement and how many points appear in Scatter mode.\n- **Max Count:** Sets the number of points in Scatter or By Count mode.\n- **Relaxation:** Pushes points apart to reduce clumping. More iterations spread them further.\n- **Scatter Seed:** Seeds the randomness for placement, jitter, density, angle, scale, and stretch.\n\n**Curve**\n- **Cut Curves by Relative Arc Length:** Measures position by actual distance along the curve rather than the curve's internal parameter.\n- **Start Point / End Point:** Set where the curve begins and ends in image space.\n- **Smoothing:** Softens the curve.\n\n**Mirror and Offset**\n- **Mirror Stamps:** Creates a reflected copy across the curve's tangent. Modes are Treat Independently (randomize each side separately) or copy values from the original or mirrored side.\n- **From Curve / Mirrored From Curve:** Offsets stamps (and mirrored stamps) perpendicular to the curve.\n- **Jitter:** Adds random position offsets.\n- **Offset along Curve:** Shifts placement forward or backward along the curve.\n\n**Angle (rotation)**\n- **Angle Layer Mask / Direction Layer Mask:** Blend in the angle and direction inputs.\n- **Angles Relative to Curve Direction:** Measures rotation relative to the curve's direction.\n- **Angle:** Base rotation in degrees. Post-processing options are Uniform, Variance (random spread, set by Angle Variance), or Min/Max (random pick between two limits).\n- **Increment per Stamp:** Adds rotation for each successive stamp, so the pattern can spiral or fully turn.\n- **Round to Multiples:** Snaps angles to fixed steps.\n\n**Scale**\n- **Scale Layer Mask:** Blends in the scale input.\n- **Scale:** Base size, with the same Uniform, Variance, or Min/Max modes.\n- **Apply Scale along Curve:** Uses a ramp to vary size along the curve.\n\n**Stretch**\n- **Stretch Layer Mask:** Blends in the stretch input.\n- **Stretch Mode:** Uniform, Variance, or Min/Max for X and Y.\n- **Stretch X / Stretch Y:** Base size along each axis.\n- **Stretch along Curve, Stretch X/Y along Curve:** Use ramps to vary X and Y size along the curve.\n\n**Blend and Color**\n- **Blend Method:** Controls how overlapping stamps combine. Options include depth-sorted over (accurate but slower), unsorted depth-weighted over (approximates sorting), Add, Subtract, Multiply, Maximum, and Minimum.\n- **Use Sort Layer / Apply Sort along Curve:** Control stacking order with the sort input or a ramp.\n- **Color Layer Mask / Stamp Color:** Blend in the color input and set tint. Modes are Uniform, Variance (random hue, saturation, and value shifts), Random from Ramp, or Ramp along Curve.\n- **Alpha Layer Mask / Stamp Alpha:** Control stamp opacity with the same modes, plus Alpha Variance.\n- **Color Seed:** Seeds the color and alpha randomness.\n- **Background Color / Background Alpha:** Set the base color and transparency behind the stamps.\n\n**Stamp Selection**\n- **Selection Mode:** Cycle through stamps in order, pick randomly (using Select Seed), use the select input (Layer Select), or cap the count with Limit Selection.\n\n**Options**\n- **Filter:** Sets the sampling method for the image.\n- **Wrap Mode:** Auto, Off, or On. Wrapping can make the main tile repeat seamlessly.\n- **Tile Size:** The region used for wrapping."}]},"uuid":"b5e39a4a-1621-401d-9feb-cec303b34572","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:48.963Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"590910f1-0036-4c3c-a1e3-d66c35e011ee","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f986acb0-bb98-4af2-a9a4-3b73151c20cd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011E9prdBjp1ietdfu1a2nKJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The **Crystal Noise** COP generates sharp, angular Worley-style noise. It combines two randomly offset Worley noises to create the angular edges. For world-space positions, use Crystal Noise 3D instead.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** Sets the output image size and metadata.\n- **pos:** Optional UV layer that replaces pixel image coordinates as the noise source.\n- **time:** Optional layer that supplies a time value per pixel.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **result:** The computed noise. The page lists no other outputs, such as ID or border.\n\n**Angularity controls**\n- **Primary Metric:** Sets how distance is measured. Euclidean gives jagged shapes, Manhattan gives diamond-like shapes, and Chebyshev gives square-like shapes.\n- **Secondary:** When enabled, the primary settings drive the first noise and the secondary settings drive the second.\n- **Flatten Faces:** Smooths the cell faces so they stay flat and the internal noises don't add bumps.\n\n**Pattern parameters**\n- **Jitter:** Randomly displaces each grid point before distances are measured, making cells more irregular. Values above 1 can cause artifacts.\n- **Element Size:** Sets the basic cell size in image coordinates. Per-Component Controls unlock Element Scale for per-axis stretching.\n- **Secondary Metric, Jitter, Element Size, and Element Scale:** Equivalent controls for the second Worley noise.\n- **Offset:** Shifts the whole noise pattern in image coordinates.\n- **Tile Size:** Sets the repeat period so the noise tiles seamlessly. Values may be rounded or clamped to keep tiling valid.\n\n**Range parameters**\n- **Noise Contrast:** Increases extremity in the noise before Amplitude and Center are applied.\n- **Amplitude:** Multiplies the noise values before Center.\n- **Center:** Offsets the output range.\n\n**3D/animation parameters**\n- **Animate:** Adds time as a third noise dimension.\n- **Pulse Length:** Sets how long each appearance lasts. Shorter pulses switch faster.\n- **Time Scale:** Multiplies frame time to change how quickly the pattern changes.\n- **Time Offset:** Adds a time offset to the start frame.\n- **Loop Length:** Makes the animation repeat after a set time so it loops seamlessly.\n\n**Post-processing (applied in listed order)**\n- **Fold:** Takes the absolute value of negative values.\n- **Complement:** Inverts values (1 − x), which works for the 0 to 1 range.\n- **Bias:** Pushes mid-gray values toward 0 or 1.\n- **Gain:** Pushes mid-gray values together and spreads values near 0 and 1 apart.\n- **Gamma:** Brightens or darkens the overall result.\n- **Contrast:** Expands or compresses the tonal range around mid-gray.\n- **Clamp Minimum / Clamp Maximum:** Limit values below or above a threshold."}]},"uuid":"764e5c7a-2b1e-484f-a4e3-8cda64f4e6fb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:49.590Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f986acb0-bb98-4af2-a9a4-3b73151c20cd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"92d8503f-a090-4fc7-bffa-258060b2892f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eKpCNrV9G1fiDTho9QYk3","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs** (all optional except the size reference)\n- **size_ref**: A representative layer that sets the output size and metadata.\n- **pos**: A UV layer that replaces pixel image coordinates as the noise position.\n- **direction**: A UV layer that sets each cell's tilt direction. Vector magnitude controls steepness.\n- **density**: A Mono layer that scales the Density culling.\n- **height**: A Mono layer that scales Random Height.\n- **rotation**: A Mono layer that scales Random Rotation.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **noise**: The computed cellular pattern.\n- **border**: A Mono SDF giving the exact distance to the border between the two nearest points.\n- **center**: A UV layer with the coordinates of the nearest grid point, useful with UV Sample for mosaic effects.\n- **id**: An ID layer with a hash of the nearest grid point. Values can be negative.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n*Type Info*: Sets the output layer's type.\n\n*Range*\n- **Amplitude**: Scales contrast between cell elements.\n- **Shift**: Raises or lowers overall brightness.\n\n*Pattern* (the main cell-layout controls)\n- **Element Size**: Size of the base cell, in image coordinates.\n- **Element Scale**: Per-axis stretching, shown with Per-Component Controls. Makes cells anisotropic.\n- **Jitter / Jitter Scale**: Randomly offsets grid points before measuring distances. Values above 1 can cause artifacts.\n- **Density / Density Seed**: Randomly removes cells whose values exceed the threshold.\n- **Lattice Type**:\n  - *Grid* gives square cells.\n  - *Hexagonal* uses a simplicial grid, producing hexagonal-looking cells.\n- **Metric**: How distance is measured, which changes cell shape:\n  - *Euclidean* gives round cells.\n  - *Manhattan* gives diamond cells.\n  - *Chebyshev* gives square cells.\n- **Smooth Edge**: Controls roundness of cells when using Euclidean.\n- **Offset**: Shifts the whole pattern.\n- **Tile Size**: Sets the repeat size so the pattern tiles seamlessly. Some values get adjusted to keep it tileable.\n\n*Shape*\n- **Mode**: Interprets shape values as absolute image-space units or as normalized 0–1 values.\n- **Gap**: Adds spacing between cells. Large values shrink cells until they disappear.\n- **Random Height / Height Seed**: Adds random per-cell height variation.\n- **Bevel**: Slopes cell edges. High values give pointed tops, low values give flat tops with hard edges.\n- **Bevel Ramp**: Custom curve that shapes the bevel profile.\n\n*Orient*\n- **Orient**: Tilts each cell's values toward a steepness.\n- **Rotate**: Rotates the overall tilt direction.\n- **Steepness**: How inclined each cell is.\n- **Random Rotation / Tilt Seed**: Random variation in tilt direction.\n\n*Distort*\n- **Distort**: Toggles footprint distortion.\n- **Amplitude, Element Size, Scale**: Control the driving noise and how strongly it distorts cell outlines.\n\n*Advanced*\n- **Global Seed**: Seeds all randomness in the pattern.\n\n*Post Processing* (applied in listed order)\n- **Fold**: Takes absolute values.\n- **Complement**: Inverts values as 1 − x.\n- **Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast**: Adjust the tonal curve and range.\n- **Clamp Minimum / Clamp Maximum**: Limit values to a range.\n\n**Pattern types**: The page doesn't list brick, triangle, or named Voronoi presets. The closest options are the square Grid, the Hexagonal lattice (which uses triangle-based simplicial grids internally), and the Metric choice, which sets the cell shape. Default Worley-style cells work for Voronoi-like looks. Brick patterns aren't covered by this node."}]},"uuid":"a854dc27-347d-4b70-8fa1-35c04ca1a785","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:49.947Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c93a794-4315-495e-bd0f-df7d4264d2a1","context":{"git_