{"parentUuid":"ce5937cb-502d-493b-a27c-78775a6b017b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NsEPxJYUez2MHsLBDoVQrw","type":"tool_result","content":"**Course: Substance Designer Essentials (Javier Perez, 17h 58m, 95 videos)**\n\n**Lesson 1: Substance Basics (4h 35m)**\n- Covers the Substance Designer interface, creating nodes, graph organization, and height values.\n- Introduces node categories: shapes and tiles, blends, transformations, noises, and flood fills, plus a pattern exercise.\n- Builds brick shapes, tiles them, adds variation, and works through alternate options.\n- Teaches the Tile Sampler for patterns, shows pattern examples, and creates outputs.\n- Adds damage with grout blending, grout options, and cracks.\n- **Project:** a set of brick or concrete tiles.\n\n**Lesson 2: Hard Surface (4h 26m)**\n- Builds complex shapes with insets, tiling patterns, and cutlines, and references graphs as reusable pieces.\n- Details a metal panel with an inset, a latch, vents, and panel variations.\n- Overlays cables and text signs.\n- Adds damage through height, roughness, base color, and dirt, then exposes graph parameters.\n- Covers gradient nodes and exporting texture outputs.\n- **Project:** a metal panel with one-off details that can be added to a main graph.\n\n**Lesson 3: Full Production (6h 19m)**\n- Starts with the height map: a cobblestone pattern, damage, grout, and floor variations.\n- Details a sidewalk with a curb, damage, and cracks.\n- Adds a rain gutter, metal grating, and a water level.\n- Works through albedo (base color) and roughness, then combines them.\n- Optimizes the graphs and prepares them for Marmoset.\n- **Project:** a cobblestone and sidewalk material with gutter and grate details.\n\n**Lesson 4: Presentation (2h 36m)**\n- Polishes and exports outputs.\n- Renders the material in Marmoset (interface, sphere and plane setups, post-processing).\n- Renders the material in Unreal Engine as a bonus (interface, materials, sphere and plane renders).\n- **Project:** polished renders for a portfolio.\n\n**Points not in the outline:**\n- Slope Blur, Warp, Histogram Scan, Edge Detect, Non-uniform blur, and height blend are not mentioned on the page. Flood fills, blends, transformations, and noises appear only as node-type categories.\n- The page does not state a methodology such as \"height first\" or \"macro to micro.\" The Lesson 3 order (height map, then detailing, albedo, and roughness) is consistent with a height-first approach, but the page does not describe it that way."}]},"uuid":"3221ba90-04af-4a2a-b464-c58d59f2f1fc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:29:30.413Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5732ffc9-1a8f-49b5-a2cc-03de01b3a61f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":829,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce5937cb-502d-493b-a27c-78775a6b017b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
