{"parentUuid":"d5af6b68-1d55-46d8-9f5b-73cfffda186a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPcYnWGCmV7nUkmwb8dDkn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Javier Perez\" Substance Designer slope blur tile sampler height map tutorial \"Gnomon\" OR \"Naughty Dog\" OR \"PlayStation\" material artist procedural\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Creating Cobblestones and Clover in Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/creating-cobblestones-and-clover-in-substance-designer\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Designer Essentials\",\"url\":\"https://www.learnsquared.com/courses/substance-designer-essentials\"},{\"title\":\"How to Design a Forest Ground Material With Substance 3D Designer\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/how-to-design-a-forest-ground-material-with-substance-3d-designer\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Source Javier Perez Takes You Space\",\"url\":\"https://substance3d.adobe.com/magazine/substance-source-javier-perez-takes-you-space/\"},{\"title\":\"Javier Perez - Substance Designer Enthusiast — Experience points\",\"url\":\"https://www.exp-points.com/substance-designer-enthusiast\"},{\"title\":\"Create Detailed Tile Trim Textures in Adobe Substance Designer w/ Javier Perez\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTWCj7mcsIU\"},{\"title\":\"Create STUNNING Tile Patterns in Adobe Substance Designer w/ Javier Perez\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RVsRF1UR7s0\"},{\"title\":\"Javier Perez - Lead Material Artist\",\"url\":\"https://www.meshmodeler.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Designer Essentials by Javier Perez < Premium Courses Online\",\"url\":\"https://online-courses.club/substance-designer-essentials-by-javier-perez/\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-designer-discussions/substance-designer-height-map/m-p/13466440\"}]\n\nHere's what the search turned up for Javier Perez and Substance Designer tutorials.\n\n**Background:** An interview on Experience Points describes him as a senior material artist currently working at Playstation VASG, with earlier credits at studios such as Infinity Ward, Kojima Productions, Sony Online, and Redemption Games. That interview is undated in the results, so his current employer may have changed. I found no results linking him to Gnomon or Naughty Dog.\n\n**Tutorials and courses:**\n- **Substance Designer Essentials (Learn Squared):** A beginner course that covers the interface and the Tile Sampler node. Its lesson plan includes a Tile Sampler patterns section and a full cobblestone height-map production lesson, per the course outline.\n- **YouTube tile trim and tile pattern videos:** Sci-fi metal tile trim textures and tile patterns, both described as made with him.\n- **NVIDIA-branded tutorial list:** A listing on his MeshModeler page includes topics such as \"Creating Tile Trim Textures,\" \"Create Stunning Tile Patterns,\" and \"Create Detailed Materials From Scratch & Height Maps.\"\n\n**Workflow advice:** In the Experience Points interview, he says a good material always starts with the height map. He adds that with my materials height maps I always start with the largest forms and move on to the finer granular details.\n\n**Slope Blur and Tile Sampler in practice:** These come up in third-party write-ups that credit his teaching. One 80.lv article says a river bed method from his tutorial was used for moss, where every aisle of moss is created separately, then they are collected into the composition and only then I add them to Tile Sampler. A forest ground article describes sculpt[ing] the edges using Slop Blur (the source misspells it) for root shapes, and credits Javier Perez with tips on the material.\n\n**Caveats:** The results don't include a direct link to the River Bed tutorial itself, so I couldn't confirm its content beyond those write-ups. Dates are inconsistent across results, with some pages roughly five to six years old. Check the YouTube channel or Learn Squared directly for current course details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c992d6e8-ca14-4822-bc57-28b87ab14984","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:29:41.410Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ef9ab1b-897c-4155-9923-1e7eeaa44ed6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":829,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5af6b68-1d55-46d8-9f5b-73cfffda186a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
