{"parentUuid":"d6d7fde1-4025-46dc-a8b1-054c1f5e41f7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YV5EE5k3FqQfm19QVx37Ad","type":"tool_result","content":"**Workflow**\n- Gathered real-world reference from NASA missions and matched forms closely to them.\n- Built a base shape designed to tile, keeping early detail light so the result still looked unique after tiling.\n- For repeating features, relied on tile generators and tile samplers, spending most of the effort on the main hard-surface shape.\n- Added detail before and after the tile sampler, balancing what went into the base shape against what came later.\n\n**Node techniques named**\n- Tile generator and tile sampler (repeating elements)\n- Transform 2D (hand-placing unique pieces so placement felt deliberate)\n- Crystals node (main fabric folds), blended and warped with procedural noise\n- Shapes and blends (compositing the 2D pipe image)\n- Non-uniform blur (rounding the pipes)\n- Random seed parameter (fold variations per tile)\n\nSlope blur and flood fill don't appear in the article, so I can't attribute them to him.\n\n**How he builds height**\n- Fabrics: folds come from Crystals, warped with noise, and checked against reference shapes. Masks control where folds and creases go.\n- Engine parts: pipes are composited from a 2D image, then softened with non-uniform blur.\n- Exterior panels: height maps were pushed further to emphasize shapes once tessellation is applied.\n\n**Exposed parameters**\n- Hiding pattern elements and changing colors (living quarters)\n- Weathering controls: dust and dirt in crevices, with adjustable dirt color, which shifts a material from new to worn\n- Random seed for fold variation\n- Scratches and dirt, which are heavier by default on exterior pieces and editable for a cleaner look\n\n**Process steps (summary)**\n1. Collect NASA reference.\n2. Build a tileable base shape.\n3. Add repeating detail with tile generators and samplers.\n4. Hand-place unique forms with Transform 2D.\n5. Build folds and fabric forms with Crystals, noise, and masks.\n6. Expose color, element visibility, and weathering controls.\n7. Push height for tessellation on exterior pieces."}]},"uuid":"00498c5a-8d35-4699-87d1-b0612ce84adf","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:07.787Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0261c485-5604-471e-bfeb-7392a19823e0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":16,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6d7fde1-4025-46dc-a8b1-054c1f5e41f7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"313df93a-dd9a-49a0-9a64-6cc6b144d70a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dwt1WduzgS4N5VZDbA7H3G","type":"tool_result","content":"**Cobblestone height build (as described in the article)**\n\n- **Stones:** The artist starts with a Tile Random and Distance draft to get the basic stone shapes. Slope Blur and Mosaic Grayscale refine the form, and two mixed Noises add surface detail. A Flood Fill adds variation in height and incline. Casper Wermuth's cliff method is partly applied to add chipped and recessed areas.\n- **Ground:** BnW Spots 3 and Moisture Noise are mixed for the base. Clouds 2 adds height variation. A Height Blend combines the ground and stone heights.\n\nThe article doesn't mention Warp or Edge Detect in this height build, and it gives no numeric parameter values or ranges.\n\n**Moss (method credited to Javier Perez)**\n\nFollowing Javier Perez's River Bed tutorial, each moss patch is built separately, then collected into a composition. That composition goes into a Tile Sampler to create a dense moss \"carpet.\" A base is added for form and relief. The finished moss is blended into the stones the same way as the ground.\n\n**Clover**\n\nFour clover leaf types are made and gathered into a composition, then placed with a Tile Sampler. A Luminance Random adds height variation so leaves overlap, and a Mask Random thins the layer out. A ground mask, inverted from the stone mask of the first Height Blend, is fed to the Tile Sampler as its Mask Map so clover grows only on the ground.\n\n**Dew drops**\n\nDrops are made from a Plasma node, with a Histogram Scan used to shape the pattern. A Safe Transform splits them into larger and smaller groups, which are mixed and blended in using a Blend and the clover mask. Histogram Scan appears here, not in the cobblestone height build.\n\n**Height, Normal, and finishing**\n\n- Normal is balanced so small details don't overpower the stones.\n- Blur HQ softens the moss relief and makes the clover leaves bend slightly.\n- Color uses Gradient Map + Blend, with Height Blend masks.\n- Roughness is finished, and spray is added to the stones.\n- A simple Scattering Map is made for Subsurface Scattering in Marmoset Toolbag 3.\n\n**Other named techniques:** Tile Random + Distance, Height Blend, the Casper Wermuth cliff method, and the Javier Perez River Bed approach."}]},"uuid":"4e79df59-c0d4-4e7d-a037-5303eb0e1cff","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:08.029Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0261c485-5604-471e-bfeb-7392a19823e0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":16,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"313df93a-dd9a-49a0-9a64-6cc6b144d70a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
