{"parentUuid":"c6cfaa56-40b1-46e0-a15e-f79644737313","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018jDAydoKyUxWEHYz4R8GDA","type":"tool_result","content":"The Flood Fill to Random Grayscale node takes a Flood Fill as its base and assigns random grayscale brightness values to its regions. It's meant for adding brightness variation across tiles.\n\nThe page doesn't list the node's parameters, their ranges, or any seed or luminosity bounds, so I can't describe those from this source. To find them, check the node's settings in Substance 3D Designer or the linked Flood Fill documentation."}]},"uuid":"ab46751a-51ce-4349-a5ac-cb68cf3a3477","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:29.506Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"43ae2350-30e9-4b8c-9cbf-2fb4d1d9fdf4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":24,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6cfaa56-40b1-46e0-a15e-f79644737313","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2717d60d-1975-4106-8234-24c93f6cb756","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxQuSpsxmY4ECRgDkPEqQt","type":"tool_result","content":"**Flood Fill to Gradient** takes a Flood Fill result and turns each tile into a linear gradient, with each tile oriented in its own direction. It's useful for building heightmaps where tiles appear randomly tilted or sloped.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **Flood Fill** (color): the base fill data that gets converted.\n- **Angle** (grayscale, optional): an external map that sets the gradient direction for each cell.\n- **Slope** (grayscale, optional): an external map that sets how strong each cell's gradient is.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Angle** (0.0–1.0): one global direction applied to all tiles.\n- **Angle Variation** (0.0–1.0): randomizes the direction per tile. The page calls this the most powerful control.\n- **Multiply by Bounding Box Size** (0.0–1.0): scales each gradient by its tile's size, so smaller tiles come out darker than larger ones.\n- **Angle Image Input Multiplier** (0.0–1.0): how much the Angle input map affects gradient direction.\n- **Slope Image Input Multiplier** (0.0–1.0): how much the Slope input map affects gradient strength.\n- **Multiply by Slope Intensity** (0.0–1.0): the page gives a range but no description of its effect.\n- **Flat Slope Color** (grayscale value): a solid gray value for flat areas. The page doesn't state a range."}]},"uuid":"c928d342-afc0-4fae-bf46-9578ccedc840","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:30.805Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"43ae2350-30e9-4b8c-9cbf-2fb4d1d9fdf4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":24,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2717d60d-1975-4106-8234-24c93f6cb756","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a9694c3c-c788-4e5c-824c-cf06656c1240","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vwy7yBcumtEnK17mLiB8LP","type":"tool_result","content":"**Histogram Scan** is a simple node in the Filters > Adjustments category that remaps the brightness and contrast of a grayscale input. It is useful for expanding or shrinking masks in a controllable way.\n\n- **Position** (0.0 to 1.0) works like a brightness control that moves the midpoint of the result. On a gradient input, it widens or narrows the transition area. The default of 0 produces an all-black result, so starting near 0.5 is more practical.\n- **Contrast** (0.0 to 1.0) sets how sharp or soft the transition is. Higher values give harder edges, and lower values give smoother falloff.\n- **Invert Position** (True/False) flips the final output, so light and dark areas swap.\n\nFor masks, adjust Position to grow or shrink the white area, and use Contrast to control edge hardness. The page does not describe weight or selection behavior, so that information isn't available from this source. Adobe's Substance Academy has a video on histogram operations that may cover more."}]},"uuid":"0ce60629-e578-4b3b-abe4-1dbaf2adab1c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:31.089Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"43ae2350-30e9-4b8c-9cbf-2fb4d1d9fdf4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":24,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matth