{"parentUuid":"a7156b47-a1c2-43d7-8845-35a0a56f7c76","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TvoPNUi6nDHqtFdpuoM4fD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance 3D Designer Directional Warp node documentation intensity angle experienceleague\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Directional warp\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/directional-warp\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide Cancel\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/filters/effects/multi-directional-warp.html\"},{\"title\":\"create jute fabric\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/create-jute-fabric\"},{\"title\":\"create roots\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/create-roots\"},{\"title\":\"dete directional warp with a special node\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/dete-directional-warp-with-a-special-node/\"},{\"title\":\"experienceleague.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/warp\"},{\"title\":\"Adding a Directional warp node\",\"url\":\"https://www.wysilab.com/OnLineDocumentation/Nodes/Nodes_MaskTransformation_DirectionalWarp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Adding a Directional warp node\",\"url\":\"https://wysilab.com/OnLineDocumentation/Nodes/Terrain-transformation/Nodes_TerrainTransformation_DirectionalWarp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Adding a Directional warp node\",\"url\":\"https://www.wysilab.com/OnLineDocumentation/Nodes/Mask-transformation/Nodes_MaskTransformation_DirectionalWarp.html\"}]\n\nThe official Adobe reference for the Directional warp node covers the two parameters you asked about, intensity and angle.\n\n**Intensity:** The Adobe reference lists Intensity as a float that sets how strong the warp is. The Intensity map offset float is subtracted from the values of the Intensity input image. The warp amount itself comes from the Intensity input, a grayscale map. That grayscale image sets how much warping gets applied to the Input image. A Substance tutorial adds that you can type in a value well above 1.\n\n**Angle:** The Warp angle float sets the angle of the warp effect, expressed in number of turns. That unit differs from the degrees used in the tutorials. One tutorial sets the angle to 90 degrees for a vertical deformation. The reference and the tutorials may therefore use different units, so check the value in the app before relying on either.\n\n**Other parameters:** The reference also lists an input filtering mode, a boolean that chooses nearest or bilinear sampling of the Input. The node also has a Primary Input (grayscale or color) for the image to be warped. It works similar to Warp, but then only in a specific direction.\n\n**Related nodes:** The Multi Directional Warp node can push in multiple directions, whereas the atomic version only allows for one. Its Warp Angle is documented on a 0.0 to 1.0 scale, which fits the turns-based unit.\n\n**Caution:** Some search results for \"directional warp\" came from Wysilab, a terrain tool, rather than Substance 3D Designer. Their parameter names and angle conventions are not the same as Substance's, so I left them out.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2194f24c-c788-48dd-afb4-c9c74f70f0b2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:05.922Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d0a16e10-1cce-493f-9254-9c1912a151d7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modifi