/\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"tile sampler\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/texture-generators/patterns/tile-sampler.html\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-designer-discussions/fill-empty-tile-shapes/m-p/13889381\"},{\"title\":\"floor tiles\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/generators/floor-tiles.html\"},{\"title\":\"Making Of / 07 November 2018\",\"url\":\"https://martindegraaf.artstation.com/blog/94eD/material-study-grass-pavers\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-designer-discussions/method-for-automatically-creating-decorative-tile-pattern/m-p/14182078\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-designer-discussions/help-make-a-brick-pattern/m-p/12890828\"},{\"title\":\"Tutorial: Mattershot Material in Substance\",\"url\":\"https://origin.80.lv/articles/recreating-a-mattershot-material-in-substance/?amp=1\"},{\"title\":\"community.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/t5/substance-3d-designer-discussions/help-make-a-brick-pattern/m-p/12900599\"},{\"title\":\"ponkke.gumroad.com\",\"url\":\"https://ponkke.gumroad.com/l/eKTJ\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2514602\"}]\n\nI couldn't retrieve the official Tile Sampler parameter reference. The Experience League and HelpX pages returned only site navigation, so I can't confirm the exact names or the full list of inputs and parameters. The pieces below come from community posts, tutorials, and related docs.\n\n**What the node does and how it differs from Tile Generator**\nThe Tile Generator is a simpler version of the tile sampler node, with less controls and inputs. Per a community post, you can use up to 6 Pattern inputs in a Tile Sampler.\n\n**Pattern inputs and the distribution map**\nIn one answered forum thread, a user built a brick pattern by having two patterns inputs to the Tile Sampler node. Then a mask in the Pattern Distribution Map input of the same node to switch between them. A distribution mask is therefore what chooses which pattern goes where. Another community expert notes that turning global offset and mask random off in the tile samplers helps tiles fit over each other when you use several samplers.\n\n**Mask and vector inputs**\nA Polycount user fed the normal goes to \"Vector Map Input\" and the shape to \"Mask Map Input\". Their tuning advice was to under rotation set the \"Vector Map Multiplied\" to 1 and under color set the \"Mask Map Threshold\" to something low. This is a user workaround, not official documentation.\n\n**Rotation and scale**\nA tutorial on grass pavers used 4 x 4 Tiling and Scale 0.99 and a Rotation Map that made certain tiles rotate and others sit in place. A Spanish-language course lists the node's parameters as Count X and Y - Random Rotation - Random Scale, which suggests that randomness is controlled separately from the rotation input.\n\nFor the authoritative parameter list, check the Tile Sampler page on Experience League directly, or open the node in Substance 3D Designer and inspect its input and parameter panel. If you can share the input names you see there, I can search for more specific guidance on them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"be65fce1-454e-4c2b-990e-e37eeca0b25e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:07.806Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d0a16e10-1cce-493f-9254-9c1912a151d7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":25,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"orig