{"parentUuid":"783877b4-3b9e-4032-a858-0a4e9f9dab4e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWikVRfi5KnF7zU9y9zTGg","type":"tool_result","content":"The Shape Stroke node, found under Filters > Effects in Substance 3D Designer, adds an outline around a shape. It works on a black-and-white mask in the grayscale version or on a shape's alpha channel in the color version, and it can be considered a fuller alternative to Edge Detect. Its parameters control the stroke's Width (from -1.0 to 1.0), the overall Opacity (0.0 to 1.0), and the Outline Color. The grayscale version also offers a Mask Color for the transparency-mapped output. The color version provides Input Is Pre-Multiplied, which specifies whether the input uses pre-multiplied alpha. Pre-Multiply Output, available in both versions, sets whether the output is pre-multiplied."}]},"uuid":"be02a427-ec30-499f-a2f0-7254546cb793","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:37.490Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"427d078b-f89c-4184-b74d-c0846ddc4643","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"783877b4-3b9e-4032-a858-0a4e9f9dab4e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ef1d2cfa-5a0f-4988-81d5-3e3e7bd24268","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013uWE3sFZBvw1353jSAc251","type":"tool_result","content":"Vector Warp is a distortion effect that moves pixels in your input based on a color vector map, rather than the grayscale map used by the Warp and Directional Warp nodes. That makes it more flexible for distortions that need varying directions.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **Input:** The color map to be distorted.\n- **Vector Map:** The color map that drives the distortion. The page is inconsistent about which channels it reads: one section says Red and Blue, while the description says Red and Green (X and Y). Check this in your version before relying on it.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Intensity (0.0 to 1.0):** Multiplies the strength of the Vector Map's effect.\n- **Vector Format (DirectX or OpenGL):** Flips how the Green channel is interpreted, between \"up\" and \"down.\" Choose the option that matches the convention your map was built with.\n\n**Usage notes**\n- The Vector Map works like a normal map but doesn't need to be normalized. Blue and Alpha can be left black.\n- Building a good Vector Map is usually the hardest part. You can convert a grayscale height map with the Normal node, combine channels with RGBA Merge, or use a flow map.\n- Use this node when standard Warp nodes can't produce the specific, direction-varying distortion you need."}]},"uuid":"73bf575e-bec0-49ba-a0bb-2c9244b8ba70","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:37.640Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"427d078b-f89c-4184-b74d-c0846ddc4643","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef1d2cfa-5a0f-4988-81d5-3e3e7bd24268","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"88a868ec-5249-4adc-a650-5eed92f5fa13","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019vHtchhgFk1eqr2QzxYpFm","type":"tool_result","content":"**Distance node overview**\n\nThe Distance node finds the nearest white pixel in a mask and produces a linear gradient that fades outward from the mask's edges. It can also copy the color from a source image at that nearest edge point. Mask pixels above a 0.5 gray value count as white. Neighboring fades stop where they meet, so they never overlap. Common uses include growing masks more predictably than blurring and contrast adjustment, creating Voronoi-style cell noise, and beveling shapes with a sharp linear falloff that you can remap later.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Color mode (Boolean):** Switches the output between grayscale and color. It also changes the type of the Source input.\n- **Maximum distance (Float):** Sets how far, in pixels, the node searches for the closest edge. The source doesn't give a numeric range.\n- **Combine source/distance (Boolean):**\n  - *Combine:* Blends the Source input with the fade. If a Source is connected, its values mix with the computed distance.\n  - *Only Source:* Outputs solid color taken only from the Source input.\n- **Distance mode (Integer):** Chooses how distance is measured.\n  - *Euclidean:* Based on squared X and Y differences.\n  - *Manhattan:* Based on absolute X and Y differences.\n  - *Chebyshev:* Uses the larger of the absolute X or Y difference.\n\n**Input connectors**\n\n- **Mask input (Grayscale, primary):** The shape whose borders are measured. The node thresholds it at 0.5 to create a binary mask.\n- **Source input (Color or Grayscale, optional):** Supplies the pixel value taken from the nearest mask border.\n\n**Usage notes**\n\n- The node is described as difficult to master.\n- Maximum distance and Distance mode both affect the shape of the fade, so test them on your mask.\n- Use Only Source when you want the Source image's color alone, without the gradient."}]},"uuid":"0940dc92-8064-49da-8365-1062bbeb7ad6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:38.112Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"427d078b-f89c-4184-b74d-c0846ddc4643","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"88a868ec-5249-4adc-a650-5eed92f5fa13","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c3122b56-d960-4ec4-b755-4e5e47b38672","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018taaaeZFKWBNtyXMipLY15","type":"tool_result","content":"**Splatter** is a pattern generator in Substance 3D Designer that scatters a map input across a surface. Each copy can have a random scale, rotation, and luminance or color variation. It is simpler to use than Tile Generator, though Tile Generator can produce similar results with more setup.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Pattern Size Width:** 0.0 to 1000.0. Number of patterns along the X-axis.\n- **Pattern Size Height:** 0.0 to 1000.0. Number of patterns along the Y-axis.\n- **Rotation:** -360.0 to 360.0. Rotates all patterns by the same amount.\n- **Rotation Variation:** 0.0 to 360.0. Adds random rotation to each shape.\n- **Zoom:** 100.0 to 10000.0. Scales the final result up. This breaks tiling.\n- **Gain:** 0.0 to 10.0. Adjusts the blending gain so patterns stand out more.\n- **Pan X:** -100.0 to 100.0. Shifts the whole result horizontally.\n- **Pan Y:** -100.0 to 100.0. Shifts the whole result vertically.\n- **Disorder:** 0.0 to 100.0. Randomly shifts shapes.\n- **Grid Number:** 0 to 8. Changes grid size to adjust scale while maintaining tiling.\n- **Disorder Angle:** 0.0 to 360.0. Sets the direction of disorder shifting.\n- **Disorder Random:** False or True. Randomizes the disorder angle for more chaotic results.\n- **Pattern Size:** 5 to 12.\n- **Size Variation:** 0.0 to 100.0. Adds random scaling to each shape.\n- **Image Input Filtering (Engine v4 only):** Bilinear + Mipmaps, Bilinear, or Nearest. Sets the filtering applied to the input image.\n- **Output Level Min:** 0.0 to 1.0. Adjusts the minimum output level.\n- **Output Level Max:** 0.0 to 1.0. Adjusts the maximum output level.\n- **Background Color:** Grayscale value. Sets a solid background color.\n- **Luminance Variation:** 0.0 to 1.0. Grayscale version only. Adds brightness variation.\n- **Color Variation:** 0.0 to 1.0. Color version only. Adds color variation.\n\n**Usage notes**\n\n- Splatter requires a map input to produce output.\n- The default settings look uniform. Adjust the Disorder parameters, especially Disorder and Disorder Random, to get a randomized look.\n- Zoom breaks tiling, so avoid it if the result must tile seamlessly.\n- Grid Number changes scale while keeping the result tileable."}]},"uuid":"65157b05-c96f-4cd5-8be0-63b6d5d17475","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:39.913Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"427d078b-f89c-4184-b74d-c0846ddc4643","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3122b56-d960-4ec4-b755-4e5e47b38672","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
