{"parentUuid":"eb43a835-1c9c-424f-9d42-9beb91e2993e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017mKZBbS91XAxdVHtvV2JVY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance 3D Designer \"Height Blend\" node documentation heightmap blend two height maps contrast position\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"function nodes overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/function-graphs/nodes-reference-for-function-graphs/function-nodes-overview.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide Cancel\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/material-filters/effects-material/height-blend.html\"},{\"title\":\"spline sample thickness\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/spline-paths-tools/spline-tools/spline-sample-thickness.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/atomic-nodes/blend/blending-modes-description.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/mesh-based-generators/utilities-mesh-based-generators/material-mesh-data-blender.html\"},{\"title\":\"Last updated on\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/material-filters/effects-material/material-height-blend.html\"},{\"title\":\"Material Nodes Overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/vn_vi/substance-3d-designer/using/nodes-overview.html\"},{\"title\":\"Material Nodes Overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/in_hi/substance-3d-designer/using/nodes-overview.html\"},{\"title\":\"Material Nodes Overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/ae_ar/substance-3d-designer/using/nodes-overview.html\"},{\"title\":\"Material Nodes Overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-designer/using/nodes-overview.html\"}]\n\nThe Adobe documentation for Height Blend covers the node's inputs and controls. In short, it combines two Heightmaps based on their height information and, in addition to the blended heightmap, generates a Black and White mask that can be used elsewhere.\n\n**Inputs**\n- Height Top and Height Bottom are grayscale inputs.\n- Mask is an optional grayscale input for masking the node's effects. Mask slot used for masking the node's effects.\n\n**Controls**\n- **Height Offset (0.0 to 1.0):** This is the position control you were asking about. It shifts where the blend level sits along the height axis, and the documentation calls it the main control for the blend.\n- **Contrast (0.0 to 1.0):** This sets how sharp the transition is. The docs describe it as adjusting the blend's contrast so transitions become sharper.\n- **Mode:** This switches between two blending modes, Balanced height and Bottom height priority. The search snippet didn't include the full explanation of how each mode behaves, so check the full page for that.\n- **Opacity (0.0 to 1.0):** Controls the node's overall strength. The snippet cut off before describing it.\n\n**Usage**\nThe docs say the node is useful when you have two high-quality Heightmaps to combine, but not necessarily a full material. If you're blending full materials based on their heightmaps, the related Material Height Blend node is the more advanced version, and it has no user-defined mask.\n\nThe results were from Adobe's older HelpX pages. Adobe has said HelpX pages will automatically redirect to the equivalent Experience League page, so the current version of the documentation may be on Experience League.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"762f95c2-9115-46c5-98c3-3a1f1c0a3f08","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:32:51.393Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"72e3f164-a376-4274-9c27-23908fe07f86","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb43a835-1c9c-424f-9d42-9beb91e2993e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
