{"parentUuid":"0458547d-0f79-44a7-96a9-bd68e4fb895b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015DYEjQFSMDhVQNX6zHV552","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Bradford Smith\" Substance Designer material artist tutorial nodes height edge\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Substance Designer: Creating Your First Substance Material\",\"url\":\"https://www.toolfarm.com/?p=29580\"},{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLE\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/getting-started-with-substance-3d-designer\"},{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLEBeginner274 min\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/getting-started-with-substance-3d-designer?learnIn=1\"},{\"title\":\"how to master substance designer 001agt\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/how-to-master-substance-designer-001agt/\"},{\"title\":\"function nodes overview\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/function-graphs/nodes-reference-for-function-graphs/function-nodes-overview.html\"},{\"title\":\"From the course: Substance Designer: Creating Nonphotorealistic (NPR) Materials\",\"url\":\"https://origin-www.lynda.com/Substance-Designer-tutorials/Building-outline-mask-part-1/2823134/2942214-4.html\"},{\"title\":\"From the course: Substance Designer: Creating Nonphotorealistic (NPR) Materials\",\"url\":\"https://www.lynda.com/Substance-Designer-tutorials/Using-Height-Normal/2823134/2942215-4.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://www.almentor.net/en/courses/Introduction-to-Substance-Designer\"},{\"title\":\"From the course: Substance Designer 2020 Essential Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.lynda.com/Substance-Designer-tutorials/Normal/2834005/2345154-4.html\"}]\n\nI couldn't find any result connecting Bradford Smith to Substance Designer tutorials. The search returned general Substance Designer learning material, but nothing that names him as author, instructor, or artist.\n\nThe closest match for height and edge work is the Adobe \"Getting Started with Substance 3D Designer\" course. It's a beginner series of about 274 minutes, and its chapters cover workflow and node architecture, creating the height data, maps such as roughness and base color, and material layering with exporting and publishing. The height section includes building the base material node, large and small shapes, and scattering shapes with the Shape Splatter node. I can't confirm who produced it from these results.\n\nOther relevant results:\n\n- **Edge and bevel work:** An 80.lv article notes that cobblestones are tiled because there's repetition, variations in each shape, and the shapes are beveled at the edges. It also describes building the height map first, from largest forms to smallest, before generating normals and other maps.\n- **Edge damage and softening:** An Almentor course lists lessons on adding depth and softening the edges of the main shapes and adding damage on the edges. Its listing doesn't give an instructor name.\n- **Bevel and edge masks:** A Lynda course on non-photorealistic materials covers an Edgeware node for outlines and a bevel node feeding a curvature node. That course is paywalled, and its results don't name the instructor in the excerpts.\n\nIf you have a source for Bradford Smith, such as a site, channel, or course title, I can search for that directly. Searching his name alone, or with \"Substance\" and the platform where you saw his work, may also help.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"07ccae07-084b-4700-84eb-b46a83884f73","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:14.775Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b9633e05-9768-409a-a91f-373ec0d39d73","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"vi