{"parentUuid":"229fd2df-1a7c-41fa-a815-aef424778211","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKEe6jxLf6j5pEoW1Ut3pZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Rogelio Olguin\" Substance Designer breakdown material height\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hi everyone,\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2350071\"},{\"title\":\"Are you looking for a beginner’s guide to texture creation in Substance Designer?\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/the-basics-of-substance-designer-with-rogelio-olguin/?amp=1\"},{\"title\":\"Gnomon / Substance Designer: Texture Creation with Rogelio Olguin\",\"url\":\"https://rogelio.artstation.com/projects/lnJKo\"},{\"title\":\"Are you looking for a beginner’s guide to texture creation in Substance Designer?\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/the-basics-of-substance-designer-with-rogelio-olguin/\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2347410\"},{\"title\":\"geometric patterns and ornamental art with ishan verma\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/products/substance3d/magazine/geometric-patterns-and-ornamental-art-with-ishan-verma.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2347198\"},{\"title\":\"slanted surface materials creating the road in sd\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/slanted-surface-materials-creating-the-road-in-sd\"},{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLEBeginner137 min\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/mdl-malachite-material-breakdown\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Designer: Creating Your First Substance Material\",\"url\":\"https://www.toolfarm.com/?p=29580\"}]\n\nI couldn't find any specific height values, such as a numeric height or a height-map setting, in the results. What the results do show is a Gnomon lecture by Rogelio Olguin that covers height work in Substance Designer.\n\n- **The lecture's focus:** The 6-hour Gnomon course covers the basics of texture creation, and it starts by setting up height information before following the artist's steps to build a cobblestone texture.\n- **Why height comes first:** The heightmap is the base for the rest of the material. Per an Adobe tutorial on a different material, nearly every other output map relies quite heavily on the information set up in the Heightmap.\n- **Chapter outline:** A forum post lists the chapters, which include Introduction, Substance Designer Basics, Cobble Creation, Cobble Dirt, Pebbles Dead Twigs, and others.\n\nFor the actual height values, you'd need the lecture itself. It's sold through the Gnomon Workshop at thegnomonworkshop.com/tutorials/substance-designer, and the ArtStation page for Rogelio Olguin's project is at rogelio.artstation.com/projects/lnJKo. Neither was readable in the search results, so I can't confirm whether either shows the exact numbers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"91004f2b-a466-4b1f-8f79-15b5694d751c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:15.157Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b9633e05-9768-409a-a91f-373ec0d39d73","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"229fd2df-1a7c-41fa-a815-aef424778211","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"96315dee-48cb-4183-b044-6baffa58a245","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHcs25RjvQDuQE1nHsw4Zx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Vincent Derozier\" Substance Designer procedural tutorial breakdown\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLEBeginner7 min\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/vincent-d-rozier-s-procedural-bust-breakdown\"},{\"title\":\"Product banner image\",\"url\":\"https://flippednormals.com/product/mosaic-creation-techniques-with-substance-designer-vincent-derozier-26659\"},{\"title\":\"levelup mosaics\",\"url\":\"https://levelupdigital.gumroad.com/l/levelup_mosaics\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday, July 11th, 2026 Posted by Jim Thacker\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgchannel.com/2026/07/tutorial-create-realistic-cliff-materials-in-substance-3d-designer/\"},{\"title\":\"Saturday, July 11th, 2026 Posted by Jim Thacker\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgchannel.com/?p=177160\"},{\"title\":\"creating realistic cliff materials using substance designer\",\"url\":\"https://mrx.thegnomonworkshop.com/workshops/creating-realistic-cliff-materials-using-substance-designer\"},{\"title\":\"Créer un oeil procédural avec Substance Designer (MAJ)\",\"url\":\"https://3dvf.com/actualite-14021-creer-un-oeil-procedural-avec-substance-designer-html/\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2362551\"},{\"title\":\"creating a procedural material in substance designer\",\"url\":\"https://www.udemy.com/course/creating-a-procedural-material-in-substance-designer/\"},{\"title\":\"a free substance 3d designer survival kit for beginners\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/a-free-substance-3d-designer-survival-kit-for-beginners\"}]\n\nI found several Substance Designer tutorials and breakdowns by Vincent Dérozier, ranging from a free Adobe article to paid video courses.\n\n**Free breakdown (Adobe)**\nAdobe Learn hosts a short article, \"Vincent Dérozier's Procedural Bust Breakdown,\" which is the closest match to what you asked for. It describes a sculpture he built in Substance Designer alone, during time off from his job at Ubisoft Montréal. The project took 3 weeks, so to avoid a breakdown with 500 steps, he focused on the key setups and recipes. His method was to break the character into separate sub-graphs for each element, so he could focus on each part without getting overwhelmed. The article also notes that separate graphs save time but risk losing sight of the big picture.\n\n**Paid video courses (Gnomon Workshop)**\n- *Creating Realistic Cliff Materials using Substance Designer*: a 4-hour workshop focused on creating realistic cliff surfaces, with a strong emphasis on balancing high levels of detail with clear visual readability. It covers building base shapes, introducing controlled breakups and deformations, and constructing a clear hierarchical structure. Later lessons include chiseling, mineral characteristics, cracks, and porosity. A CG Channel article adds that the course also covers developing color and roughness, balancing textures, and graph optimization. Access is through a Gnomon subscription, which costs $57/month or $499/year.\n- *Mosaic Creation Techniques with Substance Designer* (with Levelup.Digital): a 3-hour narrated, step-by-step video tutorial on making mosaic tile flooring. It covers breaking down a material and his personal techniques for using SVGs to build architectural projects. It is sold on Gumroad for $10.\n\n**Free introductory kit**\nDérozier also released a free introduction called a Survival Kit. Part 1 covers the basics: shapes, volume creation, blending, sculpting, noise management, and the vocabulary needed to create a material. The creator notes that it is a glossary rather than an exhaustive tutorial.\n\n**Notes**\n- His job title differs across sources. Adobe lists him at Ubisoft Montréal, Gnomon lists him as Senior Lead Content Artist at Gearbox Studio Québec, and the older Survival Kit listing names Eidos Montreal. These probably reflect different points in his career.\n- I did not find a free, step-by-step procedural breakdown beyond the Adobe bust article in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"71f446af-7ce1-4cd4-82b2-10dd435c4311","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:16.860Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b9633e05-9768-409a-a91f-373ec0d39d73","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"96315dee-48cb-4183-b044-6baffa58a245","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
