{"parentUuid":"c785525d-d047-4ab2-8026-b9879bef9104","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LazSTKCTyyyUkucmF3uSCY","type":"tool_result","content":"The article says the Gnomon Workshop released *Creating Realistic Cliff Materials using Substance Designer*, presented by Gearbox Studio's Vincent Dérozier. It runs 4.5 hours and covers Substance 3D Designer and Unreal Engine. The lessons focus on building realistic cliff surfaces as procedural materials that can be reused as a cohesive set of variants for real-time games and cinematics. Key techniques include:\n\n- **Layered shapes:** Breaking up large primary forms with smaller secondary ones.\n- **Erosion patterns:** Adding weathering effects.\n- **Fine surface detail:** Adding small-scale texture.\n- **Information layers:** Identifying the different layers of detail and building each one procedurally.\n- **Graph organization:** Keeping the node graph clean and readable.\n- **Color, roughness, and optimization:** Developing color and roughness, balancing textures, and optimizing the graph for production.\n\nThe article doesn't mention base shapes, deformations, hierarchy, chiseling, mineral characteristics, cracks, or porosity by name, and it doesn't name any specific nodes.\n\n**Publishing details:** Jim Thacker wrote the CG Channel article, dated Saturday, July 11th, 2026. The workshop is available through a Gnomon Workshop subscription, which the article says also covers over 300 tutorials. The article also notes that CG Channel is owned by Gnomon."}]},"uuid":"6f658dd8-2014-43a7-b72d-be83e0c81dc0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:31.350Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5c089392-ade0-4c95-89c0-e52e9e8fa96d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Us