{"parentUuid":"28c42b1e-2126-4f5b-b837-9df3ab75434d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QStDMt3n8yM9bLT3sKeqy3","type":"tool_result","content":"The DETE Directional Warp is a free, custom utility node for Substance Designer, created by Daniel Thiger and inspired by work from Even Liaw and Bradford Smith. It's available as a download from Gumroad.\n\n- **What it does:** It warps shapes in a chosen direction while keeping them anchored at their origin, so they don't get pushed off the canvas.\n- **How it differs from the stock node:** It adds controls the original lacks. You can set how many directions to warp in, adjust intensity, and choose the warp direction.\n- **Visual problem it solves:** Directional warping can push shapes off screen. This node avoids that, so you can warp shapes without losing them from view.\n- **Usage notes:** Thiger was scheduled to speak at GDC 2018's Substance Day on Tuesday, March 20, at 5:30, about natural materials."}]},"uuid":"10b2edff-984b-47f6-b7cc-95fd12197747","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:50.508Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aef5e6d3-dafc-415f-922e-8158140591ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28c42b1e-2126-4f5b-b837-9df3ab75434d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7615fcb2-08e1-41a2-9a99-556bd987c274","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wgn3LKA347NyrVxKiw3ssN","type":"tool_result","content":"The tutorial's height section (Ch2) lists these steps, paraphrased from the video titles:\n\n1. Set up a Substance package and its project settings.\n2. Create a base material node that all data passes through.\n3. Build the large form shapes.\n4. Build the small shapes in two parts.\n5. Create spatter shapes for use with the scatter node.\n6. Scatter medium dirt mounds with Shape Splatter.\n7. Scatter small dirt mounds with Shape Splatter.\n8. Create pebble shapes and scatter them with Shape Splatter.\n9. Build twig shapes as a subgraph, expose its parameters, and scatter them with Shape Splatter.\n\nThe page spells the node \"Shape Spatter\" in some titles and \"Shape Splatter\" in others.\n\n**Chapter list:**\n- **Ch1:** Workflow, Substance 3D Designer, and node architecture\n- **Ch2:** Creating the height data\n- **Ch3:** Roughness and base color maps\n- **Ch4:** Material layering, texture export, and sbsar publishing\n\n**Not in the content:** The page doesn't mention Tile Sampler, Slope Blur, Warp, Histogram Scan, Height Blend, or Edge Detect. It also gives no numeric values for any setting.\n\n**Workflow rules:** The page doesn't state \"height first\" or \"macro to micro\" as rules. The sequence suggests that height work comes before the Ch3 maps and that large shapes come before small ones, but the page doesn't say so explicitly."}]},"uuid":"33c6db54-1bb9-4a62-8e68-d4addf6dc2cb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:53.075Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aef5e6d3-dafc-415f-922e-8158140591ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7615fcb2-08e1-41a2-9a99-556bd987c274","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3106d4d3-82a1-4ca4-91b6-121ad2260c86","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CrztcaLYaUkqgJ1WymBZ3Y","type":"tool_result","content":"The article covers most of this chain for the Red rock height, but it doesn't mention slope blur, height blend, or erosion/chipping. Tile Sampler appears only in other materials (Round, and a Tile Generator in Blue).\n\n1. **Start with a flat grey base** and build the Height first.\n2. **Cells 4:** Generate a cell pattern, then **warp** it to make the edges irregular.\n3. **Non-Uniform Edge Detect** (a community node by Maxime Guyard-Morin): Run it on the warped cells to create a binary mask of the pieces. A standard Edge Detect also works. Keep randomness low so the segments stay tightly packed.\n4. **Flood Fill → Flood Fill to Random Gradient:** Use the mask to generate the height variation. Adjust the angle variety so the pieces tilt inward, as if from impact damage.\n5. **Second Flood Fill:** Create a random greyscale mask.\n6. **Histogram Scan:** Threshold the greyscale mask to choose which pieces crack further. Expose the **Balance** value as a parameter to control the ratio of secondary and tertiary cracks.\n7. **Repeat for finer detail:** Reuse the same setup at each smaller size, changing only the cell scale. Make larger breaks more likely than smaller ones to keep the proportions realistic.\n8. **Vector Warp Greyscale (optional):** Offset grunge or noise using a gradient map from the cracks so the detail doesn't spill across piece boundaries."}]},"uuid":"7839f0dd-0f6f-4a8b-92d9-a3b22b17e814","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:53.572Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"aef5e6d3-dafc-415f-922e-8158140591ee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/User