{"parentUuid":"894ca629-9c00-42a5-ba34-bf037c497706","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BRiYvTdJc8JUybVSXLmsjB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Artist:** Massimo Caggese, Prop Artist at elite3d (Valencia).\n\n**Workflow for the tile shapes and detailing (paraphrased):**\n\n1. **Base shapes:** Start with simple primitives, then combine them with add and subtract blend operations.\n2. **Smoothing and shaping:** Blur the shapes, adjust them with histogram scan, and warp or mirror them where needed.\n3. **Curved piece:** Build one ceramic tile piece with the CurveTool by Ilya Kuzmichev.\n4. **Assembly:** Combine the main pieces into the floral design. Subtract operations between neighboring parts control the gap thickness.\n5. **Weathering:** Add slight surface chipping to the stone parts. Leave the inner, unexposed ceramic parts nearly clean.\n6. **Variation:** Apply the TileRandomizer node by Nyronic to the stone and ceramic materials. This breaks up the noise and randomizes color and roughness across individual tiles.\n7. **Global dirt:** Add a couple of global dirt layers for a uniform, realistic finish.\n\n**Not in the article:** The source doesn't name the Tile Generator, Tile Sampler, SVG, bevel, edge, or height blend nodes, and it gives no specific parameter values or exact node order beyond the general steps above. For those details, you'd need the author's published graph or the project page on ArtStation."}]},"uuid":"d5e0c320-caaa-4d15-9d60-e71dd9e4c3a5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:05.172Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f76b46e-885b-406b-8e4e-05a808631d17","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"894ca629-9c00-42a5-ba34-bf037c497706","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e670439e-74a5-4de8-b588-5af9b94ae475","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGqF9JEfW5LkgtPmntLyKf","type":"tool_result","content":"**Artist:** Cairo Goodbrand, a 3D Environment Artist from South Africa who was based in the UK at the time. The article names Theodore McKenzie as the interviewer, though the closing credit lists Theodore Nikitin.\n\n**Publication date:** 03 February 2022\n\n**Materials broken down:**\n\n- **Round:** A pointillist recreation of a Henri-Edmond Cross painting. The article doesn't describe a separate height map. Instead, masks feed a Tile Sampler that scatters dot-shaped brushstrokes across the surface.\n- **Blue:** Underwater rocks. The artist built a height map first, then created base color, and pushed most rocks below a water surface. A parameterized rock generator, blended with Max Lighten, provides the rock forms.\n- **Red:** Fragmented salt-rock-like pieces. Height comes from a Flood Fill to a random gradient, tilted so the pieces appear to lean inward as if from impact. Cells-based cracks, masked with an edge detect, define the breakup.\n\nThe article also mentions a Green material, but only in passing (in the context of subsurface scattering), so it isn't broken down."}]},"uuid":"274f9745-43b5-4e6c-8dfb-9938d84bf46f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:05.514Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f76b46e-885b-406b-8e4e-05a808631d17","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e670439e-74a5-4de8-b588-5af9b94ae475","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9c3a93a3-67e2-47d1-8ec1-6f69fbf65378","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2sLiSqk7diA4TtLepEJFE","type":"tool_result","content":"**Artist:** Karen Stanley, an Environment Artist at Ubisoft Massive.\n\nThe article summarizes two of her free Substance Designer breakdowns, but it doesn't include the node-by-node details you listed.\n\n**Roof tiles (height-first workflow):**\n- Build the main tile shape in the height map first.\n- Use gradients to shape a profile curve.\n- Tile the shapes and add variation.\n- Layer in surface detail from grunge maps.\n- Add chipped or damaged edges with an edge detect node.\n- Derive the diffuse map from gradients and AO masks.\n- Create gloss maps with several levels of detail.\n\n**Lava (macro-to-micro workflow):**\n- Start with the large base forms.\n- Add medium and small detail, such as rolls and cracks.\n- Use warp nodes to create flow.\n- Build the color map with gradient nodes.\n\n**Not covered in the article:** slope blur, flood fill, histogram scan, tile sampler, and height blend nodes, plus any specific values. The full node graphs are in the paid PDF breakdowns linked from the article."}]},"uuid":"054fd8bd-50d7-406a-b166-67a3fa730956","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:06.101Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f76b46e-885b-406b-8e4e-05a808631d17","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c3a93a3-67e2-47d1-8ec1-6f69fbf65378","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295