 up the edges using Voronoi fractures to get an eroded, chipped look, though that work was done in Houdini with a cliff material made in Substance Designer.\n\nFor general Substance Designer cliff work, these results may help:\n\n- **Rock base shapes:** One tutorial series focuses on capturing the base shapes of various types of rocks.\n- **Erosion and cracks:** A second installment covers how to apply aged and eroded surface detail, starting from basic shapes and layering on cracks, pits, etc.\n- **Layered forms:** One artist describes working like a sculpture, starting from simple primary and secondary forms, with some layers added and others subtracted.\n- **Structured course:** A Gnomon workshop on cliff materials covers primary shapes and large-scale forms, secondary breakups, erosion patterns, and fine surface detailing.\n\nIf you can tell me where you saw Casper Wermuth's breakdown (for example, a specific ArtStation page, YouTube video, or course), I can search for that source directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"056ca305-c02f-4ec6-97c1-de23fd787e91","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:19.032Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bc0109e8-2f40-44af-a2f2-947cda776d25","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b704ac3-115a-48a8-af75-b23c47e2e2ab","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c61cf963-06fe-432a-b96f-bad488caef54","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vvi7V72kmL5n4LK2oi1sba","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance Days GDC 2018 Daniel Thiger natural materials talk Substance Designer workflow summary\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"substance day at gdc 2018\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/substance-day-at-gdc-2018\"},{\"title\":\"substance day at gdc 2018\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/substance-day-at-gdc-2018/?amp=1\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Day at GDC 2018\",\"url\":\"https://magazine.substance3d.com/substance-day-at-gdc-2018/\"},{\"title\":\"dete directional warp with a special node\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/dete-directional-warp-with-a-special-node/\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Days Comes to GDC 2018\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/substance-days-comes-to-gdc-2018/\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://scrapbox.io/Dinustydiscord/Substance_Designer\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://scrapbox.io/Dinustydiscord/Substance Designer\"},{\"title\":\"Allegorithmic Introduces Signature Series For Substance Users\",\"url\":\"https://cgw.com/Press-Center/News/2018/Allegorithmic-Introduces-Signature-Series-For-Su.aspx\"},{\"title\":\"www.artstation.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.artstation.com/a/591506\"},{\"title\":\"Product banner image\",\"url\":\"https://flippednormals.com/product/plaster-wall-with-parameter-driven-bullet-holes-daniel-thiger-26657\"}]\n\nI couldn't find a detailed workflow summary of Daniel Thiger's GDC 2018 talk. The results confirm the session existed and what it was about, but not its specific techniques.\n\n**What the talk covered:** Thiger was listed as a speaker for Substance Day at GDC 2018, which ran on March 20 in Room 3014 at Moscone West. One schedule describes his session as covering the techniques and methodology he used to build natural materials for Allegorithmic's Substance Source, and says it would show some of his workflows and how Substance Designer helped him create natural materials for Allegorithmic's Substance Source. Gain insight into some of his workflows and how Substance Designer has increa. The session was also titled \"Creating Photorealistic Materials in Substance Designer\" in a community resource list GDC 2018 - Daniel Thiger - Creating Photorealistic Materials in Substance Designer.\n\n**Context for the talk:** Thiger had a Substance Source connection through Allegorithmic's Signature Series. The inaugural Signature Series release came from game designer Daniel Thiger, lead environment artist for Bungie. Thiger, whose work includes Destiny and Destiny 2, chose to create 15 materials for three settings: jungle, desert and Iceland. These materials are fully procedural and can be tweaked as needed by the end user.\n\n**Limits of what I found:** None of the results contained the talk's slides, video, or a step-by-step account of his node graphs or process. One 80.lv article also mentioned a utility node he shared, a directional warp node, but that was a separate release and not a talk summary. For the actual workflow, check the GDC Vault recording if you have access, or Thiger's later Substance Designer tutorials. One of those, a roof tile tutorial, uses newer nodes from Substance Designer 2019.1 and covers creating a roof tile, starting from breaking down references, so it's a reasonable proxy for his general method, though it isn't the GDC talk.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1cc2d738-0e84-41f4-94e0-3ce2805228a0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:21.231Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bc0109e8-2f40-44af-a2f2-947cda776d25","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null