{"parentUuid":"2048a6ff-f04e-4443-a439-96629c5b5cfb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015rSfjZCXEUCsQp8iX7ZrjM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance Designer procedural wood planks height breakdown 80.lv wood grain tile sampler warp slope blur\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Hi! 👋 The owner of this website is looking for a job or freelance work. He does software development and design:\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgbookcase.com/learn/immersion-vr-substance-designer-material-breakdowns\"},{\"title\":\"How to Create a Procedural Material in Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://discover.therookies.co/2019/04/04/how-to-create-a-procedural-material-in-substance-designer/\"},{\"title\":\"how to create a procedural material in substance designer\",\"url\":\"https://blog.therookies.co/2019/04/04/how-to-create-a-procedural-material-in-substance-designer/\"},{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLEBeginner20 min\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-designer/web/mark-foreman-s-substance-3d-designer-tips-and-tricks\"},{\"title\":\"Wooden Floor\",\"url\":\"https://gamesartist.co.uk/wooden-floor/\"},{\"title\":\"Hi everyone,\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2309969\"},{\"title\":\"Visual Immersion\",\"url\":\"https://visualimmersionaliced.myblog.arts.ac.uk/?p=122\"},{\"title\":\"deep dive the first architecture selection update\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/products/substance3d/magazine/deep-dive-the-first-architecture-selection-update.html\"},{\"title\":\"stwshop.gumroad.com\",\"url\":\"https://stwshop.gumroad.com/l/BFNtI\"}]\n\nI didn't find the 80.lv article in these results, so I can't confirm its specific settings. The results do cover the same workflow (tile-based planks, slope blur, warp, and grain height), mostly from other sources.\n\n**Planks and slope blur**\n- A Polycount user says they make the planks with a tile generator, then chip the edges with slope blurs, and then build the grain on top. [cite 6-9]\n- A Games Artist wooden floor breakdown uses a Tile Sampler to scatter knot shapes, then deforms them with Warp and blends in knots through a mask. [cite 5-5, 5-6]\n- That same breakdown describes a knot stack made from a Bell shape, Gradient Dynamic, then Slope Blur and Warp. [cite 5-7]\n\n**Warp and grain height**\n- Mark Foreman's Adobe tutorial squashes and stretches gradients around forms in the wood base, which brings out grain rings around knots. [cite 4-1]\n- He then runs a Directional Warp over the wood heightmap along the grain so the rings follow it slightly. [cite 4-6]\n- For fibers, he uses Directional Noise 2 through a Non Uniform Blur, and prefers that over a Directional Blur because the latter smooths too much. [cite 4-3, 4-5]\n\n**Height and blend**\n- One blog overlays a wood texture's height map onto a tile-generated plank base, then adds slope blur and Perlin-driven warp to break up the grain. [cite 7-3, 7-5]\n- An architecture-focused Substance Brick breakdown notes that the slope of the brick matters a lot, and that shifting the gradient angle can crush gray values. [cite 8-4, 8-6]\n\n**Gaps:** None of these sources gives specific numeric values for height, warp strength, or slope blur amount. For those, check the 80.lv article directly or the graph file if one is linked. If you want, I can run one more search for the 80.lv article by its title.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"93867089-a274-43b9-b871-3890f074396f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:34:42.141Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"448362a9-fa0f-4b3a-892f-5a7472281f94","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","