{"parentUuid":"857e8d56-52d7-4b13-944c-c3a4bb756439","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8whKR6wmmJFxYxG9bWe6h","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Javier Perez \"River Bed\" Substance Designer tutorial pebbles tile sampler height\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"learnsquared.com\",\"url\":\"https://learnsquared.com/courses/substance-designer-essentials/1?video=2740\"},{\"title\":\"building riverstones bed in substance designer\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/building-riverstones-bed-in-substance-designer\"},{\"title\":\"building riverstones bed in substance designer\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/building-riverstones-bed-in-substance-designer/?amp=1\"},{\"title\":\"Learn for Free\",\"url\":\"https://www.learnsquared.com/courses/substance-designer-essentials/1?video=2714\"},{\"title\":\"javier perez takes you to space\",\"url\":\"https://adobe.com/products/substance3d/magazine/javier-perez-takes-you-to-space.html\"},{\"title\":\"You are here\",\"url\":\"https://www.learnsquared.com/courses/substance-designer-essentials/1\"},{\"title\":\"tile sampler\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/texture-generators/patterns/tile-sampler.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2661842\"},{\"title\":\"River Pebbles\",\"url\":\"https://gamesartist.co.uk/river-pebbles/\"}]\n\nI couldn't find a Javier Perez \"River Bed\" tutorial, so I can't tell you what height settings he uses for pebbles. The closest matches are below.\n\n- **Javier Perez's Substance Designer course:** His Learn Squared course, Substance Designer Essentials, covers the basics and the Tile Sampler node. By the end of this Lesson you will have created your own set of bricks or concrete tiles. The results mention no river bed or pebble lesson, and I didn't find any tile sampler height values.\n- **A river bed tutorial by someone else:** On 80.lv, Shray Khanna created a great tutorial, which shows how you can build a wonderful river bed material in Substance Designer. Its height map section lists stones of different sizes, mud, pebbles, leaves, plants, twigs, moss and water puddles as separate layers that get blended together. That matches the pebble workflow you're after, though it isn't Javier's tutorial.\n- **Pebbles and tile samplers in general:** One artist describes a pebble-style workflow in which the 'Rock Sampler' node can take a mask-input, which prevent rocks and pebbles from being generated in the masked areas. That's a forum post, not a tutorial, and it doesn't give height values.\n\nTo find the exact tile sampler height settings, try searching Javier Perez's YouTube channel or Adobe Substance 3D community pages for a river or pebble video. If you can open one of his videos, the height values will be in the tile sampler node's parameters or the graph view.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6f3f6df6-f34c-4e81-a7c5-cf4fd6148fa7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:35:45.797Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2515debc-7e3d-4926-911f-b735c685c2ec","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"857e8d56-52d7-4b13-944c-c3a4bb756439","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c4e43eda-48d0-4ded-a21b-bb8738a0ef78","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SAyssEcnkEyMTPfzTVfbpi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Javier Perez Substance Designer GDC talk OR \"Substance Days\" OR podcast materials workflow height map reads hallway sci-fi\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Division 2 A World\",\"url\":\"https://gdcvault.com/play/1026142/The-Division-2-A-World\"},{\"title\":\"Session Name: | The Division 2: A World of Materials (Presented by Substance) |\",\"url\":\"https://gdcvault.com/play/1026142/contactUs\"},{\"title\":\"Monday, October 8th, 2018 Posted by Jim Thacker\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgchannel.com/?p=97672\"},{\"title\":\"www.viewconference.it\",\"url\":\"https://www.viewconference.it/article/501\"},{\"title\":\"ArtStation Learning: Learn How to Create a Sci-Fi Environment in Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://magazine.artstation.com/2020/03/artstationlearning-msi-environmentsubstancedesigner/\"},{\"title\":\"blog.learnsquared.com\",\"url\":\"https://blog.learnsquared.com/tag/substance/\"},{\"title\":\"Rocks & Forest: Creating Realistic Terrain in Substance Designer\",\"url\":\"https://www.viewconference.it/article/501/creating-realistic-terrain-in-substance-designer?amphtml=1\"},{\"title\":\"blog.learnsquared.com\",\"url\":\"https://blog.learnsquared.com/tag/tlou2/\"},{\"title\":\"blog.learnsquared.com\",\"url\":\"https://blog.learnsquared.com/category/interviews/page/3/\"},{\"title\":\"Log inBy Category\",\"url\":\"https://origin.thegnomonworkshop.com/blog/substance-day-los-angeles-2018\"}]\n\nI found a sci-fi hallway series by Javier Perez that matches your description, but no GDC talk or podcast by him that covers this workflow.\n\n**Sci-fi hallway series (ArtStation Learning):** A six-part series that walks through building a sci-fi hallway in Substance Designer. It starts with the height information for each of the five pieces that make up the hallway. From there, it covers techniques and workflows to efficiently take the height information and create the remaining texture maps that are combined into final materials. The series was sponsored by MSI, and the ArtStation Learning article links to where you can watch it.\n\n**GDC:** The only GDC reference I found is a bio saying he has shared his Substance Designer knowledge at various industry events including GDC and Gnomon. I didn't find the title or date of a specific GDC talk. The GDC Vault result I found, \"The Division 2: A World of Materials,\" is by different speakers (Andrew Dixon and Jon Lauf), so it's not his.\n\n**Substance Day and Gnomon:** At Substance Day Los Angeles 2018, Javier Perez will reveal his workflow, tips, and tricks as he walks through his process for creating a Viking axe in Substance Designer. That was a masterclass, not a hallway talk.\n\n**Podcast:** I found a Learn Squared podcast-style interview about his path into material art, but the search snippet didn't include anything about hallway or height-map workflows.\n\nHis background, per the sources: he has contributed to multiple AAA projects such as Call of Duty: Infinite Warfare, Metal Gear Solid V: The Phantom Pain, Lawbreakers, and Planetside 2. A more recent bio says his most recent work can be seen in The Last of Us Part 2.\n\nIf you want the GDC talk or podcast specifically, search GDC Vault directly for his name, or check the Learn Squared podcast archive.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"92c1712e-9c43-42d8-8874-e790a875f3f2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:35:46.799Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2515debc-7e3d-4926-911f-b735c685c2ec","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"