{"parentUuid":"7145d237-fc38-4f00-b76d-d8f616468145","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014JFZXd8oqR3TPisizoEXXh","type":"tool_result","content":"**Height map node workflow (paraphrased):**\n\n1. **Shapes:** Start with a disk-shaped base. Add a multi-directional warp and Perlin noise, plus a subtle white-to-black noise range, to mimic stones abraded from different angles. Lowering the Output Size blurs the texture. A slope blur using the Clouds 2 filter at 32 x 512 adds further variation.\n2. **Flood fill:** Create three randomized gradients with flood fill and combine them using the min darken blend mode. Layer the result over the smooth stones to restore sharp, unworn edges.\n3. **Scatter:** Build six tile samplers, from large stones to small. Each one is a duplicate of the first with a different random seed and adjusted X/Y amounts. Moisture noise feeds the scale and color map inputs for subtle variation.\n4. **Mask input and height blend:** Mask the stones already placed, add a slight bevel, and connect the result to the next tile sampler's mask map input so stones don't overlap. Blend the layers with height blend nodes. Minor intersections may remain.\n\nNote that the article calls these \"tile samplers,\" not \"Rock Sampler.\""}]},"uuid":"03825944-2989-4541-ad85-3fe21ac7c193","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:35:59.742Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2de065bb-5be2-46e9-bdaf-fec327f6ca32","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":26,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7145d237-fc38-4f00-b76d-d8f616468145","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c85e111f-abe4-474a-935b-760e118ea31d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJLw4pwjeFUt6xPw3ozScn","type":"tool_result","content":"**Substance Day at Gnomon (Los Angeles, October 17, 2018)**\n\nThe evening was a Substance-focused event with talks, masterclasses, and networking.\n\n**Schedule**\n\n- **7:00 pm, Welcome address:** Allegorithmic founder and CEO Sébastien Deguy discusses what's next for the Substance suite.\n- **7:30 pm, Substance Designer masterclass:** Javier Perez, a senior material artist at Intrepid Studios, walks through building a Viking axe.\n- **8:30 pm, Substance Painter masterclass:** Blair Armitage, a character artist at Riot Games, explains how she texturing a character project, a Tifa Lockhart design updated with new elements to tie in with the upcoming Final Fantasy VII remake and the Final Fantasy XV character team's work.\n- **9:30 pm, Meet and greet:** Networking with other Substance users.\n\n**Javier Perez's masterclass**\n\n- **Focus:** Creating a Viking axe in Substance Designer.\n- **Content:** He shows his process from start to finish and shares his workflow and techniques.\n- **Specific tips:** The page doesn't list individual techniques or steps, so the details would only be available in the session itself.\n\n**Other speakers and topics**\n\n- **Sébastien Deguy:** Allegorithmic founder and CEO. Topic: the future direction of Substance.\n- **Blair Armitage:** Character artist at Riot Games. Topic: texturing a updated Tifa Lockhart character in Substance Painter.\n\nThe page also promotes Gnomon's full-time programs, 10-week courses, and online classes for artists outside the US."}]},"uuid":"eebd01e0-b88a-49bb-8ea5-e5c7c695f318","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:36:00.173Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2de065bb-5be2-46e9-bdaf-fec327f6ca32","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":26,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c85e111f-abe4-474a-935b-760e118ea31d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"61480b40-de0b-4356-b477-6e8622eae736","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VvnWmTipgHVS9vvQwcW8s7","type":"tool_result","content":"**Artist:** Shray Khanna\n\n**Height map node workflow (paraphrased):**\n\n1. **Large boulders:** A Distance node feeds a randomized Tile Sampler to create irregular shapes. Edge Detect separates them, and Flood Fill adds gradient and random brightness for varied angles and heights. Blur HQ softens the transition to the ground.\n2. **Medium stones:** The boulder mask and normal map drive a second Tile Sampler, which places warped, non-uniformly blurred round shapes into the gaps. A Slope Blur breaks up the repetition.\n3. **Layering:** Height Blend combines the base forms with the large stones, controlling depth without masks or clipping.\n4. **Surface detail:** A light Slope Blur adds undulation, and a faint Multi-directional Warp adds fine grain. Quantize Grayscale with Slope Blur adds layering. Two more stone sets, each from its own Tile Sampler, are blended in with Height Blend.\n5. **Mud:** Two cell patterns, slope-blurred Gaussian noise, and a BnW Spots 2 pass build the base. An inverted stone mask, warped with Non-directional Warps, makes the mud appear to creep up from below.\n6. **Pebbles:** A Tile Sampler scatters small stones from a custom generator. Height Blend ties them to the mud's undulation.\n7. **Moss:** Built from curvature and normal-derived masks, combined with a Dirt mask and Cells 2 for placement on the mud and a few boulders.\n8. **Leaves, plants, twigs, puddles:** Leaves and plants are scattered with Tile Samplers. Histogram Scan and Dirt shape the leaves' deterioration. Twigs are scattered and blended with Height Blend. Puddles come from Creased, Gaussian Noise, and Grunge Map 005, warped and range-limited, then blended into the lowest crevices.\n\nA Height to Normals node then generates the normal map.\n\n**Notes:** The article doesn't mention Splatter, so I've described the scattering as Tile Sampler-based only. It also doesn't give specific node values or slider settings."}]},"uuid":"61acbebf-5aa8-4442-bffd-8628b0e04261","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:36:02.210Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2de065bb-5be2-46e9-bdaf-fec327f6ca32","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":26,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61480b40-de0b-4356-b477-6e8622eae736","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
