{"parentUuid":"81c37d78-eee8-4f9b-9044-65f1c59ab27e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013RqKyFK3AUr9s2patKTWFT","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **mono:** The source mono layer. The node computes distances from an isocontour of this layer.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **sdf:** A signed distance field showing the distance to an isocontour of the mono input.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Iso:** Sets the threshold that marks the boundary of the distance field.\n- **Invert:** Flips the sign of the result. By default, values above the iso level count as inside (negative distance), and values below count as outside (positive distance).\n- **Iterations:** Controls how many passes the solver makes. One pass is enough for a uniform speed field. Complex speed variation may need more passes for distances to fully propagate.\n- **Tile Size:** Sets the size of the blocks the layer is split into, which balances serial and parallel work. It shouldn't change the result once the solve has converged, and the defaults should usually be fine.\n\nThe page doesn't list a \"method\" parameter, so I haven't described one."}]},"uuid":"ab122345-a20e-496c-9ea6-6e9e828d4667","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:49.065Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55641498-c074-41c4-802e-059634967cea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81c37d78-eee8-4f9b-9044-65f1c59ab27e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8470a6e6-874f-4973-bf01-71427440c2b6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CEdR1CAEaBb9cYn9tNU4xC","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **A:** The layer, VDB, or attribute being compared.\n- **B:** The layer, VDB, or attribute it's compared against. It can be any type convertible to A's type.\n- **tolerance:** A mono input that sets a tolerance for each pixel.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **mask:** A mono result from 0 to 1. It is 1 where the comparison holds and 0 where it doesn't.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets which layer type the source accepts.\n- **Comparison Value:** A constant to compare against when B isn't connected. It's checked against each channel of A.\n- **Tolerance:** Widens the test. For equality, the tolerance applies on both sides of the value. For strict inequalities, it applies on one side. Pixels within the tolerance get a soft mask value instead of a hard 0 or 1.\n- **True If (operators):** Chooses the condition that produces a 1:\n  - Equal (==) or not equal (!=) to each other.\n  - A greater than B (>) or greater than or equal to B (>=).\n  - B greater than A (<) or greater than or equal to A (<=).\n- **Components:** For multi-channel data like RGB or UV, decides whether the mask requires all channels to pass (True if All) or just one (True if Any).\n- **Falloff:** Controls how pixels that fail the test but fall within the tolerance fade out:\n  - None: a hard cutoff.\n  - Linear: a straight fade from 1 to 0.\n  - Elendt: an S-shaped fade that eases in and out."}]},"uuid":"b77a2d0a-f1d7-43fb-ade7-b6a04c5fd945","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:49.912Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55641498-c074-41c4-802e-059634967cea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8470a6e6-874f-4973-bf01-71427440c2b6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"fd203d3c-6ebd-4cff-991c-5938fd7eeb45","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YaZoEZQ377Z3bVec6XyGXR","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs and outputs**\n- **Input:** One source layer. The **Signature** parameter sets which layer type the source accepts.\n- **Output:** The page doesn't describe the output.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Blends the quantized result with the original. A value of 1 uses only the quantized value, and lower values mix in more of the original.\n- **Method:** Chooses how step size is set. *Width and Offset* sets the spacing directly. *Number of Segments* sets the total number of levels.\n- **Segments:** The number of quantization levels when using *Number of Segments*. For example, 3 gives levels at 0, 0.5, and 1.\n- **Width:** The spacing between levels, as a fraction of the 0–1 range. A width of 0.1 gives 11 levels.\n- **Offset:** Shifts where the levels fall. An offset of 0.05 with a width of 0.1 places levels at 0.05, 0.15, 0.25, and so on.\n- **Rounding:** Determines which level a value snaps to.\n  - *Floor* snaps down to the nearest level at or below the value.\n  - *Closest* snaps to the nearest level.\n  - *Ceiling* snaps up to the nearest level at or above the value.\n  - *Custom* uses the Rounding Threshold to decide the cutoff.\n- **Rounding Threshold:** Used with *Custom* rounding. It sets how far a value must be toward the upper level before it snaps up. Values of 0, 0.5, and 1 behave like Floor, Closest, and Ceiling.\n- **Compute Range:** Fills Minimum Value and Maximum Value from the input's actual minimum and maximum.\n- **Minimum Value / Maximum Value:** With *Number of Segments*, these define the range that gets divided into the segment count.\n- **Clamp Below / Clamp Above:** When enabled, clamp input values to the minimum or maximum before quantizing.\n\n**Dithering:** The page doesn't mention dithering or any dithering parameter."}]},"uuid":"328c2e66-9a65-429a-a84c-17cfefbc2067","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:50.795Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55641498-c074-41c4-802e-059634967cea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd203d3c-6ebd-4cff-991c-5938fd7eeb45","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"660c6114-6f9e-4991-9485-5d5d8d36b895","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01467bHaaQq5rHFxxcKZSinj","type":"tool_result","content":"**UV Sample parameters**\n\n- **Signature:** The layer type the source accepts.\n- **UV Space:** Sets the range the UV input must use.\n  - *Texture* uses 0 to 1 across the input's data window, which suits latitude/longitude maps.\n  - *Image* uses -1 to 1 across the display window, which keeps square pixels and ignores cropping or overscan.\n- **Filter Scale:** Controls anti-aliasing. It defaults to the voxel size and can be raised or lowered to match the UV map. Attributes have no intrinsic filter size, so you usually need to set it manually.\n- **Filter:** The sampling method. The default is Box.\n\n**UV Sample inputs**\n\n- **uv:** The UV layer or attribute that supplies the coordinates. It also sets the output's resolution and metadata.\n- **filterscale:** An optional per-pixel multiplier for Filter Scale. It's needed because UV maps can have seams that prevent the node from detecting the rate of change.\n- **texture:** The mono, UV, RGB, or RGBA input to sample.\n\n**Output**\n\n- **sample:** The UV layer or attribute, with each pixel set to the matching value from the texture input.\n\n**Not covered on this page**\n\nThe page doesn't mention a border parameter, a scale value from uvscale, or a center input for Cellular Noise. It also doesn't describe per-island workflows directly.\n\n**Per-island use (inferred)**\n\nUV Map by ID creates a UV map for each connected ID island, and the page lists it as a related node. Since UV Sample takes any UV layer on its uv input, you could likely feed it a UV Map by ID output to sample a texture per island. The page doesn't confirm this workflow. It also doesn't say how Cellular Noise connects to UV Sample. It only describes Cellular Noise as generating cellular noise."}]},"uuid":"5ed7a9cf-af45-48d0-9f28-072e468706ee","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:50.966Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55641498-c074-41c4-802e-059634967cea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"660c6114-6f9e-4991-9485-5d5d8d36b895","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"37c6e4f1-3e73-47ee-a6fa-f359e357462b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HE8SP92eLEoVwKJVAdbWWc","type":"tool_result","content":"**Compare and Blend** blends between two inputs on a per-pixel basis by comparing values in A and B.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **true:** The layer, VDB, or attribute whose pixels are used where the comparison passes.\n- **false:** The layer, VDB, or attribute whose pixels are used where the comparison fails.\n- **A:** The first value in the comparison.\n- **B:** The value A is compared against.\n- **tolerance:** An optional mono input that sets the tolerance separately for each pixel.\n\n**Output**\n- **chosen:** The result, mixing the true and false inputs according to each pixel's comparison result.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** The layer type the node accepts (layer, VDB, or attribute).\n- **True If:** The comparison operator that decides when a pixel counts as true:\n  - Equal (==) or Not equal (!=)\n  - A greater than B (>) or A greater than or equal to B (>=)\n  - A less than B (<) or A less than or equal to B (<=)\n- **B Value:** A fallback constant used for B when nothing is wired into B.\n- **Bias:** Pushes borderline results toward the true or false input.\n- **Tolerance:** A margin around the comparison point where pixels get a partial, soft mask value instead of a hard true or false. It applies on both sides for equality checks and on one side for strict inequalities.\n- **Falloff:** Controls how the soft mask fades for pixels that fail the test but fall within the tolerance:\n  - None: a hard cutoff with no fade.\n  - Linear: a straight fade from 1 to 0.\n  - Elendt: an S-shaped fade that eases in and out.\n\nNote that the documentation names these controls \"Tolerance\" and \"Falloff.\" It doesn't list parameters called \"threshold\" or \"soft width,\" so Tolerance and Falloff are the closest equivalents."}]},"uuid":"810fa04a-a7d3-4ad6-a1fd-721eb26a4f83","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:38:51.792Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55641498-c074-41c4-802e-059634967cea","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"37c6e4f1-3e73-47ee-a6fa-f359e357462b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
