{"parentUuid":"ee96ff79-b21e-43a1-8236-b3ae7ab6f7f7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YFkjaVT4oUPYUza9sJ6nwk","type":"tool_result","content":"The excerpt only covers the basics. A Fill effect works like a Fill Layer, but you apply it as an effect on a layer or a mask. This lets you build more complex materials or masks within a single layer.\n\nThe excerpt doesn't describe the modes (uniform color, procedural, bitmap), the projection types (UV, triplanar, planar), the anchor point, or any height-related parameters. Those details would need to come from the full documentation page."}]},"uuid":"75656d95-8c78-47ac-8280-4a75cd7c98a6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:01.670Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a0376eb5-ab5b-4892-a0c5-67c2d90f5c7f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee96ff79-b21e-43a1-8236-b3ae7ab6f7f7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"30cde11a-8bc1-4184-8cc6-57471ba7bab2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pw8sav1XMfEzV73FA6Tzx9","type":"tool_result","content":"The Compare Mask effect builds a mask by comparing two channels, a source and a target, and outputs white where the comparison holds. It works only on Mask on Layers.\n\n- **Channel:** Picks which texture channel to compare. The options come from the Texture Set settings.\n- **Compare:** Sets where each side of the comparison gets its data. The source or target can be the flattened layers below, the current layer alone, the layer's existing mask content (such as a Fill or Generator effect), or a constant value.\n- **Operation:** The middle dropdown chooses how the sides are tested. The source can be lower than, within tolerance of, or higher than the target.\n- **Constant:** The value used when a side is set to constant.\n- **Hardness:** Controls how soft or sharp the resulting mask edges are.\n- **Histogram:** Shows the value distribution of both sides. If they don't overlap, the mask will be empty.\n\nFor combining with generators, the page notes that the \"This Mask\" option can read a mask that already contains a Generator effect, so the comparison can refine generated content. Right-clicking a layer and choosing \"Add mask with height combination\" adds this effect and switches the Height channel's blending mode to Normal, which is the default for that workflow.\n\nThe page doesn't cover Blur, Invert, or a separate Mode setting, so I can't describe those from this content."}]},"uuid":"055c577b-e602-4cb2-b2bf-205f34ae6ae1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:02.755Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a0376eb5-ab5b-4892-a0c5-67c2d90f5c7f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30cde11a-8bc1-4184-8cc6-57471ba7bab2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c6e33c8f-efc4-4a59-8f1a-68a647595887","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UwQ4JcHR8R99GV8Wqskw2Y","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't cover masks or the parameters you listed (Input min/max, Output min/max, Invert, Gamma), so I can't describe those from it. It does describe the Levels effect's core controls:\n\n- **Histogram:** Shows how pixels are spread across dark, mid, and bright tones, which helps you judge overall brightness and tonal range.\n- **Top controls:** Three handles for shadows, midtones, and highlights. Moving them redistributes the tones to add contrast.\n- **Bottom controls:** Black and white points, which set the endpoints of the tonal range. Pushing them past each other can invert the image.\n- **Affected Channel:** Applies the adjustment to the full RGB image or to one of the red, green, or blue channels. Adjusting several channels independently requires separate Levels effects.\n- **Clamp:** Limits values to the standard range. Keep it on for non-HDR channels such as Base Color.\n\nFor the parameters you asked about, check the Substance 3D Painter documentation or the Substance Academy course on Levels linked from the page."}]},"uuid":"2918de19-d488-4031-8f39-858a47e22046","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:03.693Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a0376eb5-ab5b-4892-a0c5-67c2d90f5c7f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6e33c8f-efc4-4a59-8f1a-68a647595887","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-9