{"parentUuid":"8e20f8cf-ec53-413f-baad-604d46735d5a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GkEB7Y57LZbrMCqV51MpuW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance Painter anchor point reference height channel layer \"anchor point\" texture set channel which channel Fill layer source anchor how it works\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Anchor point\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-dev/painter-python/api/substancepainter-package/layerstack-module/layers-and-effects/anchorpoint\"},{\"title\":\"experienceleague.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-dev/painter-python/api/substancepainter-package/source-module/reference\"},{\"title\":\"TUTORIAL ARTICLEAdvanced9 min\",\"url\":\"https://www.adobe.com/learn/substance-3d-painter/web/substance-painter-peeled-paint-effect\"},{\"title\":\"anchor point\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-painter/features/effects/anchor-point.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2574380/\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2574764\"},{\"title\":\"anchor points return as a solid black mask in material channels 1629471\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/bug-reports-58/anchor-points-return-as-a-solid-black-mask-in-material-channels-1629471\"},{\"title\":\"Anchor Point\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/anchor-point\"},{\"title\":\"evermotion.org\",\"url\":\"https://evermotion.org/tutorials/show/10767/oldest\"},{\"title\":\"substance painter\",\"url\":\"https://garagefarm.net/blog-es/substance-painter\"}]\n\nAnchor points let one layer's content feed other parts of the stack, and the Fill layer is one of the places they can be referenced. I didn't find a single page that walks through choosing a channel for an anchor, so the channel behavior below comes from the API reference and community reports.\n\n**What an anchor point is**\nAn anchor point exposes a layer or element so other parts of the stack can reference it, each with its own adjustments. Anchor Points are available in the Effects menu. They can be added on both layers and masks. You can create an anchor point from your layer by right-clicking it and selecting \"Add anchor point\".\n\n**How a Fill layer uses one**\nA referencing layer instantiates the anchor point's content into itself. Anchor Points can be used as a reference in a Fill Layer, a Fill Effect, or the input of a substance filter. In the Fill layer's source, you pick the anchor from the \"anchor points\" tab of the material/mask picker, as the Adobe peeled-paint tutorial does with its fill effect.\n\n**Ordering and limits**\n- Only Anchor Points which are below the layer referencing it can be used as references. Moving an anchor above its referencing layer will break the reference.\n- An anchor point can only be referenced inside the texture set it was created in. Creating links between an anchor and its references is not possible across Texture Sets.\n- The best practice is to put it at the bottom of the layer stack.\n\n**Which channel is used**\nThe API reference describes a \"multi-channel context\" for a reference, where a `channel_mapping` property controls how channels are matched. Its example maps, for instance, Base Color to Metallic and Roughness to Height. Reading the mapping raises an error if the reference is not in a multi-channel context. So the reference's channel mapping, not a separate anchor setting, decides which source channel feeds each destination channel. A `referenced_channel` property also exists for single-channel references, but the snippet cuts off before describing it.\n\nIf you want a grayscale height-style result to drive the Height channel, the practical route is to reference the anchor from the Fill layer's Height channel. I could not confirm from these results whether the UI exposes the same mapping directly, so check the Fill layer's channel options in your version.\n\n**Known issues**\n- A Polycount thread reported that if you create the anchor point from the fill layer, the generators read the value of the fill layer without the mask. Creating it from the mask instead gave only the alpha of the mask. That thread is older and about generators.\n- A June 2026 Adobe community report says that after updating from 12.0.3 to 12.1.0, anchor points coming from a mask could only be reused inside another mask. The same post says anchor points placed on a Fill Layer or Paint Layer still work correctly both in masks and in Fill Layers/material channels. If a grayscale mask anchor goes black in a material channel, anchoring from a Fill or Paint layer is the workaround that user found.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a28c28b2-dd35-4519-8fa8-e239beb03ec7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:17.892Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7a358085-1eaa-4d2a-9371-b1b4ec2327a4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e20f8cf-ec53-413f-baad-604d46735d5a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
