{"parentUuid":"918aa404-d338-4ef1-afac-dff608f731de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQrZpoAzQv7viwo3hHJLF9","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer or VDB to sharpen.\n- **size:** An optional per-pixel amount that scales the **Size** parameter.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel amount that scales the **Mask** parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **filter:** The sharpened layer or VDB.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the new value blends with the original. The default of 1 uses only the new value.\n- **Units:** Chooses whether the sharpen radius is measured in image space or pixels.\n- **Read Pixels outside Image:** Includes pixels beyond the image edges, based on the border type.\n- **Size:** Sets the sharpen radius. Larger values give crisper results, and smaller values soften the effect.\n- **Scale Size:** Scales the sharpen radius.\n- **Amplitude:** Sets how strongly the blurred mask is applied to the original. Higher values sharpen more.\n- **Gain:** Multiplies the original brightness. Setting it to 0 with a positive Amplitude creates a high-pass filter.\n- **Threshold:** Sets the minimum pixel difference needed before sharpening occurs. Higher values help avoid sharpening high-frequency noise."}]},"uuid":"76e7e4df-05c9-4012-b167-ad19b51a1baa","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:56.390Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"918aa404-d338-4ef1-afac-dff608f731de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"03675161-a385-44cc-b43d-7418910965b5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLHyysG16QKer9YAZVsvDJ","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** A reference layer that sets the output image size and controls the metadata.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **pos:** An RGB layer or Vector VDB holding the 3D coordinates of each pixel.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Source Position:** Chooses the position used per pixel: world-space location, camera origin, or view direction (a normalized vector pointing away from the camera).\n- **X, Y, Z Border:** Controls how coordinates outside the canonical cube (sides of size 2) are remapped. Options are Clamp (snap to the nearest side), Mirror (reflect at the boundary), Wrap (use the opposite side), and Extend (leave values unchanged).\n- **X, Y, Z Shift:** Adds an offset to the coordinates before border correction.\n- **X, Y, Z Cycles:** Scales the coordinates before border correction. With Wrap, this acts as a cycle count.\n\n**Use**\nThe Position Map generates a reference layer in which each pixel stores a location in 3D space. Noise nodes such as Fractal Noise 3D can use it as their reference positions. The border, shift, and cycle settings control how those values repeat or wrap, which helps create periodic patterns."}]},"uuid":"c2fa5e4f-8a36-4715-96cf-089c023cf772","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:56.950Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"03675161-a385-44cc-b43d-7418910965b5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason