{"parentUuid":"983c93b5-b784-4388-a379-d59694fef921","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFtWAt6YL55K6dWkYEg26f","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't describe an anisotropic option, a sharpness parameter, or a direction parameter, so I can't cover those. Here are the inputs, outputs, and parameters it does describe.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer the filter is applied to.\n- **radius:** An optional per-pixel map that scales the filter size, multiplied by the Radius parameter.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel map that scales the Mask amount.\n\n**Output**\n- **blur:** The filtered layer.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the filtered value replaces the original. The default of 1 uses only the filtered value.\n- **Method:** Chooses how the filter is computed. Approximate precomputes the statistics in one pass, which is faster but varies the effective radius. Exact computes each pixel directly, which is costlier but more accurate. Large kernels get expensive either way.\n- **Luminance:** Sets the brightness measure used to pick the smoothest of the four regions. Options include several weighted luminance formulas, average, max or min channel, vector magnitude, HSV hue, saturation, or value, and single channel extraction. When there are multiple channels, the same region is chosen for all of them.\n- **Radius:** Sets the size in pixels of the four sampling regions. It also offsets them so they don't overlap.\n- **Blur Scale:** Scales the size of each region used for averaging. Lower values keep the result sharper, and higher values add blur without changing which region is picked.\n- **Blend to Blur:** At 0, the output comes from the smoothest region. At 1, the output averages the region averages, which gives a larger blur. In-between values weight the regions by their standard deviation.\n- **Separation:** Scales how far apart the four regions sit. At 0, all regions sample the same spot, which makes a box blur. Values above 1 pull the regions toward distant parts of the image."}]},"uuid":"6fd96f58-e84c-41a9-9223-41b710cfaa4f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:57.077Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"983c93b5-b784-4388-a379-d59694fef921","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4e5381e2-865e-4568-b977-22ba6a603a37","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TK5CrAtfoKdv2aL91E8b3y","type":"tool_result","content":"**Layer Merge (Average) COP**\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source:** Accepts the layers, VDBs, or attributes to combine. All inputs must share the same Signature type. If an input differs, Houdini automatically converts it to the required type using channel extension rules, based on the Signature parameter or the first input.\n\n**Output**\n- **combine:** The merged result of all source inputs.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the node accepts.\n- **Space:** Determines how pixels in different inputs are matched:\n  - *Image:* Matches by 2D canvas coordinates, ignoring 3D transforms.\n  - *Texture:* Stretches data windows so the layers overlap exactly.\n  - *Pixel:* Matches display windows so pixels stay the same size, offset by the data window.\n  - *World:* Projects the foreground onto the background using the background's camera, like the 3D viewport.\n- **Border:** Controls sampling outside an input's edges. Auto uses the layer's own border setting, except that a Constant border on the input is treated as Clip.\n- **Filter:** Sets the sampling method used to read the image.\n- **Operation:** Sets how pixel values are combined, per channel:\n  - *Add:* Sums the values.\n  - *Average:* Takes the mean of the values.\n  - *Multiply:* Multiplies the values together.\n  - *Min:* Keeps the lowest value.\n  - *Max:* Keeps the highest value.\n  - *Over:* Composites earlier RGBA inputs over later ones. Non-RGBA layers copy the last layer's pixels.\n  - *Clip by Data Window:* Applies a hard mask matching the foreground's data window, so the image doesn't spill into the destination.\n  - *Crop to Content:* Crops the output to the combined transformed data windows of the sources."}]},"uuid":"fc58fed3-0463-41c8-9034-addec18aa5e6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:58.121Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e5381e2-865e-4568-b977-22ba6a603a37","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"95904554-2e90-412a-bae9-55cf39f77c6a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011eZ6RanWXSpJSJTVS29iub","type":"tool_result","content":"## Function COP Node: Inputs, Outputs, and Parameters\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source**: The layer or VDB the function is applied to.\n- **mask** (optional): A per-pixel mask that scales the **Mask** parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **function**: The input with the function applied.\n\n**Common Parameters**\n- **Signature**: Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask**: Controls how much of the new value blends with the original. The default of 1 uses only the new value.\n- **Scale**: Multiplies the incoming layer.\n- **Shift**: Adds a value after the Scale multiplication.\n- **Function Class**: Chooses Arithmetic, Powers, or Trigonometry.\n- **Base**: Used by Modulus, pow(b, x), and Base-Log.\n- **Exponent**: Used by pow(x, E).\n- **Angle Units**: For trig functions, sets whether values are radians, degrees, or circles (2π radians).\n\n**Arithmetic Functions**\n- **Absolute**: Returns each channel's absolute value.\n- **Sign**: Returns -1, 0, or 1 based on whether the value is negative, zero, or positive.\n- **Normalize**: Divides each channel by the vector's magnitude.\n- **Negate**: Multiplies each channel by -1.\n- **Reciprocal**: Returns 1 divided by each channel's value.\n- **Floor**: Rounds down to the nearest integer.\n- **Round**: Rounds to the nearest integer.\n- **Ceil**: Rounds up to the nearest integer.\n- **Modulus**: Returns the fractional part of each value, using Base.\n\n**Power and Log Functions**\n- **Square Root**: Takes the square root of each channel.\n- **pow(x, E)**: Raises each channel to the Exponent.\n- **pow(b, x)**: Raises Base to the power of each channel.\n- **exp(x)**: Raises e to the power of each channel.\n- **Base-Log**: Takes the logarithm of each channel using Base.\n- **Natural Log**: Takes the base-e logarithm of each channel.\n\n**Trigonometric and Hyperbolic Functions**\n- **Sin, Cos, Tan**: Standard trig functions.\n- **Arc Sin, Arc Cos, Arc Tan**: Inverse trig functions.\n- **Hyperbolic Sin, Cos, Tan**: Hyperbolic trig functions.\n- For atan2, the page recommends the UV to Polar COP node.\n\n**Not on this page:** The page doesn't mention **smoothstep** or **fit**, so I can't describe them from this content. Also, the page lists e as 2.17128128, but the correct value is about 2.71828."}]},"uuid":"be69b5a6-b3a9-4438-9881-f319ab3cdba5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:58.925Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"95904554-2e90-412a-bae9-55cf39f77c6a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a22d95e1-0d31-4196-89f9-fd6dedb63207","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X3WdbY8NpVzsNY12n5JJbR","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n\n- **source:** The layer, VDB, or attribute that receives the HSV effect.\n- **hueshift:** An optional per-pixel hue amount, scaled by the Hue Shift Min, Max, and Width settings.\n- **saturation:** An optional per-pixel saturation amount, scaled by Saturation Scale and Saturation Shift.\n- **value:** An optional per-pixel brightness amount, scaled by Value Scale and Value Shift.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel mask, scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Output**\n\n- **hsv_adjust:** The source with the HSV effect applied, as a layer, VDB, or attribute.\n\n**Parameters**\n\n- **Signature:** Sets the data type the source accepts: layer, VDB, or attribute.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the new value blends with the original. The default of 1 uses only the new value.\n- **Operation:** Chooses the mode: adjust hue/saturation/value, convert RGB to HSV, or convert HSV to RGB.\n- **Hue Shift:** Rotates all colors around the hue wheel by a set number of degrees. Grays are unaffected.\n- **Hue Shift Mode:** Determines how a wired hueshift input is applied, either by Min/Max or by Width.\n- **Hue Shift Min:** In Min/Max mode, the rotation applied when the hueshift input is 0. Values in between are interpolated toward the Max.\n- **Hue Shift Max:** In Min/Max mode, the rotation applied when the hueshift input is 1.\n- **Hue Shift Width:** In Width mode, the total degree span that the hueshift input's 0-to-1 range covers, centered on zero.\n- **Keep Luminance:** Preserves perceived brightness when hues change, since some hues look brighter than others.\n- **Saturation Scale:** Multiplies saturation. Values above 1 increase color intensity; values below 1 reduce it.\n- **Saturation Shift:** Adds or subtracts saturation. It's mostly used to reduce saturation, because adding it to gray pixels gives them an arbitrary color.\n- **Value Scale:** Multiplies brightness.\n- **Value Shift:** Adds or subtracts brightness from all pixels.\n- **Treat RGBA as Premultiplied:** Multiplies the red, green, and blue channels by alpha, for inputs already stored that way."}]},"uuid":"5eba40b2-1ef4-4d50-9a49-353992d810f5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:59.466Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9ac4832d-7c9c-4607-a3ef-54aefd7abc41","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a22d95e1-0d31-4196-89f9-fd6dedb63207","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
