otes that the Height Selector isolates pixels in a greyscale heightmap based on their value. He also describes building a Linear Grain node for directional noise, which he warps with Perlin noise to get a wobbly wood grain. The article doesn't give a full step-by-step, so treat it as a summary of his approach rather than a complete tutorial.\n\n**Mosaic tile floor (Sekula):** A Substance Designer community resource list (Scrapbox) lists \"Peter Sekula - Mosaic Tile Floor\" under its tiles section, along with his cypress bark entry. The list is a link collection without a description, so I couldn't confirm the tutorial's format, length, or whether it's free. My searches didn't turn up a page for it.\n\n**Closest alternative:** If you're after a mosaic tile floor tutorial in Substance Designer, Vincent Dérozier's course with Levelup.Digital covers that topic. It's a fully narrated, step-by-step tutorial on how to create Mosaic Tile Flooring. It is listed at $10 on Gumroad and covers 3 hours of video along with a reference breakdown, SVG setup, heightmap and color, and additional tile material. Another option is a Udemy course on mosaic materials with an SVG workflow, which is 3h 15m total length and includes clean SBS files for study purposes, though its videos are unnarrated.\n\nTo find Sekula's mosaic floor tutorial directly, try searching his name with \"ArtStation\" or \"Substance Designer tiles,\" since his cypress bark breakdown was originally posted there.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c18ce9a2-5429-4487-b1dd-2fe3c8f13699","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:41:09.544Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c7922d6e-52be-4177-8944-15ae34e144fe","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":29,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"por