{"parentUuid":"4b017d8b-8d86-4eca-9d18-dca0cc16b280","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013nE2itK7vXToY7NZhXNnrN","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **mono:** The original mono layer to convert.\n- **height:** The resulting heightfield. This is an output, though the page lists it under Inputs.\n\n**Outputs**\nThe page doesn't list outputs separately. The single result is the heightfield, which the page labels \"height.\"\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Height Scale:** Multiplies the height values so they map to the correct world-space positions.\n- **Height Offset:** Shifts the height values by a fixed amount.\n\nThe page doesn't mention grid size or units, so I can't confirm either parameter exists.\n\n**Why it's needed before HeightField COP nodes**\nThe page doesn't say that this node is required before HeightField Erode or other HeightField nodes. It does say the node changes a layer's type info to height and rescales its values into world-space positions. Presumably, HeightField nodes expect that type and scale, so a plain mono layer must be converted first. The page doesn't confirm this.\n\n**Height layer vs. mono layer**\nA mono layer is a generic single-channel image layer. A height layer is the same kind of data, but its type info marks it as height, so Copernicus treats its values as elevations in world space. The page doesn't give a fuller definition of a height layer."}]},"uuid":"7c4ab350-2a52-45b6-9c55-ec430d7b0adf","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:43:31.391Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a9432465-baa5-4819-b8fb-6d89105a5abd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b017d8b-8d86-4eca-9d18-dca0cc16b280","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"12b3b062-9ea8-4510-b21a-922cada96a75","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012gqVAX5oNuWDAYpEd1E4AB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Parameters**\n\n- **Mask:** Sets how much of the clipped result is blended back into the original height.\n- **Compute Range:** Automatically fills Lower Limit and Upper Limit with the input's minimum and maximum heights.\n- **Lower Limit:** When enabled, flattens heights that fall under this floor. You can pick the value with the eyedropper and a viewport click.\n- **Upper Limit:** When enabled, flattens heights that rise above this ceiling. It also supports eyedropper picking.\n- **Clamped Values:** Chooses what clipped pixels become, either the limit itself or a smoothed transition.\n- **Replace with Limit Value:** Snaps clipped pixels to the limit they exceeded, so values past the bounds become the bound.\n- **Soft Clip:** Eases clipped areas into the original terrain over a gradual range instead of a hard edge.\n- **Soft Clip Direction:** Determines which side the smoothing applies to.\n- **Soft Clip Outside Range:** Smooths the transition outside the limits, widening the clipping effect.\n- **Soft Clip Inside Range:** Smooths the transition inside the limits, narrowing the clipping effect.\n- **Soft Clip Range:** Sets the width of the smoothing band between the limit and the original values.\n\n**Inputs**\n\n- **height:** The heightfield to be clipped.\n- **lower:** An optional per-pixel multiplier for the lower limit, letting the floor vary across the layer.\n- **upper:** An optional per-pixel multiplier for the upper limit, letting the ceiling vary across the layer.\n- **mask:** An optional per-pixel map that works with the Mask parameter to control where clipping is applied.\n\n**Outputs**\n\n- **height:** The resulting heightfield after clipping.\n- **lowermask:** A mask showing where the lower limit clipped the terrain.\n- **uppermask:** A mask showing where the upper limit clipped the terrain."}]},"uuid":"0b97b533-8bbd-4a73-8058-7cd4fba26ada","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:43:31.862Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a9432465-baa5-4819-b8fb-6d89105a5abd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"12b3b062-9ea8-4510-b21a-922cada96a75","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
