{"parentUuid":"6dada064-cca6-4199-92bc-6587ce4f3306","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ANLJuAwMH5xKsYAe1fEbv3","type":"tool_result","content":"The overview doesn't explain height layers or a Mono to HeightField step, and it doesn't name specific noise or erosion nodes. It does describe the broader approach.\n\nCopernicus heightfields work with 2D maps rather than the voxel grids used by SOP-based heightfields, which makes them much faster. They also give access to a large set of image-processing tools, many of which run on the GPU. The page presents this as the start of a new approach, with the long-term goal of moving all SOP heightfield functionality into Copernicus. Newer additions mentioned include a strata node, more noise types, boulders, and terrain colorizing.\n\nThe Copernicus version isn't yet a full replacement for SOP-based terrains. It lacks some nodes and isn't optimized for very large images. You can export terrains to SOP space to apply SOP heightfield nodes, or to Solaris for rendering with Karma. The COP-SOP pipeline is still early, and masks may not behave as expected.\n\n**Subpages:**\n\n- **Creation:** [Base terrain](baseterrain.html), [Workflows](workflows.html), [Projection](projection.html), [Terrain recipes](recipes.html)\n- **Masking:** [Masking](masking.html)\n- **Natural effects:** [Erosion](erosion.html), [Slump](slump.html), [Terracing](terracing.html), [Strata](strata.html), [Boulders](boulders.html)\n- **VEX:** [VEX scripts for heightfields](vexsnippets.html)\n- **Colors:** [Terrain colors](colors.html)\n- **Conversion:** [Conversion](conversion.html)"}]},"uuid":"cafcde10-bce9-4368-b744-3a9c5f346adb","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:44:22.011Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"81baa3d4-bddd-437f-8900-34d2f98ff6f8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6dada064-cca6-4199-92bc-6587ce4f3306","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"3c0bc042-947d-42ca-b42f-cc943aae7f28","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PYEtN8ovyBoAxrGLEnHqzX","type":"tool_result","content":"**New in Copernicus (Houdini 22)**\n\n**Heightfields and terrain**\n- New HeightField COPs for building terrain. The Terrains section of the What's new page lists them.\n- Normal to Height COP converts a normal map into a height (displacement) layer.\n- Planar Inflate COP builds a height layer from a 2D signed distance field.\n- Height to Caustics COP and Refract from Height COP work with height layers.\n- Height to Ambient Occlusion and Height to Shadow COPs gained a Space parameter.\n\n**Textures and UVs**\n- Adjacency nodes help with texture seams and can build seamless textures from geometry attributes: Attribute Sample with Adjacency, Distort with Adjacency, Extrapolate with Adjacency, Geometry to Adjacency, and Space Transform with Adjacency.\n- Paint 3D COP paints on layers or UV-mapped geometry (still in beta).\n- UV Shape, UV Inverse, and UDIM Pack COPs are new.\n- Triplanar COPs gained Normal Type and filtering options.\n- File COP includes new test images and a test video.\n\n**Baking**\n- Bake Geometry Textures COP is now version 2.0.\n- Bake Pre-Process COP is new and sets up rays for baking, with a visualization state.\n\n**Grunge maps**\n- 14 new Grunge COPs produce layered-noise patterns: Aurora, Bark Strips, Birch Bark, Drips, Galvanized Steel, Layered Noise, Leaking Streaks, Moisture, Mold Spots, Pine Bark, Rust, Rusty Surface, Sheets, and Wipe Trails.\n\n**Neural and ML**\n- ML Computer Vision Inference COP applies an ONNX model to detect and mask objects.\n- Neural Cellular Automata Core COP evolves cell states over iterations.\n- Neural Cellular Automata Decode COP turns cell states into visible patterns.\n- Neural Layer to Depth (MoGe-2) COP estimates depth, normal, and position maps.\n- Neural Layer to Mask (SAM2) COP creates masks from prompt coordinates.\n- Recipes include ML Train Neural Cellular Automata, Neural Cellular Automata, and Neural Cellular Automata Block."}]},"uuid":"92506205-fbbb-496e-aaaf-0b8b52196a14","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:44:24.439Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"81baa3d4-bddd-437f-8900-34d2f98ff6f8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c0bc042-947d-42ca-b42f-cc943aae7f28","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a1f7bf57-a80b-453a-badc-c8066059f9de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JS22BkFiEV2TwZi5hxvBmL","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't include the node chain or parameter values, so I can't paraphrase those. It only summarizes the tutorial's approach:\n\n- It builds a broken tile texture by varying each tile's position, scale, rotation, and slope.\n- It adds gaps and noise to make the tiles look more realistic.\n- It creates materials for the tiles and the ground.\n- It assembles a simple Solaris scene with a water plane and renders it in Karma XPU.\n- It stresses a procedural workflow so you can adjust and iterate easily.\n\nThe nodes you listed (cellular noise, edge detect, feather, remap, blend, and so on) don't appear on this page, so I can't confirm them. For the actual setup, you'd need the full video tutorial or the project files, which the page says require a newsletter subscription."}]},"uuid":"2c8c26b6-5011-4e3c-9bd2-11f7db651baa","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:44:25.644Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"81baa3d4-bddd-437f-8900-34d2f98ff6f8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1f7bf57-a80b-453a-badc-c8066059f9de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"80471581-46b6-4b32-958e-7cf56bfc7206","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PaqzJ659xbVx1gWJ2ahXQZ","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't cover height maps, slope direction, blur, or remap as Copernicus recipes, so I can't paraphrase those directly. It does have related material on distortion, procedural textures, and pitfalls, which I've summarized below.\n\n**Distort recipes**\n- **Sine ripple:** Build a 2D position in a snippet, offset X by a sine of Y scaled by a small amount, then feed the result into a copinput to warp the image.\n- **Radial chromatic aberration:** Displace coordinates outward by distance from the center, with the effect growing toward the edges. Run each RGB channel through a slightly different strength, then recombine.\n- **Reverse lookup for remapping pixels:** For each output pixel, find the matching position on the source layout and sample that color. Sampling forward instead produces wrong results.\n\n**Procedural texture recipes**\n- **Cellnoise with rotated gradients:** Use the cell center to get a per-cell UV gradient, shift it so the origin sits at the cell middle, rotate it with a quaternion, then shift back. Multiply the result by cellnoise color for randomized flakes or chips.\n- **Scanlines:** Map a sine of Y into a narrow brightness range and multiply it into the color.\n- **Grid generator:** Use modulo on X and Y against a line width to draw lines.\n- **Color ramps:** Run a baked result through a lookup to produce roughness or metalness maps from a ramp.\n- **Normal-based masks:** Use the absolute dot product of the normal with world axes to blend triplanar projections. This is closer to normal-based masking than to true slope direction.\n\n**Edge handling**\n- **Extrapolate boundaries:** Extends colour past UV shell or alpha edges to prevent seam artifacts and fix premultiplied edges. The page recommends it as a single node in place of a manual edge-detect and blur chain.\n\n**Pitfalls**\n- **Signatures:** When a copinput outputs a 4D vector (RGBA), split it back into separate float channels before wiring to RGBA.\n- **Snippets vs. wrangles:** Newer Cops snippets expose global inputs and outputs directly, so you can skip wiring. Older Cops had no wrangle, and you had to use VOP snippets with explicit connections.\n- **Plane indexing:** Image planes in Cops VOPs are referenced by index rather than by name, which is awkward.\n- **Stability:** Older Cops chains could fail to update, show pale pink missing textures, or produce garbled output.\n- **Performance:** Node thumbnails carry a surprising cost, so turn them off in preferences.\n- **Viewport crop:** An accidental Shift-drag crop can look like a bug. Shift plus middle-click clears it.\n- **Live paths:** To reference a Cops output live in SOPs, add `[$F]` to the `op:` path rather than rendering to disk.\n\n**Cheat sheet**\n- Use `op:` before a node path to reference Cops output as a texture.\n- Use `cinput` for fast lookups and `finput` for filtered ones.\n- Use `uvsample` to pull geometry attributes into pixels.\n- Use `assign(R, G, B, col)` to write output directly from a snippet."}]},"uuid":"ef4f48d3-9537-4785-9a26-c3945b44237c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:44:28.969Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"81baa3d4-bddd-437f-8900-34d2f98ff6f8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com