{"parentUuid":"8b18d21a-23b6-4b6e-ad66-9c9dd0589d84","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8uQZvFhBhYRrocHhVukwt","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **size_ref:** Sets the output's dimensions and metadata.\n- **min:** Controls the minimum color value when Range Values is Min/Max.\n- **max:** Controls the maximum color value when Range Values is Min/Max.\n- **ramp:** Supplies the gradient sampled for colors when Range Values is Color Ramp.\n- **seed:** Varies the random color distribution, including per pixel or per custom shape.\n\n**Output**\n- **random:** The layer with the random colors applied.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the node outputs.\n- **Range Values:** Chooses how colors are picked: Min/Max bounds, a Color Ramp, or a list of Specific Values.\n- **Color Model (Min/Max):** Defines the bounds in RGB or HSV space.\n- **Relative to Color (Min/Max):** Sets a base color so the random range varies only slightly around it.\n- **Red, Green, Blue, Hue, Saturation, Value Min/Max:** Set the limits for each component in the chosen color model.\n- **Color Ramp:** Maps the random value along a ramp to produce the color.\n- **Color Palette (Specific Values):** Loads preset palettes that fill the color list.\n- **Number of Colors (Specific Values):** Sets how many color sets are available.\n- **Color # (Specific Values):** Sets each set's base color and how related colors are derived, such as complementary, analogous, triadic, tetradic, shades, or tints.\n- **Weight:** Controls how often each color option is chosen.\n- **Angle:** Sets the color-wheel spacing between related colors.\n- **Distance:** Sets the brightness or saturation spacing for shades or tints.\n- **Random per Pixel:** Makes the selection vary per pixel for grain-like noise.\n- **Seed:** Changes the random result when the current output isn't desirable.\n- **Time:** Makes the colors vary over time.\n- **Zero Negative IDs:** With a seed input, outputs black where the seed is a negative integer, treating those areas as background."}]},"uuid":"4bf8bdef-068e-4707-a436-b6d773a7e204","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:53:42.762Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ca7c3e52-8f2a-4f9b-b42f-60ca9abff8bc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b18d21a-23b6-4b6e-ad66-9c9dd0589d84","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"1383ec50-9bcf-4666-9d5a-3daa7f6a93ba","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UbMoQrkUtopDSBZLkvSCNH","type":"tool_result","content":"**ID to Mono** converts an ID layer, VDB, or attribute into a float value.\n\n**Input**\n- **id**: The original ID layer, VDB, or attribute to convert.\n\n**Output**\n- **mono**: The resulting mono layer, VDB, or attribute containing the float values.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature**: Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Conversion**: Sets how the integer becomes a float. It has three methods:\n  - **Cast**: Converts the integer directly to a float. Very large IDs can't be represented accurately.\n  - **Safe Pack**: Reversibly packs the integer into a float. For many IDs, the result is the equivalent float value. This method matches the `pack_inttosafefloat` VEX function.\n  - **Bitwise**: Reinterprets the integer's bits as a float. The mapping is reversible, but the float doesn't reflect the integer's size.\n\n**Choosing a method for seeds or gradients** (my inference, not stated on the page):\n- **Safe Pack** keeps values proportional to the IDs, which suits gradients.\n- **Bitwise** scatters values unpredictably, which can work for random seeds, since nearby IDs produce unrelated floats.\n- **Cast** is the simplest option but loses accuracy for large IDs.\n\n**See also:** Mono to ID, which performs the reverse conversion."}]},"uuid":"3e92b23c-e147-446d-8fce-17dcddf96905","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:53:43.164Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ca7c3e52-8f2a-4f9b-b42f-60ca9abff8bc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1383ec50-9bcf-4666-9d5a-3daa7f6a93ba","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"81f77d3e-eab1-45dd-8967-240b2d6eca8f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCdm9VvefBnULj4yhvBq8r","type":"tool_result","content":"**Fill Connected** is a Copernicus node that flood fills the connected regions of a layer, replacing them with a constant color.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source:** The layer to flood.\n- **fillvalue** (optional): A layer that supplies the fill color.\n- **mask** (optional): A per-pixel amount that is scaled by the Mask parameter.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **fill:** The source layer with the connected region replaced by the fill color.\n- **flood:** A layer that is white where the fill was applied and black elsewhere.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the source accepts.\n- **Mask:** Controls how much of the new value blends with the original. The default of 1 uses only the new value.\n- **Seed Location:** The image coordinate where the flood starts. You can click in the image to set it.\n- **Tolerance:** The maximum pixel-value difference from the seed that the fill can spread across. Connectivity is all-or-nothing, even when Fall Off is used.\n- **Fall Off:** A ramp that reduces the fill's opacity for pixels that differ more from the seed value.\n- **Source:** Chooses where the fill color comes from:\n  - **Value:** Uses the Color parameter.\n  - **Image Location:** Samples the fillvalue input at the Source Location.\n  - **First Pixel / Last Pixel:** Uses the first or last pixel of the fillvalue input.\n- **Color:** The fill color used when Source is set to Value.\n- **ID:** The ID value to flood when working with ID layers.\n- **Source Location:** The position in the fillvalue input to sample as the fill color."}]},"uuid":"9440bd11-4b60-4778-873b-62bcd6f90dd5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:53:43.389Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ca7c3e52-8f2a-4f9b-b42f-60ca9abff8bc","cont