ve to low poly mesh per UV tile, the default; Relative to Min/Max per UV tile; Manual) and Scaling divisor, visible only with Manual')\nB('Height role: it is a baked height that can seed the Height channel')\nB('COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `height` (Height Space, Inner Distance and Outer Distance remap it; the SideFX page says it often needs remapping); normalize with `remap` or `heightfieldtomono` (Compute Range, Input and Output Min and Max, Clamp to Output Range)')\nS()\nH(4, 'A2.9 Bent normals and common baking settings')\nB('Source: ' + E + 'baking/mesh-map-settings and ' + E + 'baking/how-to-bake-mesh-maps')\nB('Bent Normals stores the averaged unoccluded direction using Secondary rays, occluder distances, Relative to bounding box, Spread angle, Distribution, Ignore backface and Self occlusion; the `bakegeometrytextures` output list (normal, edgenormal, worldnormal, position, occlusion, curvature, edge, cavity, thickness, height, alpha, custom) has no bent-normal output')\nB('Common settings in Painter: output size, dilation width, antialiasing, high-poly meshes or the low mesh used as high, cage distance-based or automatic (experimental) or a custom file with the same vertex count (red spots mark intersections), Match always or by mesh name, ignore backface; a skew correction page exists')\nB('COP counterparts on `bakegeometrytextures`: Tracing Mode (Surface Normal or Cage Mesh), Ray Bias, Auto Generate Cage, Cage Offset, Soften Cage, Sample Multiplier, Max Distance, Match Pieces by Name, Enable UV Boundary Filling, Mask Out High Resolution Mesh; skew inputs exist (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bakegeometrytextures.html and https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/22/copernicus.html)')\nS()\nH(4, 'A2.10 Mesh map to Copernicus lookup rows')\nR('Painter mesh map', 'bakegeometrytextures output', 'Flat-height substitute (no mesh)')\nR('Normal (tangent)', '`normal`, `edgenormal`', '`heighttonormal`')\nR('World space normals', '`world