on\"},{\"title\":\"creating props for games vol 2 texturing shading for production\",\"url\":\"https://rare.thegnomonworkshop.com/blog/creating-props-for-games-vol-2-texturing-shading-for-production\"}]\n\nJavier Perez teaches at Gnomon, and his Gnomon course is the advanced follow-up to the course you named.\n\n- **Course:** Gnomon lists Texturing and Shading for Games 2, taught by Perez, as a 10-week online course. It builds on the skills learned in Texturing and Shading for Games 1. The listing I found is for the Fall 2025 term, and I didn't find a separate Gnomon page for Part 1, so the current schedule may differ.\n- **Software:** The course covers Marmoset Toolbag, Unity3D, Unreal Engine, and Substance Designer. Its tuition is listed at $1,650.\n- **Format:** Each week combines in-engine demonstrations with critique of homework, and the course ends with a final project reviewed in class.\n- **Background:** Gnomon's instructor profile says Perez has 11+ years of experience in creating game-ready assets. His credits include work on The Last of Us Part I and II, Call of Duty, and Metal Gear Online. He also lists Adjunct Professor, Laguna College of Art and Design among his roles.\n- **Current role:** A Meet Mat 5 texturing contest bio describes him as a Lead Material Artist | PlayStation Studios. The same bio says he shares his passion for Substance Designer by teaching at Laguna College of Art and Design and Gnomon School of Visual Arts, as well as speaking at industry events like GDC. That bio cites 13 years of experience, while Gnomon's profile says 11+, so the two sources don't agree on that figure.\n\nSeveral search results were Gnomon Workshop tutorials by Nick Reynolds, such as \"Creating Props for Games, Vol. 2,\" which has a similar title. They aren't related to Perez or his Gnomon School course.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"90d291bd-6386-46e7-8024-169b5f0a2929","tim