ep node count low (Charlie Foreman); expose few parameters (Perez, Lynch)')\nB('Copernicus chain: one named block per read (macro, meso, micro) each ending in a `null`, merged with `blend` (Maximum for raised unions, Add for zero-mean sculpting deltas, Mask = amplitude); monitors kept beside the chain: `heighttonormal`, `heighttoambientocclusion`, `curvature`; range tools: Auto Levels node = `equalize` (OFFICIAL-MAP), Levels node = `remap` (OFFICIAL-MAP); the headroom compression is `remap` Output Min 0 and Output Max 0.8 (UNVERIFIED mapping)')\nB('Parameter hints: the `equalize` page warns that equalizing per frame can flicker for procedural changes and recommends a `remap` with a fixed range; `remap` Compute Range fills Input Min and Max from the layer; `statistics` outputs average, minimum and maximum (SOURCE: ' + SX + 'equalize.html and ' + SX + 'statistics.html)')\nB('Visual signature (UNVERIFIED): the reference shows readable large masses at thumbnail size, mid-size steps at half size and tooth only at full size; if tooth is the only readable scale the surface is micro-only (fabric, sandpaper) and the macro block can stay flat')\nB('Local notes: Copernicus1.md line 1537 imposes node names of the form letter, number, subject, role (for example `C03_TL__distance_to_corner`) and line 1627 requires every detail layer to have a zero mean; line 1509 records that an earlier fiber-wood attempt failed partly because the macro form came after the fibers')\nS()\n\nH(4, 'T02 Shape blockout, bevel profiles and distance fields')\nB('Problem solved: give each tile, stone or cell a believable footprint and cross-section (flat top, bevel, dish, pillow) before any damage')\nB('Designer chain (SOURCE): Tile Generator for grids; polygon plus linear gradient in minimum-darken into Tile Random (Soto); primitives combined by add and subtract, blurred, histogram-scanned and warped (Caggese); Edge Detect plus Bevel for tile seams (Prakapenka); Edge Detect to bevel corners, Distance to