tail (the bottom normal is reoriented to the top surface); painting normals defaults to Detail (11 October 2026)\n54\t- SOURCE: right-click \"Add mask with height combination\" adds a Compare Mask effect and sets the Height channel blend mode to Normal; Compare Mask compares a chosen channel of a source side and a target side (layers below, this layer, this mask, or a constant) with an operation of lower than, within tolerance or higher than, a Hardness control and a Histogram view (11 October 2026)\n55\t- SOURCE: the Height To Normal filter has Overwrite Existing Normal, Use World Units, Normal Intensity (only when world units are off), Surface Size in cm and Height Depth in cm (only when world units are on); no normal orientation or blend option is listed on its page (11 October 2026)\n56\t- COP: height is a Mono layer (floating point); keep detail layers zero-mean so that `blend` Add behaves like Painter Linear Dodge on signed values (LOCAL: Copernicus1.md line 1627 states that every detail layer must have a zero mean) (11 October 2026)\n57\t- COP: `heighttonormal` replaces the Height To Normal filter: Normal Type Offset (0 to 1, for files) or Signed (-1 to 1, for geometry), Height Scale (steeper normals when larger, plays the role of Normal Intensity), Kernel Size (wider derivative distance smooths stepping, the closest knob to Smooth versus Sharp, UNVERIFIED), Read Pixels outside Image (turn on with a wrap border for tiling); LOCAL line 1522 warns that the output is already encoded 0 to 1 and line 1561 that it refuses an RGBA layer (11 October 2026)\n58\t- COP: `combinenormals` (inputs bg and fg, Normal Type, Combine Method Whiteout, UDN, Reoriented) replaces Normal mixing and the Normal-channel blend modes; Whiteout matches Normal Map Combine and Reoriented matches Normal Map Detail (UNVERIFIED pairing), and swapping bg and fg gives Inverse Detail (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n59\t- COP: `compare` (inputs A, B, tolerance; outputs a 0 to 1 mask; True If operators; Tolerance and Falloff None, Linear or Elendt) replaces Compare Mask; `normaltoheight` (Solver FFT or Poisson, Normal Type, Height Scale, Center, borders) rebuilds a height from a baked normal when only the normal exists (11 October 2026)\n60\t\n61\t### A2 Baked mesh maps (bakers) and what each is used for (11 October 2026)\n62\t\n63\tBaking mode (shortcut F8) produces the mesh maps that generators, filters, smart materials and smart masks read; the same ideas exist in Copernicus as the outputs of `bakegeometrytextures` (version 2.0 in Houdini 22) with `bakepreprocess` as the new ray set-up node. (11 October 2026)\n64\t\n65\t#### A2.1 Normal map from mesh (11 October 2026)\n66\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/normal-map-from-mesh (11 October 2026)\n67\t- Purpose: moves the detail of a high-poly mesh onto the low-poly mesh as a normal map; Painter always bakes tangent space and follows the project orientation (11 October 2026)\n68\t- Key parameters: Map Type (world or tangent, hidden in Painter), Normal Orientation (OpenGL or DirectX, DirectX is the baker default, tangent space only) (11 October 2026)\n69\t- Height role: it is the base normal into which painted height is mixed when Normal mixing is Combine, so it carries the large relief that Height then refines (11 October 2026)\n70\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` outputs `normal` (tangent) and `edgenormal` (rounded edges without extra geometry); Normal Space and Normal Y Direction choose signed or offset and the Y orientation; no bake is needed for a flat texture, use `heighttonormal` (11 October 2026)\n71\t\n72\t#### A2.2 World space normals (11 October 2026)\n73\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/world-space-normals (11 October 2026)\n74\t- Purpose: stores normal, tangent or binormal in world space, which lets generators find surfaces that face up, down or sideways (dust on upward faces) (11 October 2026)\n75\t- Key parameters: Baking Type (Normal default, Tangent, Binormal), optional Normal Map input, Normal Orientation (OpenGL or DirectX, DirectX default, Normal type only) (11 October 2026)\n76\t- Height role: indirect, it decides where height-like deposits such as dust or snow are allowed (11 October 2026)\n77\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `worldnormal`; for a flat tile UNVERIFIED: `heighttonormal` with Normal Type Signed then `channelsplit` to isolate the component that says \"facing up\" (11 October 2026)\n78\t\n79\t#### A2.3 ID (Color Map from Mesh) (11 October 2026)\n80\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/color-map-from-mesh and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)\n81\t- Purpose: bakes a distinct color per part of the mesh so selections and masks are easy (11 October 2026)\n82\t- Key parameters: Color Source (Vertex Color blended smoothly between vertices, Material Color per face, Mesh ID per object, Polygroup or Submesh ID per element; the Painter page also names file ID), Color Generator (Random, Hue Shift or Grayscale, only for the ID sources) (11 October 2026)\n83\t- Height role: per-part masks that include or exclude a height treatment such as wear (11 October 2026)\n84\t- COP: `idtomask` (ID Pattern, Keep by Range, Keep by Chance with Probability and Seed, Keep within Mask), `idtomono` (Conversion Cast, Safe Pack or Bitwise) and `monotoid` convert ids; the `custom` output of `bakegeometrytextures` rasterizes user attributes (UNVERIFIED that an id attribute travels through it); flat substitutes are `segmentbyconnectivity` id, `cellularnoise` id and `tilepattern` id (11 October 2026)\n85\t\n86\t#### A2.4 Ambient occlusion (11 October 2026)\n87\t- Sources: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/ambient-occlusion and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)\n88\t- Purpose: ambient shadow map, dark where light is blocked such as crevices and contact points (11 October 2026)\n89\t- Key parameters (Painter page): Secondary rays, Minimum and Maximum occluder distance, Spread angle, Distribution, Ignore backface, Self occlusion, Attenuation, optional ground plane with an offset; (baker page) Quality with 3, 5 (default), 10 or 16 passes, Precision Bias, Distance Fade, optional Normal Map and World Space flag, Invert Normal which produces a thickness-style map, Use Unselected Mesh Parts (11 October 2026)\n90\t- Height role: shows how recessed a feature is; drives dirt and wear masks; a quick judge of height reads while building (11 October 2026)\n91\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `occlusion` for meshes; flat height input: `heighttoambientocclusion` (Height Scale, Space, View Radius, Step Scale, Sample Count, Sample from Hemisphere, Remap Ramp); OFFICIAL-MAP: Ambient Occlusion (HBAO) node = `heighttoambientocclusion` (11 October 2026)\n92\t\n93\t#### A2.5 Curvature (11 October 2026)\n94\t- Sources: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/curvature and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)\n95\t- Purpose: convex areas bright, concave areas dark, flat areas mid-gray; the base of edge wear (convex) and cavity masks (concave) (11 October 2026)\n96\t- Key parameters: (Painter) Method, Secondary rays, Sampling radius, Relative to bounding box, Self intersection, Tonemapping automatic per UV tile or manual minimum and maximum; (baker page) Algorithm, Details, Enable Seams, Seams Intensity (11 October 2026)\n97\t- Height role: convex edges are where height is chipped away, concave cavities are where dirt height accumulates (11 October 2026)\n98\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` outputs `curvature`, `edge` and `cavity`; flat height input: `curvature` (Method Finite Difference or Angle Deficit, Curvature Type Gaussian, Mean, Principal max or min, Output Type Curvature, Convexity or Concavity, Kernel Size, Normalize, Minimum and Maximum) (11 October 2026)\n99\t\n100\t#### A2.6 Position (11 October 2026)\n101\t- Sources: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/position and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings (11 October 2026)\n102\t- Purpose: records where each texel sits in space, for gradient masks such as rust at the bottom or dust at the top (11 October 2026)\n103\t- Key parameters: Mode (all axes in the color channels or one axis as grayscale), Axis, Normalization Type (bounding box, bounding sphere or none), Normalization Scale (Per Material, or Full Scene which is the default and keeps values continuous across objects) (11 October 2026)\n104\t- Height role: altitude weighting of deposits and wear (11 October 2026)\n105\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `position`; `posmap` generates a position layer (Source Position, X Y Z Border, Shift and Cycles); flat substitute: `ramp` (Type Horizontal or Vertical, Rotation, Start Position, End Position, Outside Range) (11 October 2026)\n106\t\n107\t#### A2.7 Thickness (11 October 2026)\n108\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/thickness-map-from-mesh (11 October 2026)\n109\t- Purpose: rays go from the surface into the interior; dark means thin, bright means thick; used for subsurface effects and as a mask (11 October 2026)\n110\t- Key parameters: Secondary Rays (default 64), Minimum and Maximum Occluder Distance (defaults 0.00001 and 0.1), Relative to Bounding Box, Spread Angle (default 180), Distribution (Cosine default or Uniform), Ignore Backface, Self Occlusion (Always or By Mesh Name), Automatic Normalization (11 October 2026)\n111\t- Height role: thin rims are likely chipping zones; it is a mask, not a height (11 October 2026)\n112\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `thickness`; no flat equivalent is documented; UNVERIFIED substitute: `heighttoambientocclusion` run on the inverted height, because the Painter AO baker page says inverting normals yields a thickness-style map (11 October 2026)\n113\t\n114\t#### A2.8 Height map from mesh (11 October 2026)\n115\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/bakers/bakers-settings/height-map-from-mesh (11 October 2026)\n116\t- Purpose: measures the surface difference between the high-poly and the low-poly mesh (11 October 2026)\n117\t- Key parameters: Normalization (Relative to ray distance; Relative to low poly mesh per UV tile, the default; Relative to Min/Max per UV tile; Manual) and Scaling divisor, visible only with Manual (11 October 2026)\n118\t- Height role: it is a baked height that can seed the Height channel (11 October 2026)\n119\t- COP: `bakegeometrytextures` output `height` (Height Space, Inner Distance and Outer Distance remap it; the SideFX page says it often needs remapping); normalize with `remap` or `heightfieldtomono` (Compute Range, Input and Output Min and Max, Clamp to Output Range) (11 October 2026)\n120\t\n121\t#### A2.9 Bent normals and common baking settings (11 October 2026)\n122\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/mesh-map-settings and https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/baking/how-to-bake-mesh-maps (11 October 2026)\n123\t- Bent Normals stores the averaged unoccluded direction using Secondary rays, occluder distances, Relative to bounding box, Spread angle, Distribution, Ignore backface and Self occlusion; the `bakegeometrytextures` output list (normal, edgenormal, worldnormal, position, occlusion, curvature, edge, cavity, thickness, height, alpha, custom) has no bent-normal output (11 October 2026)\n124\t- Common settings in Painter: output size, dilation width, antialiasing, high-poly meshes or the low mesh used as high, cage distance-based or automatic (experimental) or a custom file with the same vertex count (red spots mark intersections), Match always or by mesh name, ignore backface; a skew correction page exists (11 October 2026)\n125\t- COP counterparts on `bakegeometrytextures`: Tracing Mode (Surface Normal or Cage Mesh), Ray Bias, Auto Generate Cage, Cage Offset, Soften Cage, Sample Multiplier, Max Distance, Match Pieces by Name, Enable UV Boundary Filling, Mask Out High Resolution Mesh; skew inputs exist (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bakegeometrytextures.html and https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/22/copernicus.html) (11 October 2026)\n126\t\n127\t#### A2.10 Mesh map to Copernicus lookup rows (11 October 2026)\n128\t| Painter mesh map | bakegeometrytextures output | Flat-height substitute (no mesh) | 11 October 2026 |  \n129\t| Normal (tangent) | `normal`, `edgenormal` | `heighttonormal` | 11 October 2026 |  \n130\t| World space normals | `worldnormal` | `heighttonormal` Signed then `channelsplit` (UNVERIFIED) | 11 October 2026 |  \n131\t| ID | `custom` (UNVERIFIED) | `segmentbyconnectivity`, `cellularnoise` id, `tilepattern` id, then `idtomask` | 11 October 2026 |  \n132\t| Ambient occlusion | `occlusion` | `heighttoambientocclusion` | 11 October 2026 |  \n133\t| Curvature | `curvature`, `edge`, `cavity` | `curvature` Output Type Convexity or Concavity | 11 October 2026 |  \n134\t| Position | `position` | `ramp` or `posmap` | 11 October 2026 |  \n135\t| Thickness | `thickness` | none documented; UNVERIFIED: AO of inverted height | 11 October 2026 |  \n136\t| Height from mesh | `height` | the height itself, normalized by `remap` | 11 October 2026 |  \n137\t- Sources for these rows: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bakegeometrytextures.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoambientocclusion.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curvature.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttonormal.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/ramp.html and the baker pages cited in A2.1 to A2.9 (11 October 2026)\n138\t\n139\t### A3 Generators (11 October 2026)\n140\t"}]},"uuid":"723b34f6-6824-4ecc-a331-90af77192861","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:10:47.274Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a7df0061-d02a-4f83-9b96-b4488ae1e68d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
