{"parentUuid":"cc355a7b-dd9a-4c00-a3ea-4d6dead49175","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018YB4qUDYgkj4NSwwyN3kRM","type":"tool_result","content":"139\t### A3 Generators (11 October 2026)\n140\t\n141\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/generator (11 October 2026)\n142\t- SOURCE: a generator is a substance that builds a mask or texture from the mesh topology using baked utility maps such as Position, Curvature and World Space Normal; most outputs are black and white, so generators mostly drive masks, and they are added by right-clicking a mask or a layer, choosing Add generator, then picking the generator with the Generator button in the Properties panel (11 October 2026)\n143\t- Reading rule for this section: a Painter generator needs a mesh; for a flat tiling height texture the same masks are derived from the height itself, with `curvature`, `heighttoambientocclusion`, `heighttonormal`, `ramp` and noise nodes (the skeleton is given in A3.10) (11 October 2026)\n144\t\n145\t#### A3.1 Dirt (11 October 2026)\n146\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/dirt (11 October 2026)\n147\t- Purpose: builds a black-and-white buildup of dirt and grunge in crevices, along edges and on flat areas from curvature and ambient occlusion, optionally refined by micro height and micro normal inputs (11 October 2026)\n148\t- Baked maps needed: Position, Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal; optional inputs Custom Grunge, Micro Normal, Micro Height (each a texture or an anchor point) (11 October 2026)\n149\t- Key parameters: Seed, Invert, Dirt Level, Dirt Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Grunge Scale, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Masking (how strongly edges mask out dirt, from the curvature map); Micro Details: Micro Height, Micro Normal, Curvature Type (Standard is sharp and can miss broad detail, Sobel is slightly blurrier, Smooth blurs at several levels and can lose detail), Curvature Intensity, Height Details Intensity, AO Radius, AO Depth (11 October 2026)\n150\t- Height role: the mask says where deposit height is added (dust, mud) or where pits are cut; the Micro Height input injects fine bump detail into the mask itself (11 October 2026)\n151\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `curvature` (Output Type Concavity) -> `blend` Multiply with an inverted `heighttoambientocclusion` -> `blend` Add or Maximum with grunge from `fractalnoise` or `grunge_layerednoise` (Grunge Amount = the Mask parameter, Grunge Scale = Element Size) -> `remap` Operation Threshold (Dirt Level = Threshold, Dirt Contrast = inverse of Width) -> optional `blur`; to deposit height, `blend` Add of mask times a depth constant (11 October 2026)\n152\t\n153\t#### A3.2 Metal Edge Wear (11 October 2026)\n154\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/metal-edge-wear (11 October 2026)\n155\t- Purpose: simulates damage and scratches on the parts of a mesh most likely to be knocked, as a black-and-white mask (11 October 2026)\n156\t- Baked maps needed: Position, Curvature (defines the edges), Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal; optional Custom Grunge, Micro Normal, Micro Height (11 October 2026)\n157\t- Key parameters: Seed, Invert, Wear Level, Wear Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Grunge Scale, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Smoothness, Ambient Occlusion Masking (occluded areas get no wear), Curvature Weight (very low values keep only grunge); Micro Details identical to Dirt (11 October 2026)\n158\t- Height role: wear mask times a chip depth is the standard way to carve edge chips into a height; the same mask drives roughness and metal elsewhere (11 October 2026)\n159\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `curvature` (Output Type Convexity) -> `remap` Threshold (Wear Level and Wear Contrast) -> `blend` Multiply by (1 minus occlusion) for AO masking -> breakup with `fractalnoise` or `grunge_galvanizedsteel` -> `blur` for Edges Smoothness -> `blend` Subtract from the height; scratches with `streakblur` on a `randommono` set to Random per Pixel; chips with `shapescatter` whose `density` input is the wear mask (11 October 2026)\n160\t\n161\t#### A3.3 Fiber Glass Edge Wear (11 October 2026)\n162\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/fiber-glass-edge-wear (11 October 2026)\n163\t- Purpose: black-and-white mask for worn and frayed edges on fiberglass; the Designer counterpart note says it could suit cloth (11 October 2026)\n164\t- Baked maps needed: Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal, Position; optional Micro Height, Micro Normal, Custom Grunge (11 October 2026)\n165\t- Key parameters: Seed, Invert (flips internal maps such as curvature or AO before they combine), Wear Level, Wear Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Smoothness, Ambient Occlusion Masking, Curvature Weight; Micro Details as in Dirt (11 October 2026)\n166\t- Height role: frayed rims, fibers that stand proud or are cut at an edge (11 October 2026)\n167\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: same chain as Metal Edge Wear plus a short `streakblur` (Mode Max or Blur, small Length) along the edge direction to give a frayed look (11 October 2026)\n168\t\n169\t#### A3.4 Mask Editor (11 October 2026)\n170\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/mask-editor (11 October 2026)\n171\t- Purpose: one flexible generator that combines custom textures, baked maps and micro details into a black-and-white mask; it is heavier than most generators (11 October 2026)\n172\t- Inputs: Texture and Texture (Secondary), World Space Normals, Position Gradient, Thickness, Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, Micro Normal, Micro Height (11 October 2026)\n173\t- Global controls: Global Invert, Global Blur, Global Balance (moves the midpoint like brightness), Global Contrast; layer opacity controls for Texture, Texture 2, Ambient Occlusion, Curvature, World Space Normal, Position Gradient and Thickness (11 October 2026)\n174\t- Texture groups: Invert, Grayscale Conversion, Blending Mode, Scale, Contrast, Brightness, Triplanar, Triplanar Contrast, Non-Square Tiling (11 October 2026)\n175\t- Map groups: AO (Invert, Blending Mode, Blur, Balance, Contrast); Curvature (Invert, Blending Mode, Mode Edges or Cavities or Dual or Unprocessed, seven detail scales Sharp, Fine, Soft, Medium, Large, Big, Huge, Contrast, Brightness); World Space Normal (Invert, Blending Mode, Blur, Balance, Contrast, Brightness, plus Right to Left, Top to Bottom and Front to Back each with its own Invert and Blending Mode); Position Gradient (Invert, Balance, Contrast, Brightness, Blending Mode, three sub-gradients that blend only with each other); Thickness (Invert, Blur, Contrast, Brightness); Micro Details (Micro Height, Micro Normal, Curvature Type, Curvature Intensity, Height Details Intensity, AO Radius, AO Depth) (11 October 2026)\n176\t- Height role: a mask factory; the output multiplies a chip depth or a deposit depth that is applied to height (11 October 2026)\n177\tMask Editor control to Copernicus lookup rows (all COP chains UNVERIFIED unless stated): (11 October 2026)\n178\t| Mask Editor control | Copernicus node and parameter | Note | 11 October 2026 |  \n179\t| Global Invert | `invert` | direct | 11 October 2026 |  \n180\t| Global Blur | `blur` Filter Gaussian, Size, Units | Size scales the radius | 11 October 2026 |  \n181\t| Global Balance | `function` Shift, or `bright` | moves the midpoint | 11 October 2026 |  \n182\t| Global Contrast | `contrast`, or `remap` Threshold Width | smaller Width means harder edge | 11 October 2026 |  \n183\t| Layer opacity | `blend` Mask parameter | Mask 1 uses only the new value | 11 October 2026 |  \n184\t| Blending Mode | `blend` Operation (Add, Subtract, Multiply, Maximum, Minimum, Overlay, Screen, Difference, Exclusion, SoftLight, HardLight, Dodge, Burn) | names from the Blend COP page | 11 October 2026 |  \n185\t| Curvature Mode | `curvature` Output Type Curvature, Convexity or Concavity | Dual = Maximum of both | 11 October 2026 |  \n186\t| Curvature seven scales | `curvature` at several Kernel Size values, merged with `average` Operation Max or Add | structure is an inference | 11 October 2026 |  \n187\t| World Space Normal directions | `heighttonormal` Signed -> `channelsplit` -> `remap` | flat tile only | 11 October 2026 |  \n188\t| Position Gradient | `ramp` Horizontal or Vertical | Start and End Position set the span | 11 October 2026 |  \n189\t| Thickness | none documented for flat height | bake only | 11 October 2026 |  \n190\t| Texture Scale | `xform2d` on a noise or file layer | mesh triplanar needs `triplanar` | 11 October 2026 |  \n191\t\n192\t#### A3.5 Mask Builder (legacy) (11 October 2026)\n193\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/mask-builder (11 October 2026)\n194\t- Purpose: older multipurpose generator, replaced by Mask Editor, mixing Grunge, AO, Curvature, a Top/Down Gradient, World Space Normal, Scratches, Scatter and Micro Details (11 October 2026)\n195\t- Key parameters: Seed, Level, Contrast, Invert, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, strength sliders for each effect (Scratches only show when Grunge, AO or Curvature is above zero); Grunge (Scale, Use Custom Grunge, Secondary Custom Grunge, Invert); AO (Range, Contrast, Noisiness, Invert); Curvature (Convex Range, Convex Contrast, Convex Invert, Concave Range, Concave Contrast, Concave Invert, Smoothness, Level Boost, Noisiness); Gradient (Range, Contrast, Invert, uses Position so its normalization scale matters); World Space Normal (Top, Bottom, Front, Back, Right, Left Intensity, with Front = +X and Right = +Z by default); Scratches (Amount, Scale); Scatter (Scale, Density, Size, Size Variation, Opacity Variation) (11 October 2026)\n196\t- Height role: the Scatter group builds random stamp masks usable as chip or dent masks (11 October 2026)\n197\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: same lookup as Mask Editor; Scatter -> `shapescatter` (Stamps X and Y, Density, Scale Mode Variance, Alpha Variance); Scratches -> `streakblur` on thin random lines or `curvescatter` with line stamps (11 October 2026)\n198\t\n199\t#### A3.6 Ambient Occlusion generator (11 October 2026)\n200\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/ambient-occlusion (11 October 2026)\n201\t- Purpose: black-and-white mask from the baked AO, with an optional custom texture and micro details; as a layer mask it often needs Invert so the layer shows in occluded areas (11 October 2026)\n202\t- Baked maps needed: Position, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal (11 October 2026)\n203\t- Key parameters: Global Invert, Global Blur, Global Balance, Global Contrast, Use Texture, Use Micro Details; AO group (Invert, Blur, Balance, Contrast); Texture group (Texture Opacity, Invert, Grayscale Conversion, Blending Mode, Scale, Contrast, Brightness, Triplanar, Triplanar Contrast); Micro Details (Micro Height, Micro Normal, AO Radius, AO Depth) (11 October 2026)\n204\t- Height role: recess mask for dirt or dust height (11 October 2026)\n205\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `heighttoambientocclusion` -> `invert` -> `remap`; Micro Details AO Radius and Depth map to a second `heighttoambientocclusion` with a small View Radius and Height Scale (11 October 2026)\n206\t\n207\t#### A3.7 Curvature generator (11 October 2026)\n208\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/curvature (11 October 2026)\n209\t- Purpose: black-and-white mask from the baked curvature, with optional custom texture and micro details; requires a baked position map (11 October 2026)\n210\t- Key parameters: Global group as above; Curvature group (Invert, Mode Edges, Cavities, Dual or Unprocessed, scales Sharp, Fine, Soft, Medium, Large, Big, Huge, Contrast, Brightness); Texture group; Micro Details (Micro Height, Micro Normal, Curvature Type Standard, Sobel or Smooth, Curvature Intensity, Height Details Intensity) (11 October 2026)\n211\t- Height role: edge masks (convex) for chipping and cavity masks (concave) for deposits (11 October 2026)\n212\t- COP chain: `curvature` with Output Type Convexity or Concavity, Normalize on, then `remap`; flat input is a Mono height or a normal field whose Normal Type matches `heighttonormal` (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curvature.html) (11 October 2026)\n213\t\n214\t#### A3.8 Position generator (11 October 2026)\n215\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/position (11 October 2026)\n216\t- Purpose: black-and-white gradient mask from where the surface sits, top to bottom or side to side; needs baked Position and World Space Normals (11 October 2026)\n217\t- Key parameters: Global Invert, Global Blur, Global Balance, Global Contrast, Use Texture; Position Gradient (Invert, Balance, Contrast, Brightness, Right to Left, Top To Bottom, Front to Back, each directional gradient with its own Invert and Blending Mode); Texture group (11 October 2026)\n218\t- Height role: altitude weighting of height deposits (11 October 2026)\n219\t- COP chain: `ramp` (Type Horizontal or Vertical, Rotation, Start Position, End Position, Outside Range Clamp, Repeat or Mirror) -> `remap`; for a mesh `posmap` or the `position` bake output (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/ramp.html) (11 October 2026)\n220\t\n221\t#### A3.9 Light (11 October 2026)\n222\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/light (11 October 2026)\n223\t- Purpose: simulates a directional light on the mesh from the baked World Space Normal and Position; in a fill layer it outputs color, metalness, specular roughness, normal and height channels, or it can serve as a mask (11 October 2026)\n224\t- Key parameters: Invert, Horizontal Angle, Vertical Angle, Highlight Glossiness, Highlight Level, Light Attenuation (11 October 2026)\n225\t- Height role: the page lists a height channel among its fill outputs and states nothing more, so its exact effect on height is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)\n226\t- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `heighttoshadow` (Type Directional, Azimuth, Altitude, Angular Size, Height Map Scale, Step Scale) gives self-shadowing of a height; a shaded look needs the normal from `heighttonormal` dotted with a light vector in a `wrangle` (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoshadow.html) (11 October 2026)\n227\t\n228\t#### A3.10 Mesh-free generator skeleton for a flat height tile (11 October 2026)\n229\t- Sources: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curvature.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoambientocclusion.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttonormal.html , https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/remap.html (11 October 2026)\n230\t- Edges (convex) = `curvature` Output Type Convexity; cavities (concave) = `curvature` Output Type Concavity; occlusion = `heighttoambientocclusion`; up-facing = `heighttonormal` Signed -> `channelsplit`; gradient = `ramp`; grunge = `fractalnoise` or the 14 H22 `grunge_*` nodes; threshold and contrast = `remap` Operation Threshold; blend and amounts = `blend` with the Mask parameter; then subtract or add the mask times a depth from the height (all UNVERIFIED as a combined recipe, each node verified individually) (11 October 2026)\n231\t- Wrangle caution from LOCAL Copernicus1.md lines 1538 and 1561: a Wrangle COP writes only the RGBA output `C`, so write `p@C = set(a, b, c, d);` and split channels with `channelextract` before `heighttonormal` (11 October 2026)\n232\t\n233\t### A4 Filters (11 October 2026)\n234\t\n235\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/filter (11 October 2026)\n236\t- SOURCE: a filter is a substance that changes the content of a layer or a mask; with the layer in Passthrough blend mode the filter can modify everything below it; dragging a filter from the Shelf into the stack creates such a layer and sets every channel to Passthrough (not usable on masks that way); extra filters arrive as SBSAR files and custom ones are made in Designer (11 October 2026)\n237\t- SOURCE: the filter index has five groups, Standard (Blur, Blur Directional, Blur Slope, Clamp, Color Balance, Color Correct, Contrast Luminosity, Drop Shadow, Fill Area Color, Fill Area Mask, FXAA, Glow, Gradient, Gradient Dynamic, Grayscale Conversion, Highpass, Histogram Scan, Histogram Shift, HSL Perceptive, Invert, Mirror, Pixelate, Posterize, Sharpen, Smoothstep, Threshold, Transform, Warp), Finishes (nine MatFinish), MatFX (ten), Lighting (two baked-lighting filters) and Advanced (Anisotropic Kuwahara, Bevel, Bevel Smooth, Color Match, Directional Distance, Gradient Curve, Height Adjust, Height To Normal, Mask Outline, PBR Validate, Quantize, Stylization, Tri-Planar Advanced) (11 October 2026)\n238\t\n239\t#### A4.1 Blur (11 October 2026)\n240\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/blur (11 October 2026)\n241\t- Purpose: softens detail in a map or a mask; applies to a whole material or one texture (11 October 2026)\n242\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap (toggles wrapping) (11 October 2026)\n243\t- Height role: smooths a height before it drives a slope or a warp; the page does not mention height specifically (11 October 2026)\n244\t- COP: `blur` (Filter Gaussian or Box, Units Image, Pixels or Local, Size, optional `size` input that scales the radius per pixel, Read Pixels outside Image); Blur Wrap corresponds to reading outside the image with a wrap border (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n245\t\n246\t#### A4.2 Blur Directional (11 October 2026)\n247\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/blur-directional (11 October 2026)\n248\t- Purpose: softens a grayscale map or mask along one direction instead of all directions (11 October 2026)\n249\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Angle, Intensity (11 October 2026)\n250\t- Height role: stretches noise into streaks (grain, brushing) before it becomes relief (11 October 2026)\n251\t- COP: `streakblur` Mode Blur (Direction Type Angle or Direction, Angle, Units, Length, Bias, optional `direction` and `scalelength` inputs) (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/streakblur.html) (11 October 2026)\n252\t\n253\t#### A4.3 Blur Slope (11 October 2026)\n254\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/blur-slope (11 October 2026)\n255\t- Purpose: a grayscale filter that smears or fades pixels, most visibly along sharp contrast edges; typical uses are chipped or worn edges, dirt that bleeds past its boundary and smeared rust (11 October 2026)\n256\t- Key parameters: input Custom Noise; Seed, Intensity, Intensity Divider, Blending Mode, Quality; Source group Source Type (default noise, previous input, custom noise), Blur, Position, Contrast, Source Tiling (11 October 2026)\n257\t- Height role: the page does not name the height channel; as a mask or a height layer filter it rounds, chips or smears edges, in the same family as the Designer Slope Blur whose Min mode erodes bright areas (11 October 2026)\n258\t- COP, OFFICIAL-MAP: Slope Blur = the Distort by Slope recipe, a `slopedir` wired to the `dir` input of a `distort`; the source is pushed away from higher control values, toward lower ones; chain with the Painter source noise: `fractalnoise` -> `blur` -> `slopedir` -> `distort` (Streak Blur, Min or Max; `scale` input for per-pixel intensity); parameter correspondences are UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)\n259\t\n260\t#### A4.4 Warp (11 October 2026)\n261\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/warp (11 October 2026)\n262\t- Purpose: distorts textures, masks, shapes and outlines with noise, in regular, directional and multidirectional modes (11 October 2026)\n263\t- Key parameters: input Custom Noise; Seed, Warp Mode, Intensity, Intensity Divider, Angle, Blending Mode, Directions; Source group Source Mode (Default Noise, Previous Input, Custom Noise), Source Blur, Source Balance, Source Contrast, Source Tilling (spelled so on the page) (11 October 2026)\n264\t- Height role: bends straight relief lines; inside a mask it deforms mask shapes; the page says nothing about using it directly on height (11 October 2026)\n265\t- COP, OFFICIAL-MAP: Warp node = `distort`; regular: noise -> `slopedir` -> `distort` `dir`; directional: `distort` Direction Type Angle with the noise on the `scale` input; multidirectional: two or four `distort` nodes at 90 or 45 degree steps merged by `average` (UNVERIFIED structure) (11 October 2026)\n266\t\n267\t#### A4.5 Sharpen (11 October 2026)\n268\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/sharpen (11 October 2026)\n269\t- Purpose: adds crispness to the selected channels; best with a light touch; can sit on a top passthrough layer to sharpen everything below (11 October 2026)\n270\t- Key parameters: Sharpen Intensity (11 October 2026)\n271\t- Height role: raises micro contrast of a height; over-use creates halos that turn into normal artifacts (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n272\t- COP: `sharpen` (Units, Size, Scale Size, Amplitude, Gain, Threshold, optional `size` and `mask` inputs) (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sharpen.html) (11 October 2026)\n273\t\n274\t#### A4.6 Highpass (11 October 2026)\n275\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/highpass (11 October 2026)\n276\t- Purpose: isolates fine detail by removing broad brightness variation; commonly used to clean images for tiling (11 October 2026)\n277\t- Key parameters: Color Space, Radius, Apply To Alpha (11 October 2026)\n278\t- Height role: extracts micro relief from a meso height so it can be re-added at low amplitude (11 October 2026)\n279\t- COP: `sharpen` with Gain 0 and a positive Amplitude is a high-pass filter by the SideFX description; alternative `blur` then `blend` Subtract (UNVERIFIED); the name `highpass` used in Copernicus1.md is not a COP (11 October 2026)\n280\t\n281\t#### A4.7 HSL Perceptive (11 October 2026)\n282\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/hsl-perceptive (11 October 2026)\n283\t- Purpose: shifts tone, intensity and brightness of a color texture layer (11 October 2026)\n284\t- Key parameters: Mode (Perceptive follows human color vision, Regular follows internal representation), Hue, Saturation, Lightness (11 October 2026)\n285\t- Height role: none, it is a color filter (11 October 2026)\n286\t- COP: OFFICIAL-MAP HSL node = HSV nodes, so `hsv` (Hue Shift, Keep Luminance, Saturation Scale and Shift, Value Scale and Shift); Keep Luminance is the closest to Perceptive (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n287\t\n288\t#### A4.8 Height To Normal (11 October 2026)"}]},"uuid":"0166ef1f-050c-48b7-bc1a-b97ade326966","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:10:54.566Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc355a7b-dd9a-4c00-a3ea-4d6dead49175","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","se