hich accepts a UV layer to position the ramp (11 October 2026)\n301\t\n302\t#### A4.10 Gradient (11 October 2026)\n303\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/gradient (11 October 2026)\n304\t- Purpose: maps grayscale tones onto a custom multi-color gradient (11 October 2026)\n305\t- Key parameters: Display Gradient (Debug), Color Quantity, Blend Color in Linear, Color N, Color N Position; Input Transformation Grayscale Mode (Desaturation, Luma, Average, Max, Min), Blur Intensity, Balance, Contrast, Invert (11 October 2026)\n306\t- Height role: curve shaping and visualization of height ranges (11 October 2026)\n307\t- COP: `ramp` (Ramp editor with Point No., Position, Color, Value) and `remap` Use Ramp; OFFICIAL-MAP: Gradient nodes = Ramp nodes; LOCAL line 1542 warns that a `remap` ramp must cover the whole input range because beyond Input Max the value goes wrong and large black borders appear (11 October 2026)\n308\t\n309\t#### A4.11 Gradient Curve (11 October 2026)\n310\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/gradient-curve (11 October 2026)\n311\t- Purpose: remaps grayscale values through a curve chosen from presets (11 October 2026)\n312\t- Key parameters: Preset, Invert, Balance, Contrast (11 October 2026)\n313\t- Height role: reshapes the height histogram (rounder crests, flatter plateaus) (11 October 2026)\n314\t- COP: `remap` with Use Ramp, or `remap` Operation Threshold for a step; LOCAL line 1559 says never to use a `remap` ramp for a fitted curve because it is baked into a quantized table that created 2 to 3 pixel steps and bands in the normal, and recommends evaluating the curve in VEX (Hermite) in a `wrangle` (11 October 2026)\n315\t\n316\t#### A4.12 Histogram Scan (11 October 2026)\n317\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/histogram-scan (11 October 2026)\n318\t- Purpose: adjusts contrast and brightness of a grayscale input; used on fill layers or masks to grow, shrink or sharpen masks (11 October 2026)\n319\t- Key parameters: Position (shifts the histogram, changes overall brightness), Contrast (how gradual the falloff is), Invert Position (11 October 2026)\n320\t- Height role: turns a noise into a clean mask of peaks or valleys, the basis of chip, crack and plateau masks (11 October 2026)\n321\t- COP, OFFICIAL-MAP: Histogram nodes = Remap nodes, with Operation Threshold doing what Histogram Scan does; Threshold When Greater, Threshold = the Position equivalent, Width = the softness (Width 0 is a hard cutoff); the mapping from Contrast to Width is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)\n322\t\n323\t#### A4.13 Histogram Shift (11 October 2026)\n324\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/histogram-shift (11 October 2026)\n325\t- Purpose: moves the whole tonal range and wraps values pushed past one end back to the other end (11 October 2026)\n326\t- Key parameters: Position (11 October 2026)\n327\t- Height role: banding or wrapped contour effects when applied to a height (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n328\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: `remap` Operation Remap with Outside Range set to Repeat (values outside the input range wrap through the range) and a shifted Input Min and Input Max (11 October 2026)\n329\t\n330\t#### A4.14 Smoothstep (11 October 2026)\n331\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/smoothstep (11 October 2026)\n332\t- Purpose: keeps a band of grayscale tones between two limits with a smooth fade instead of a hard cut, a softer alternative to Threshold or Histogram Scan (11 October 2026)\n333\t- Key parameters: Minimum, Maximum (11 October 2026)\n334\t- Height role: soft masks for gradual wear (11 October 2026)\n335\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: `remap` Operation Threshold with a non-zero Width, or `compareblend` with Falloff Elendt (an S-shaped fade); the `function` COP page lists no smoothstep (11 October 2026)\n336\t\n337\t#### A4.15 Threshold (11 October 2026)\n338\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/threshold (11 October 2026)\n339\t- Purpose: converts the input to a high-contrast black and white result by comparing each pixel to a cutoff; like Histogram Scan at maximum contrast (11 October 2026)\n340\t- Key parameters: Threshold, Mode (Greater, Greater or equal, Lower, Lower or equal) (11 October 2026)\n341\t- Height role: binary masks from a height or noise (11 October 2026)\n342\t- COP: `remap` Operation Threshold with Width 0 and Threshold When matching Mode, or `compare` (Comparison Value, True If operators, Tolerance 0, outputs `mask`) (11 October 2026)\n343\t\n344\t#### A4.16 Clamp (11 October 2026)\n345\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/clamp (11 October 2026)\n346\t- Purpose: restricts values to a lower and upper bound, working per color channel (so it can shift hue; Levels preserves hue better) (11 October 2026)\n347\t- Key parameters: Min, Max (11 October 2026)\n348\t- Height role: flattens plateaus and floors of a height or mask (11 October 2026)\n349\t- COP: `clamp`; for a smooth limit on a height layer `heightfield_clip` has Lower Limit, Upper Limit and Soft Clip (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_clip.html) (11 October 2026)\n350\t\n351\t#### A4.17 Contrast Luminosity (11 October 2026)\n352\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/standard-filters/contrast-luminosity (11 October 2026)\n353\t- Purpose: basic brightness and contrast control for fill layers and masks (11 October 2026)\n354\t- Key parameters: Contrast (also the falloff), Luminosity (11 October 2026)\n355\t- Height role: scales and offsets a height range crudely (11 October 2026)\n356\t- COP: `contrast` and `bright`, or `function` Scale and Shift (11 October 2026)\n357\t\n358\t#### A4.18 Height Adjust (11 October 2026)\n359\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/height-adjustments (11 October 2026)\n360\t- Purpose: non-destructive edit of a height channel: flip, shift or scale values (11 October 2026)\n361\t- Key parameters: Invert, Offset (applied first), Multiply (applied second; a zero height stays zero); stack a second Height Adjust to multiply first and offset after (11 October 2026)\n362\t- Height role: direct, it is the height level control (11 October 2026)\n363\t- COP: `invert`, then `function` with Scale and Shift; Painter Offset o then Multiply m equals (x + o) * m, so Scale m and Shift m * o (UNVERIFIED algebra); keep signed-height conventions consistent with A1 (11 October 2026)\n364\t\n365\t#### A4.19 Bevel (11 October 2026)\n366\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/bevel (11 October 2026)\n367\t- Purpose: adds a raised sloped edge along the borders of grayscale shapes and masks (11 October 2026)\n368\t- Key parameters: Bevel Wrap (tiles seamlessly), Distance, Corner Type (rounded or sharp), Smoothing (removes stair-stepping on curved bevels), Blur Mode (uniform, or non-uniform which concentrates on bevel areas and keeps more detail) (11 October 2026)\n369\t- Height role: builds the slope profile around tile and stone footprints; the page does not confirm height input, only grayscale shapes and masks (11 October 2026)\n370\t- COP, OFFICIAL-MAP: Bevel node = `feather` (Feather Direction Circle for round, Diamond, Square or Octagon for angular corners, Feather Method Distance for Unit Change, Feather from High to Low, Include Border on for tiling, per the Feather page); Smoothing -> a following `blur