ber 2026)\n387\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/mask-outline (11 October 2026)\n388\t- Purpose: traces the edge of a mask to draw a border outside, inside or on both sides (11 October 2026)\n389\t- Key parameters: Mask Position, Start From Black, Threshold, Width, Blur, Curve Shape (11 October 2026)\n390\t- Height role: outline masks for rims and grooves (11 October 2026)\n391\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: `monotosdf` -> `sdftomono` with Draw Outline, Outline Alignment (inside, outside or centered) and Outline Width, or `edgedetect` followed by `dilateerode`; the `edgedetect` page has no width parameter so width comes from Blur Before and a following `dilateerode` (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sdftomono.html and https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetect.html) (11 October 2026)\n392\t\n393\t#### A4.23 Quantize (11 October 2026)\n394\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/quantize (11 October 2026)\n395\t- Purpose: reduces a layer to a small set of colors and extracts a palette (11 October 2026)\n396\t- Key parameters: Color Amount, Contour Smoothing, Dithering, Dithering Pattern, Distance Color Space (Lab or RGB), Apply To Alpha, Alpha Threshold (11 October 2026)\n397\t- Height role: on a gray height it produces terraces or shard-like steps (UNVERIFIED for Painter; Designer artists use it for shard steps on tile damage, see B4) (11 October 2026)\n398\t- COP: `quantize` (Method Number of Segments or Width and Offset, Segments, Rounding Floor, Closest, Ceiling or Custom, Compute Range, Clamp Below and Above); the page documents no dithering (11 October 2026)\n399\t\n400\t#### A4.24 Anisotropic Kuwahara (11 October 2026)\n401\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/advanced-filters/anisotropic-kuwahara (11 October 2026)\n402\t- Purpose: painterly smoothing that blurs along directions detected in the image so strong edges stay defined (11 October 2026)\n403\t- Key parameters: Extract Direction, Radius (maximum 32), Smoothness, Sharpness, Tensor Smoothness, Anisotropy, Anisotropy Angle (plus an angle map input) (11 October 2026)\n404\t- Height role: simplifies a noisy height into flat facets with kept edges (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n405\t- COP: `kuwaharafilter` (Method Approximate or Exact, Luminance, Radius, Blur Scale, Blend to Blur, Separation); its page documents no anisotropic or direction option, so the anisotropic part has no documented counterpart (SOURCE: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/kuwaharafilter.html) (11 October 2026)\n406\t\n407\t#### A4.25 MatFinish family (nine metal finishes) (11 October 2026)\n408\t- Source folder: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/finish-filters/ (matfinish-brushed-linear, matfinish-galvanized, matfinish-grainy, matfinish-grinded, matfinish-hammered, matfinish-perforated-circles, matfinish-powder-coated, matfinish-raw, matfinish-rough) (11 October 2026)\n409\t- SOURCE common facts: each is applied to a fill layer after base color, roughness and metallic are set, as the final surface treatment; most take baked Position and World Space Normals for triplanar mapping; none of the nine pages states which channels (height, normal, roughness) it writes, so the height role of every finish below is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)\n410\t- Brushed Linear: parameters Seed, Scale, Brushing Intensity, Length, Rotation; COP UNVERIFIED: `fractalnoise` with a very stretched Element Scale (Per-Component Controls) -> `streakblur` (Angle = Rotation, Length) -> `blend` Mask for the intensity (11 October 2026)\n411\t- Galvanized: parameters Seed, Scale, Flakes Intensity, Use Custom Flake, Triplanar Mapping, inputs Custom Flake, Position, World Space Normals; COP: `grunge_galvanizedsteel` exists in Houdini 22 (