ormation in the layers below, so it shows nothing when the normal channel is empty or uniform (11 October 2026)\n423\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap, Input Mode, Wear Level, Wear Contrast, Edges Smoothness, Grunge Amount, Grunge Scale; material groups for Metallic Roughness (Base Color, Metallic, Roughness) and Specular Glossiness (Diffuse, Specular Color, Glossiness); Settings Generator Mask Control, Generator Mask Contrast, Generator Mask Blur, Alpha Background Value, Curvature Intensity, Invert Curvature, Combine Curvature, Normal Intensity, AO Spreading (11 October 2026)\n424\t- Height role: reads normals derived from existing relief, so height must exist below it; the page does not say it writes height (11 October 2026)\n425\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: `heighttonormal` -> `edgedetect` (Method Sobel, Blur Before) or `curvature` Convexity, then `fractalnoise` breakup and `remap` Threshold (11 October 2026)\n426\t\n427\t#### A4.27 MatFX Edge Damages (11 October 2026)\n428\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/matfx-filters/matfx-edge-damages (11 October 2026)\n429\t- Purpose: chipped, worn and scratched detail along edges without recoloring the damage, suited to plastics and resins; it changes height only if height data already exists below (11 October 2026)\n430\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap, Level, Contrast, Scratches Intensity, Damages Roughness, Damages Depth (11 October 2026)\n431\t- Height role: Damages Depth is the chip depth subtracted from existing height (11 October 2026)\n432\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: the edge chipping chain of technique T10 in Part B (11 October 2026)\n433\t\n434\t#### A4.28 MatFX HBAO (11 October 2026)\n435\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/matfx-filters/matfx-hbao (11 October 2026)\n436\t- Purpose: horizon-based ambient occlusion computed from height data, for contact shading and depth (11 October 2026)\n437\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap, Channel Source, Use World Units, Height Depth, Radius, Intensity, Relief Balance (11 October 2026)\n438\t- Height role: reads height to produce occlusion (11 October 2026)\n439\t- COP, OFFICIAL-MAP: Ambient Occlusion (HBAO) = `heighttoambientocclusion` (Height Scale for Height Depth, View Radius for Radius, Remap Ramp for the intensity curve; correspondences UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)\n440\t\n441\t#### A4.29 MatFX Peeling Paint (11 October 2026)\n442\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/matfx-filters/matfx-peeling-paint (11 October 2026)\n443\t- Purpose: flaking and chipped paint; placed inside a group so the layers below show through where paint lifts (11 October 2026)\n444\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap, Peeling Level, Peeling Distance, Flake Level, Air Bubble Density, Flaking Density, Flaking X Amount, Flaking Y Amount; Curvature input Use Curvature, Curvature Distance, Curvature Contrast; Technical Luminosity, Contrast, Hue Shift, Saturation, Normal Intensity, Height Range, Height Position, Ambient Occlusion Intensity (11 October 2026)\n445\t- Height role: Height Range and Height Position set the thickness and level of the lifted paint skin (11 October 2026)\n446\t- COP, LOCAL recipe: Copernicus1.md lines 1357 to 1364 build the same effect with `fractalnoise` Worley cells stretched, a `remap` threshold near 0.70 to 0.74 for the plateau mask (about 65 percent paint, 35 percent bare wood), `edgedetect` on the mask contour, `blur` radius 2.5 and a `remap` for the raised curl of amplitude 0.06 (11 October 2026)\n447\t\n448\t#### A4.30 MatFX Rust Weathering (11 October 2026)\n449\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/matfx-filters/matfx-rust-weathering (11 October 2026)\n450\t- Purpose: rust buildup, corrosion, drips and aged wear (11 October 2026)\n451\t- Key parameters: Blur Intensity, Blur Wrap; Rust Spreading, Spreading Smoothness, Varnish Damage Scale; Drips Intensity, Drips Samples Amount, Drips Smoothness; blend intensities for Normal, Ambient Occlusion, Height, Base Color, Roughness, Metallic (11 October 2026)\n452\t- Height role: has an explicit Height Intensity blend, so it writes a rust relief into height (11 October 2026)\n453\t- COP, UNVERIFIED: `grunge_rust`, `grunge_rustysurface`, `grunge_drips`, `grunge_leakingstreaks` (all among the 14 Houdini 22 grunge nodes) masked and blended with `blend`; drips along gravity with `distort` Streak Max (11 October 2026)\n454\t\n455\t#### A4.31 MatFX Shut Line (11 October 2026)\n456\t- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/filters/matfx-filters/matfx-shut-line (11 October 2026)\n457\t- Purpose: panel lines and seams, recessed shut lines or raised seams with extra height and color detail (11 October 2026)"}]},"uuid":"0ba6e0f8-6451-4628-af83-1e13d409efc8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:11:00.198Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0c490dc4-297a-413a-9778-e91744d247f4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
