hapes, debris, strata and terraces (11 October 2026)\n749\t- Problem solved: rock faces and terrain-like materials need gullies, debris piles, banded layers and ledges that a plain noise cannot give (11 October 2026)\n750\t- Designer chain (SOURCE): Slope Blur Min and Max cascades (T03); an erosion-style pattern from a cloud map warped by Directional Warp and blended onto the rock (Furneri); Thiger tutorial sections Erosion and Layering and Dune and Pebbles; the Derozier cliff lessons Mid Shapes and Surfacing (stepping, chiseling) and the Gnomon description of erosion patterns as the second layer of detail (11 October 2026)\n751\t- Copernicus chain (node pages SOURCE, combination UNVERIFIED): `monotoheightfield` (Height Scale, Height Offset; changes type info to height and rescales to world positions) -> `heightfield_erode` -> `heightfieldtomono` (Compute Range, Input and Output Min and Max, Clamp to Output Range); recommended order on https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/heightfields_cop/workflows.html is noise, blend, erosion cascade from large features to small, slump, terraces then erosion to soften them, strata with Tilt (effective only with Space set to World) (11 October 2026)\n752\t- `heightfield_erode` (SOURCE https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_erode.html and https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/heightfields_cop/erosion.html): inputs height, debris, sediment, flow, erodability, rainfall; outputs height, debris, sediment, flow (a UV layer usable on `distort`.`dir`); Simulate off with Iterations; Feature Size (minimum 3 times the pixel size; large values give broad channels, stack passes starting around 20 or more), Spread Iterations, Random Seed, Erodability (1 soft, 0.1 granite-like), Hydro group Flow Force (0 disables), Bank Angle, Rainfall Coverage, Slope Influence, Erosion Rate, Deposition Rate, Removal Rate (higher gives a rocky look), Evaporation Rate (low gives long rocky channels, high gives small soil-like depressions), Thermal 