{"parentUuid":"f1168e0e-a785-4b5e-9ffa-aeeb957bb37e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"a30145bc0fb1a513e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCTravQ1cyB8aNWqjt8VTJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance Designer brushed metal tutorial anisotropic noise directional blur scratches height breakdown\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"anisotropic kuwahara grayscale\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/filters/effects/anisotropic-kuwahara-grayscale.html\"},{\"title\":\"Directional blur\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/directional-blur\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/filters/effects/anisotropic-kuwahara.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/substance-compositing-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-compositing-graphs/node-library/material-filters/pbr-utilities/pbr-render.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2068784\"},{\"title\":\"system requirements\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/cl/substance-3d-designer/getting-started/system-requirements.html\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2063195\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2063072\"},{\"title\":\"post effects\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-designer/interface/3d-view/camera/post-effects.html\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"learning substance professional tips and tricks\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/learning-substance-professional-tips-and-tricks\"},{\"title\":\"learning substance professional tips and tricks\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/learning-substance-professional-tips-and-tricks/?amp=1\"},{\"title\":\"www.texturecan.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.texturecan.com/tag/Brushed/\"},{\"title\":\"Website powered by\",\"url\":\"https://joshuapelican.artstation.com/projects/eaa5G3\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2702211\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2419150\"},{\"title\":\"polycount.com\",\"url\":\"https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2702081\"},{\"title\":\"texturecan.com\",\"url\":\"https://texturecan.com/tag/Scratched\"},{\"title\":\"COM REDSHIFT3D REDSHIFT4C4D NODES CORE SCRATCHES\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/en-us/Content/html/COM_REDSHIFT3D_REDSHIFT4C4D_NODES_CORE_SCRATCHES.html\"},{\"title\":\"COM REDSHIFT3D REDSHIFT4C4D NODES CORE SCRATCHES\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/2026/en-us/Content/html/COM_REDSHIFT3D_REDSHIFT4C4D_NODES_CORE_SCRATCHES.html\"}]\n\nI didn't find a step-by-step Substance Designer brushed metal tutorial in these results. I did find documentation and community discussion on the individual pieces you named.\n\n**Directional blur:** Adobe's docs describe this node as a motion-blur-like operation that blurs along a user-defined angle, unlike the regular Blur node, which spreads evenly in all directions. Unlike the regular 'Blur' node, which blurs equally in all directions, 'Directional blur' works along a user-defined angle. Its Intensity sets the blur radius in pixels, and its Angle sets the direction. The direction of the blur effect in number of turns clockwise, starting from horizontal. The docs also note that an extended, higher-quality alternative is provided in Anisotropic Blur, with a performance trade-off.\n\n**Directional scratches:** The Directional scratches filter appears in the 2D view's filter library, alongside directional noise presets. 25. Directional noise 2, 26. Directional noise 3, 27. Directional noise 4, 28. Directional scratches. The library listing doesn't describe its parameters, so check the node's properties after you drop it in.\n\n**Community guidance:** On Polycount, one artist working on brushed metal said the feathering on the surface could be a little tighter, for brushed metal its usually very densely covered. That points to tighter, denser directional streaks as the main fix for a too-sparse look. Another thread suggested cone shape, gradient map, use the gradient picker on the anisotropic noise for radial brushed patterns, though one replier said the lines moved outward from the center rather than parallel to the edge, so that approach is not a drop-in fix.\n\n**Related tool in another app:** Maxon's Redshift docs describe a Scratches shader that can bias scratches along a particular direction - making it great for brushed metals. Its guidance is that for brushed metal, increasing the Steps to 1 gives us just that. Its UV-space advice (the orientation of the UV islands has a direct impact on the orientation and size of the scratches) applies to Substance too, since UV orientation controls which way directional effects run on the model.\n\n**Suggested workflow (my own, not from these sources):**\n1. Start with a fine Anisotropic Noise or Directional Noise at high tiling for the brushed grain.\n2. Feed it into Directional Blur or Anisotropic Blur with the angle set to your brush direction.\n3. Layer Directional Scratches on top with a blend mode, and keep their intensity low.\n4. Blend the result into Height with a small amplitude so the grain reads without overwhelming the base surface.\n5. Use a Levels or Histogram Scan node to control how much roughness variation comes through.\n\nIf you want a specific tutorial, searching for a video or article title (e.g., \"Substance Designer brushed metal\" with a channel or year) will likely turn up more than this search did.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4697b003-9839-4825-a4ad-943f72fbbe89","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:16:32.860Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8a339f0b-5b14-4718-891d-45fef7da7ef4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":35,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":12},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1168e0e-a785-4b5e-9ffa-aeeb957bb37e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"deep-stirring-lark"}
